{"call_id":"call_I3kw8N0fT1570lX0LtMGqE2n","process_id":"95104","turn_id":"019ca6f9-32da-7241-b2a2-aa427f46c5c4","command":["/usr/bin/bash","-lc","kspec meta observations list --json"],"cwd":"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"kspec meta observations list --json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","stdout":"[\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF89NXNJVRJQ6RTHJ310SHXC\",\n    \"type\": \"idea\",\n    \"content\": \"Need better error messages\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": \"@session-start\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T10:16:15.283Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:06.781Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": \"@01KF89NY\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93NC0FXND1244CN31ZH22Z\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"ReferenceIndex Result<T> pattern gotcha: resolve() returns Result objects with .ok field, not items directly. Must check result.ok before accessing result.item - TypeScript doesn't enforce this at compile time. Pattern: if (result.ok) { use result.item } else { handle error }. Encountered multiple times across iterations.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:20.175Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:07.260Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93NCXZNXTPWAPCFPNH0STG\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Linter/tooling auto-revert blocker: During ralph loop iterations, file changes were repeatedly auto-reverted by linter/auto-save system. Code written and verified would disappear after edits. Affected shadow.ts, index.ts, test files. Possible causes: aggressive format-on-save, linter deleting code it doesn't understand, file watcher conflicts. Blocks implementation work when it occurs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:21.120Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:07.778Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93NDYAX7CWP4QP7072AHMH\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop session state freshness: Multiple issues with stale state in automation loops. (1) Iteration started on non-main branch from previous session. (2) Session context showed already-completed task as ready because context generated before commits reflected. (3) Picked completed work repeatedly. Solutions: generate context AFTER pulling latest, validate task is actually pending before starting, checkpoint script should update .kspec before next iteration.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:22.155Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:08.181Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93P6NTQJP3C2ZSND2J2MZT\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Subprocess spawning complexity: When promoting observations to tasks, initially tried spawning npm/tsx subprocess which caused temp directory path issues in tests. Switched to direct API calls (createTask/saveTask) which simplified implementation and avoided process overhead. Pattern: prefer direct API over subprocess when both run in same codebase.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:47.483Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:08.526Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93P7W2A063T315RXPC6ZF7\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Commander --json flag conflict: Command-specific --json flags conflict with global --json flag in Commander. Solution: use global flag only, check isJsonMode() instead of options.json. This pattern should be documented or enforced via convention.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:48.706Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:08.975Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93P8XZK7K9V8ERYYH6FE0Z\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Bash tool cd persistence: Commands run in same directory as previous command unless explicit cd. Running 'cd .kspec && git status' left session in .kspec worktree. Need explicit 'cd /path/to/main' to return. Can be confusing when working with shadow branch.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:49.792Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:09.402Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93PA837GGVE8DH3PVZE8WC\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"CLI output pattern: When implementing CLI commands with both human-readable and JSON formats, use success(message, data) instead of calling both success() and output() separately. The success() function already handles JSON mode internally, avoiding duplicate/mixed output.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:51.140Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:09.731Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93PBBYDPRH0WQSKN4Y18SV\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task status accuracy gap: Found task marked as priority 3 ready but implementation was already complete. All code, tests, and functionality existed. System correctly updated spec alignment when task completed, but task remained in ready list longer than it should have. Need earlier alignment checks or better detection of 'code exists but task not marked done' scenarios.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:52.286Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:10.062Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93PCN5NVFEHR801G77EK3X\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Shadow branch auto-commit PR challenges: PR included WIP commits from shadow that were auto-committed. Consider: (1) squash strategy for shadow commits when creating PR, (2) explicit checkpoint command before PR creation, or (3) shadow commit message convention (wip: prefix) to make cleanup easier.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:53.606Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:10.411Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93PDXFBPM2B1WYE6HFYJCX\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review automation friction: Had to manually launch review subagent, wait for output, interpret results, then fix issues. Could streamline with dedicated /review skill that: (1) checks for open PRs, (2) launches review subagent automatically, (3) interprets results + decision tree, (4) applies fixes if trivial, (5) merges if appropriate.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:54.895Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:10.930Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93Q1Y31HP8245N4DF67MCA\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Auto-sync vs interactive prompts anti-pattern: When adding interactive prompts to modify state, always check if automatic sync/calculation logic already exists. AlignmentIndex calculates spec status from all linked tasks - interactive prompt would allow single-task override, creating drift. Pattern: if system has 'calculated truth', don't add manual override without considering multi-entity consistency.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:51:15.396Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:11.342Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93Q2W8DC2RNGG1NA4ABQE0\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Test fixtures spec_ref conflicts: Test fixtures should avoid spec_ref assignments that conflict with derive tests. When adding spec_ref to test tasks, check if they're used in derive --dry-run tests which expect tasks not to exist yet.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:51:16.360Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:11.921Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93Q4JZ571ZGRTHZ3QXCYJQ\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Parser vs CLI layer disconnect: Meta includes were fully implemented in parser but CLI used wrong accessor (metaCtx.manifest.* vs metaCtx.*). This kind of bug suggests value in integration tests that exercise full stack, not just parser logic. Consider smoke tests for all CLI commands with complex scenarios.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:51:18.112Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:12.429Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93Q6BCQXGTJ7X4FAK13KVT\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Spec gap discovery during implementation: AC mentioned 'origin: observation_promotion' but origin field didn't exist in schema. Good example of spec-code drift. Consider: pre-implementation spec validation against schema, or schema-first approach where AC references must match existing schema fields.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:51:19.917Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:13.031Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93Q83M6RJ0YXH1H2H4F3TK\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"kspec-meta shadow branch divergence: Shadow branch has diverged significantly from remote (99 local vs 2 remote commits). Merge conflicts in sessions/ and modules/. May need manual reconciliation or a fresh sync strategy. Task changes are committed locally and functional.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:51:21.717Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:13.557Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93Q9S85XSBT1JVV1S1F9F3\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Type guards for union types: When narrowing AnyLoadedItem | LoadedMetaItem to LoadedTask, check for required properties that exist on Task but not on meta items. Use 'status' in item && 'depends_on' in item - NOT optional properties like closed_reason which won't exist on incomplete tasks.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:51:23.432Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:14.020Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94EZQT8WP107P6QV9ZC4JD\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review workflow pattern: Review subagents proved critical for catching issues before merge. Established pattern: (1) check for open PRs, (2) launch review subagent, (3) fix trivial issues directly, (4) re-review confirms fixes, (5) merge when checks pass. Works smoothly when changes are minor - automated review + fix + merge flow is efficient. Multi-step workflow (review→fix→merge→continue) provides good session continuity. Review caught real issues: reference matching bugs, TypeScript errors, duplicate PRs, missing tests. Self-review via subagent is valid for automation loops despite GitHub not allowing self-approval.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:04:19.579Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:14.432Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94F0W0BPTB5RP6FDWH63SM\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Incremental refactoring pattern: Large multi-iteration refactors work well when pattern is established early. Key lessons: (1) Create module first with comprehensive coverage, (2) Start with smallest files to establish pattern, (3) Commit incremental progress with clear 'what done/remains' tracking, (4) Use TodoWrite for sub-phases. String/error centralization phases showed this: early PRs for small wins, direct commits for established patterns. Tests catch issues early, smaller files build confidence. Having checkpoints and running totals (e.g., '179 of 201 = 89%') made continuation easy. This phased approach balances review overhead with execution speed.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:04:20.737Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:14.851Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94F20W3MKFPBA1XN0ABQ7P\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Implementation pattern (schema→parser→CLI→tests): New features follow clean path. Reuse agent command structure (formatTable, formatVerbose, JSON output via output()). Reference validation integration is clean - add to REF_FIELDS. Meta reference implementation was straightforward thanks to existing ReferenceIndex infrastructure. Pattern of implementing formatters first, then command registration works well. Testing is fast and reliable. Module add followed same pattern: validate inputs, create data, write file, update manifest, shadow commit. Could extract into reusable helper.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:04:21.916Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:15.326Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94FHX7C98EFRCSGAXAKBBR\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Reference implementation value: Checking prior work (../kspec-acp-test, ../kspec-ralph-test) before implementing saves significant design time. Found identical spec and working implementation providing clear blueprint. Prior work avoids edge cases and provides consistency. Explore subagents are valuable for understanding prior implementations - provided comprehensive details: file paths, schema patterns, CLI structure, test isolation challenges. Having parallel agent repos with prior work is highly valuable. Pattern: exploration as standard first step for implementation tasks.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:04:38.184Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:15.816Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94FK4G7W86NXDVTAZ77SK8\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task verification workflow: Some ready tasks are already implemented from prior sessions. Pattern: when starting task, verify current state by reading code, running tests, checking existing functionality before implementing. Saves time and avoids duplicate work. Meta commands (resolve, observe, promote, conventions) were already implemented but tasks remained pending. Need better sync between implementation status and task status - perhaps command to scan for already-implemented specs and auto-complete tasks. Consider 'verify implementation status' step especially for CLI commands.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:04:39.441Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:16.168Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94FMF9Y5VCS7EQXP4G2FRJ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Session/workflow patterns: Spike tasks with no code output don't need commits - value is in task notes documenting research. Shadow-only changes (task state updates) don't need main-branch PRs since shadow branch is source of truth. PR skill correctly detects no changes and exits cleanly for metadata-only tasks. PR workflow smooth with auto-generated branch names and /pr skill. Shadow CLI verification iteration showed pattern: pick task, verify implementation exists, complete task, no code changes needed.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:04:40.810Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:16.582Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94G1HYX2DCY796SKB9XB7P\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task guardrails and completion checks: Feature dogfooded successfully - tested on itself during completion. Interactive prompt provides immediate feedback about AC coverage ensuring implementations match specs. Implementation preserves spec status.maturity when updating implementation status (important pattern to avoid losing maturity context). Default to 'draft' if status doesn't exist yet.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:04:54.208Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:17.054Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94G2RY8JAX71K9BC8HJSF7\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Context and session integration: Meta focus command implementation straightforward thanks to well-structured SessionContext schema and existing loadSessionContext/saveSessionContext functions. Pattern of supporting show/set/clear modes in single command is clean and user-friendly. Auto-prepending @ to references maintains UX consistency. Context integration showed context BEFORE active work for immediate agent orientation - context is 'what thinking about' while active tasks are 'what doing'.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:04:55.454Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:17.500Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94G3YV75DYWZENYG19N9NX\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Review subagent catches real issues: Found validation strictness issue with RefSchema (too strict for manual files), TypeScript compilation errors, import path issues. Demonstrates value of code review even for simple changes. Pattern: when review finds flag conflicts or behavioral issues, fix includes both code AND spec updates. Renamed --verbose to --debug-shadow based on review finding conflict.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:04:56.668Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:17.832Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94GR1RQ0JXWNHD6RQGZ4SE\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Schema strictness value: ULID validation strictness caught real bugs - test fixtures had 24-char ULIDs passing because MetaUlidSchema was too lenient. Fixing schema to use UlidSchema forced proper fixture ULIDs. Important pattern: schema strictness prevents silent data corruption.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:05:17.241Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:18.266Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94GSM8KQP9QSQK47KT3J7X\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"JSON output helper pattern: output() provides clean separation between JSON and human-readable modes. Used successfully: return observation object in JSON mode, success message for human mode. Pattern: output(dataObject, () => humanFormatter()). Avoids duplicate/mixed output that happens with separate success() + output() calls.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:05:18.857Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:18.669Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94GV0DY58HXPVZJRQWBBAP\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"findChildItems path-based hierarchy: Implementation based on _path nesting worked well - path structure makes parent-child relationships explicit and easy to query. Similar pattern could be useful for other hierarchical queries: siblings, ancestors, tree depth.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:05:20.270Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:19.089Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94GWFGAHGPNM9HNCCESTSC\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Commander introspection for help: Commander's structure is stable and well-defined, making it reliable source of truth for help output. Consider applying to other CLI frameworks (Oclif, yargs). Separation of auto-generated syntax vs curated concepts is clean and maintainable.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:05:21.777Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:19.568Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94GXWR0CDRDG5GJ898XR24\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Command suggestion with Levenshtein: Feature implemented cleanly using Levenshtein distance. Threshold of 3 works well for catching typos without false positives. Commander.js already handles subcommand suggestions, so only needed top-level command handling.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:05:23.225Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:19.960Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94HCFSAD6WJ4PJG1T0SSY1\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Validation architecture scales: Adding warnings alongside errors required minimal changes - new type, updated return structure, simple CLI formatting. Separation of concerns (refs.ts for logic, validate.ts for orchestration, validate CLI for display) made enhancement straightforward. Pattern worth replicating: warnings as first-class citizens alongside errors.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:05:38.169Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:20.309Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94HDYHTGCMZCC6MMFYJGNJ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Spike workflow refinement: When completing spike, capture recommendation in closed_reason (brief) + final note (detailed). Spike task notes form mini research doc. Pattern: findings → analysis → recommendation. Example: task-archive spike documented current system, reviewed references, recommended MVP approach all in notes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:05:39.666Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:20.795Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94HFCXHSBAYMYXVTKRV3T8\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Convention validation foundation: Implementation validates convention schema. To be fully functional needs integration with actual content sources (git log for commits, task notes for note validation, etc.). Foundation is complete, content gathering is future enhancement.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:05:41.150Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:21.247Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94HGRMD0BF4524V3KQ8V2Q\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task origin field tracking: Added origin enum to track task creation source (manual, derived, observation_promotion). Could be extended for other sources like 'agent_suggestion', 'test_failure', 'lint_error'. Useful for metrics and understanding task flow.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:05:42.548Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:21.698Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF96T3VVQ8CTXQYQ4XNMTQ1W\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"Shadow branch PR workflow clarification: When work only updates shadow branch (.kspec/) metadata - task state, inbox items, notes - should PRs still be created? Ralph instructions say 'create PR after commit' but this seems intended for code changes on feature branches. Shadow changes track the work; code changes are the work output. Current behavior: skip PR when working tree is clean. Need clarification on whether meta manifest changes should follow different review process than code changes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:45:21.404Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:22.131Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF96T6E67ZB7FVJ8JEDBKTYS\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Iteration workflow patterns: (1) Verification-only iterations produce no commits - efficient, avoids code churn, skipping PR is correct when working tree clean. (2) Implementation vs verification task distinction - verification tasks are quick wins for automation loops, implementation tasks need focused sessions. (3) Iteration findings show shadow branch is source of truth for task state (git status on main shows clean after adding inbox items), session context can be stale. Pattern: prioritize verification in loops, save implementation for context-rich sessions.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:45:24.039Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:22.610Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF96TKTHJ8DNBGCTR8ACQ7DN\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review momentum: When reviewing own PRs from previous iterations, fix trivial issues directly (like invalid ULIDs) rather than leaving comments. Merge when checks pass unless changes are substantial. This keeps momentum going in automation loops.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:45:37.746Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:23.094Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF96TN2JQ4PPH7MW0G42MXBT\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"CLI label centralization: item.ts and inbox.ts had drifted from established src/strings/labels.ts pattern. Quick grep audit found inconsistencies. Fix was straightforward: import centralized labels and replace hardcoded strings. Pattern prevents drift: new commands should import from strings/ from the start.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:45:39.027Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:23.455Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF96TPK7BTRZ1XZ9BK5YD6G8\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Reference directory exploration: For spikes, launching dedicated Explore subagent for reference dirs (kspec-acp-test, kspec-ralph-test) prevents context bloat while getting comprehensive findings. Subagent found identical spec content across both test dirs. Pattern worked well - consider for other research tasks.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:45:40.584Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:23.878Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF96TQV69YX5RQKAJQDQ1S25\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Shadow CLI verification: Picked task from ready list, found all three commands (status, log, repair) already implemented with 43 passing tests. Verified functionality, completed task, updated spec alignment. No code changes needed. Key learning: spec items marked 'implemented' were accurate.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:45:41.863Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:24.454Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF96V5J1QJR44K8M7MMGFS0M\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Meta schema verification batch: Completed 8 meta-related tasks in single iteration by verifying existing schema implementations in src/schema/meta.ts. Pattern: start task, read schema file, verify fields match spec, document in notes, complete. Efficient for verification tasks when implementation already exists.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:45:55.906Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:24.860Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF96V6MZKAJC86KJD949CW8P\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Display-first implementation strategy: Many derived tasks for meta-spec features were already implemented. Schema layer and CLI display commands (meta show, meta agents, etc.) are complete. Gap is in interactive/mutation commands and validation integration. Pattern: display-first is pragmatic - read operations complete, write operations deferred. Allows early testing of schema design.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:45:57.023Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:25.443Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF96V82FAJANHX3P5GWEH8HQ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Convention schema test gap: Schema was already implemented but lacked test coverage. When picking up implementation tasks, check if code exists first - may just need tests or documentation rather than new code. Tests added brought coverage up to spec.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:45:58.480Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:25.758Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF96V9DF3FX5XH224TM996TE\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Session checkpoint hook value: Hook caught uncommitted .gitignore change. Important to follow never-commit-to-main rule - all changes should go through PRs. Hook successfully prevented incomplete session state.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:45:59.857Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:26.087Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF9WR7HTSHYCHSFKYFG31JSJ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel exploration agents gave comprehensive context quickly for documentation audit\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T01:08:48.314Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:26.540Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF9ZFAGH35RQG6J9BA20TM6E\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop iteration 1 completed successfully: merged PR #58 (meta thread), implemented and shipped meta question command as PR #63. Pattern replication from existing code (meta thread) worked perfectly - implementation and tests completed in single iteration with all tests passing.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T01:56:22.161Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:27.048Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA0DVCMDFM7QFDJQ2ZCY21G\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task descriptions with clear problem statements enable fast resolution - the ralph newline issue had a detailed description that made the fix obvious: just move console.log() before success() call. Spent <5 min from task start to fix complete.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T02:13:02.485Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:27.570Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA0S3X005NWJY3D8931BGP5\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Hook debugging methodology: For hook errors, test with synthetic inputs (valid JSON, invalid JSON, edge cases) to isolate root cause before fixing. The '2>&1' pattern in test commands reveals stderr leakage that wouldn't be visible in normal hook execution.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T02:19:11.648Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:28.048Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA0WGSE81VFMN080ARJEQHG\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task verification pattern successful: Check git history for related commits before implementing. Task @01KF9B4W was already completed in ff935fd - verification took <2 minutes, saved duplicate work.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T02:21:03.150Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:28.565Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA17QWT1KQJGG4J8E6ZT6AZ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Clear task scope led to clean implementation - 'ralph loop session save' was well-defined with obvious file naming (context-iter-N.json) and storage location (.kspec/sessions/{id}/). No ambiguity about what to build or where to put it. Good example of actionable task with minimal design decisions needed.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T02:27:10.874Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:28.966Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA1T2TD09TXAD8KHNAB0JFJ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Comprehensive design work captured entirely in task notes - created detailed analysis of agent-first CLI improvements with 5 key areas, phased implementation plan, and 5 follow-up inbox items. This design-in-notes pattern works well for planning tasks that inform future spec creation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T02:37:11.885Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:29.515Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA1T7F256DV5H7W73GG1V3C\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Shadow branch worktree was missing at iteration start - required manual 'git worktree add .kspec kspec-meta' then 'kspec shadow repair' to restore. This may be an environment issue (worktree cleanup?) or session isolation problem. Worth investigating why .kspec worktree disappeared between iterations.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T02:37:16.642Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:30.005Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA2BWD2KC305W3SBDYQR2DH\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Minimal viable implementation pattern works well: Started with complex task (subagent review workflow), scoped down to core value (review context command), shipped working feature in single iteration. Command provides immediate value for manual use while leaving door open for automation later. Design-first approach (notes documenting decisions) helped keep scope manageable.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T02:46:55.139Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:30.439Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA32BJBH3D2HY6ACYNJBNWA\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review subagent workflow worked effectively - launched dedicated review agent, identified missing test coverage and type safety issues, implemented fixes, verified all tests pass (555/556), merged with proper trailers. Review-fix-merge cycle completed in single iteration.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T02:59:11.564Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:30.782Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA380DVCVJT84GA2XNBRWY0\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Documentation-focused task worked well with todo tracking - broke down 5 documentation updates into clear steps, executed systematically, verified commands against CLI, completed all updates in single iteration with comprehensive commit message\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T03:02:16.764Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:31.185Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA3SBMD2507GB1TYZTN8G8R\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Smooth workflow on implementing kspec meta context - spec was clear, implementation straightforward, comprehensive test coverage added, all tests pass. The meta command family now has a unified context view that complements the individual management commands (focus, thread, question).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T03:11:45.294Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:31.619Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA4RFT8D2T2SW95A8ZK1JZE\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Shadow branch auto-commit workflow is seamless - created 5 spec items with ACs, all automatically committed without manual intervention. Task completion tracked properly across worktrees.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T03:28:45.385Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:32.212Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA4Y20RN7W6ZMG7ZNE1VE3E\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"ACs discovery pattern: Reading implementation code + corresponding tests provides complete picture of behaviors that need acceptance criteria. For @status-cascade, found 5 distinct behaviors (prompt shown, cascade accepted, cascade rejected, JSON mode, no children) by examining handleStatusCascade function and integration tests.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T03:31:47.864Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:32.655Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA599DH7QAR73HRWZMMWR5Z\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Efficient workflow iteration: picked task, analyzed code (Read tool), identified root cause (syncSpecImplementationStatus saves but doesn't commit), implemented minimal fix (2 identical changes in start/complete), verified with tests (561/561 pass), committed and created PR. Single-focus iteration completed in ~10 minutes of work.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T03:37:55.889Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:33.151Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA63VXRCMDNFNEVSNNHQ71M\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Tree view implementation was straightforward - used existing findChildItems pattern and _path property to build hierarchy. The box-drawing character approach (├──, └──, │) provides clear visual structure without complex dependencies. Integration with existing filters worked seamlessly because tree formatting happens at display layer, not query layer.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T03:52:26.808Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:33.546Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA6WBT1A8WRNQ4F7NM2KAFX\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR workflow smooth - auto-generated branch name from task slug (feat/add-priority-flag-to-derive), created branch from main with unpushed commit, reset main, pushed branch, created PR. The pattern of: checkout -b new-branch && git checkout main && git reset --hard origin/main && git checkout new-branch works cleanly for moving commits from main to a new branch.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T04:05:49.505Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:34.020Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA8C874AX1X3SDB2BZWC6AE\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task start spec context feature - clean DX improvement that follows existing patterns. Pattern: show context at point of action (when starting work), suppress in JSON mode, add test coverage with real fixtures. The alignment guidance string pattern in src/strings/guidance.ts is effective for maintaining consistent agent messaging.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T04:31:58.693Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:34.442Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA9KJ13NES8R3R26QESDS02\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test coverage tracking implementation demonstrates good separation of concerns - validation logic in parser/validate.ts, display logic in CLI commands. The AC annotation pattern (// AC: @spec-ref ac-N) provides simple traceability without complex tooling. Duplicating scanTestCoverage in task.ts is acceptable given the focused use case, though could be extracted to utils if pattern grows.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T04:53:26.691Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:34.910Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA9N9FMZCAJAQNE97K479RF\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task state management across sessions: found task @01KF9G2X left in_progress from previous iteration. No built-in command to reset task to pending - only cancel (which marks it cancelled) or complete. Added note documenting state, but task remains in_progress. Consider adding 'kspec task reset' or 'kspec task stop' command to move tasks back to pending when abandoned mid-work.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T04:54:23.476Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:35.387Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAA0XW7PHR9EWXEP3HR1HR7\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Iteration 16 handled two tasks effectively: completed test coverage tracking (my primary work) and discovered/completed abandoned WIP for spec item notes (3 WIP commits from previous session). The spec item notes feature was nearly complete - just needed commits. This demonstrates good cross-session continuity when WIP is properly committed with clear messages.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T05:00:44.808Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:35.760Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAAC1AYM45CE8B8MDWGJ4GW\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Reusing NoteSchema across both tasks and spec items worked perfectly - no code duplication, consistent behavior, and symmetric CLI commands. The pattern of import { NoteSchema } from './task.js' into spec.ts demonstrates good schema reuse.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T05:06:48.798Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:36.184Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFABRSMHWD0Q33800AX7TYSS\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review workflow worked well: subagent found TypeScript compilation errors (missing imports), implemented fix directly on feature branch, verified with tests, then merged. Clean separation between review agent and implementation agent.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T05:31:15.473Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:36.709Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFABRY971XP4KD8D3198R2KT\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Spec-first workflow for schema changes: Updated @maturity-states spec with new 'deferred' status and added ACs before implementing in schema. This ensures spec remains source of truth and provides clear acceptance criteria for implementation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T05:31:20.231Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:37.258Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFADNW4SYG78Y13M8KHXAR92\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Auto-generating implementation notes from specs during derive significantly streamlines the spec-first workflow. Rather than requiring manual 'kspec task note' after derive, the context is automatically captured. This reduces cognitive load and ensures implementation context isn't lost. The pattern of using spec description + AC summary provides exactly the right level of detail for implementation reference.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T06:04:36.889Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:37.742Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFADRNQN3SG8FMZF3EMWHF6N\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"INSTALL.md creation went smoothly - clear task description made it easy to know what to write. Agent-focused documentation should always have: concise commands, copy-pasteable snippets, clear success criteria after each section, troubleshooting for common gotchas.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T06:06:08.629Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:38.272Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAEFD4XYVVXH61FNA9HWHGT\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review workflow with subagent worked smoothly. The review subagent provided detailed analysis covering code quality, test coverage, task/spec alignment, and commit conventions. Decision tree in RALPH_LOOP_INSTRUCTIONS.md made merge decision clear. Merged PR #75, then picked next task and completed docs work. Clean iteration from review → merge → new work → PR.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T06:18:33.501Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:38.692Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAF48W58CCFZBC0DBGCCK21\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Git worktrees use hooks from main .git/hooks (via commondir), not from .git/worktrees/-kspec/hooks. This is a key architectural detail that wasn't obvious from git documentation. Testing revealed the issue when hooks weren't being called. The commondir file points to '../..' which makes git look for hooks in the main repo.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T06:29:57.253Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:39.120Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAFEAADJPTN5ZRHK0PDYGJY\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Small DX improvements (like setup:dev script) have high impact for low effort. Pattern: when you find yourself documenting a multi-step setup process, consider if it can be a single script instead.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T06:35:26.413Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:39.559Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAGYE5VYH1YSNS7ZD4R20BX\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Shadow branch worktree repair workflow issues: (1) Nested .kspec/.kspec directories created by repeated git worktree add commands, (2) Commands that navigate into .kspec (cd .kspec && ...) fail when already in subdirectory, causing directory confusion, (3) Git worktree metadata (/.git/worktrees) can become desynchronized from actual directory state, (4) kspec shadow repair command failed with 'spawn /bin/sh ENOENT' error. Resolution required: manual git worktree prune, removal of nested directories, and manual git operations in worktree with KSPEC_SHADOW_COMMIT=1 to bypass hook. Consider: (a) More robust worktree repair that handles nested directories, (b) Better error messages showing current directory context, (c) Idempotent repair commands that check current state before operations.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T07:01:43.227Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:40.049Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAH2B2H0P3ZZRXMKY7F35BV\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Completed full task cycle in iteration 25: merged open PR, resolved shadow branch sync issues, picked and completed task @01KFAB9B, committed work, created PR #80. The worktree friction observation captured detailed troubleshooting context for future improvements. Task completion workflow worked smoothly once shadow branch was synchronized.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T07:03:51.122Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:40.632Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAHKB1REKZMA6EP9HM7J1FZ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Integration test strategy: Using command JSON output directly from promote command instead of querying tasks list afterward provides more accurate, focused tests and avoids format parsing issues. The promote command returns the created task in its JSON output, which is exactly what we need to verify.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T07:13:08.152Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:41.043Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAJSS392ZV47Z373HK29HAM\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Batch operation pattern scales well - created reusable executeBatchOperation() utility that handles all common concerns (mutual exclusion, partial failures, output formatting). Applied to 3 commands (complete, cancel, delete) with minimal duplication. Pattern: extract single-item logic into executeOperation callback, utility handles iteration/error collection. Makes adding batch support to new commands straightforward.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T07:34:07.722Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:41.409Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAM6VF2MY7QKC526SZX8PY8\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test-first debugging pattern worked excellently for batch operations\\n\\nThe PR review subagent identified a critical bug: resolveTaskRef() called process.exit() \\ninstead of returning errors, breaking partial failure handling.\\n\\nThe fix process was clean:\\n1. Review identified the bug with clear evidence\\n2. Created batch-compatible resolver that returns {task, error}\\n3. Updated batch.ts to expect new format\\n4. All existing tests passed (no regression)\\n5. Added 9 new tests covering all 8 ACs\\n6. Tests caught edge cases (ambiguous ULID prefixes)\\n\\nKey insight: When refactoring error handling, create new functions instead of modifying\\nexisting ones. The original resolveTaskRef() serves single-ref commands that should exit\\non error. The new resolveTaskRefForBatch() serves batch commands that should continue.\\n\\nThis separation of concerns made the fix safe and testable.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T07:58:44.706Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:41.783Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFANADZJA4VAFBSH0F8FAWXP\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Test observation from Ralph Loop\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T08:18:10.546Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:42.284Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAND9RY95MCTPE02QB9103E\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Iteration 29 workflow was efficient and clean: picked highest priority task, implemented feature with comprehensive tests (5 tests covering all AC), manual testing verified functionality, PR created. The --from-inbox flag for meta observe enables bucket correction during triage - items captured in wrong bucket can be easily converted.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T08:19:44.542Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:42.833Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAPKVHCJGKTVM1690P8P8CF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Passthrough args implementation pattern - When adding passthrough args to CLI commands that normally parse output, create separate raw output path. Trying to parse structured output with custom format flags breaks. Used searchCommitsRaw() for raw git output when passthroughArgs.length > 0, avoiding format conflicts.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T08:40:47.917Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:43.177Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAPWQVB7K0DV4ZK6TDRJMM2\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review and merge workflow worked smoothly. Dedicated review subagent provided comprehensive analysis covering code quality, test coverage, and spec alignment. Clear APPROVE recommendation made merge decision straightforward. This validates the review-before-merge pattern in RALPH_LOOP_INSTRUCTIONS.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T08:45:39.051Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:43.493Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAQN66S95434T70FPXES77X\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Implemented kspec setup worktree detection cleanly by leveraging existing shadow module utilities. The repairShadow() function already handled the complex worktree creation logic, so implementation was primarily about adding the detection and prompting layer. This demonstrates the value of the shadow module's well-factored utilities for worktree management.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T08:59:00.185Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:43.850Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFARJ6TDYJFKS5EP5XAJB89W\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Bulk refactoring pattern: Created automated script to replace magic numbers with constants across 18+ files. This approach was much faster than manual edits and ensured consistency. The script handled the mechanical replacements, then manual fixes addressed edge cases (import paths). This pattern is reusable for similar bulk refactoring tasks (e.g., error message standardization, import path updates).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T09:14:51.085Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:44.386Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFATCXG9439H99JN0KK8SV71\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Multi-round PR review with dedicated subagents worked extremely well. Pattern: (1) Launch review subagent after PR created (2) Review finds issues (3) Fix issues (4) Launch new review subagent (5) Repeat until clean (6) Merge. This approach caught all CONFLICT exit code inconsistencies through 3 fix iterations before merge. The independent review prevented merging incomplete work. Key: each review cycle provides fresh perspective and catches missed cases.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T09:46:54.857Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:44.886Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFATQ46A835BQ657YX7AC853\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Implementing features with clear acceptance criteria is much faster than without. The @stale-status-detection spec had 5 well-defined ACs that mapped directly to implementation steps. AC format (Given/When/Then) made it easy to verify each scenario. Spent more time fixing type issues than implementing logic. Key learning: read schema thoroughly first to understand data structures before writing validation logic.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T09:52:29.386Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:45.251Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFATS86AMESWQJA9E1T2JCVM\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Staleness detection implementation completed successfully. The feature detects status inconsistencies between specs and tasks, with 3 key checks: task dependencies completed but task pending, spec implemented without tasks, and task completed but spec not started. All tests pass.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T09:53:39.018Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:45.817Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFATSF5A7KEEY4CHSKTCFG4G\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Found task in progress but work already committed. This may happen when: (1) previous iteration completed but didn't mark task complete, (2) concurrent work from another process, or (3) git operations completed before kspec state sync. Consider adding 'kspec shadow sync' at session start to ensure state is current.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T09:53:46.155Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:46.180Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFATSKF22KHRZYCQ0TJP1P1E\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Complete iteration workflow: (1) Check open PRs and review/merge, (2) Pick highest priority ready task, (3) Implement with clear ACs, (4) Manual test verification, (5) Commit with task/spec trailers, (6) Create PR. This pattern ensures no work is left in limbo - PRs are either merged or created by end of iteration. The /pr skill makes PR creation seamless.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T09:53:50.562Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:46.720Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFATTDS4G9VHDXXF4DDHS1C2\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Iteration 34 outcome: Merged 1 PR (semantic exit codes with 4 commits), implemented and shipped stale status detection (3 commits, PR #88 created). Multi-round review pattern prevented incomplete merges. Every iteration should end with either merged PRs or new PRs created - no work left uncommitted or unpushed. This keeps the project moving forward consistently.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T09:54:17.508Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:47.283Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAVMTHF0KRC1YKH8QMF1W9W\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Global --json mode interactions complicate command-specific JSON output. Commands that want to output simple JSON (like {path, branch}) end up wrapped in {success, ...} objects or interfere with git stderr. Consider: (1) per-command JSON output control, (2) dedicated JSON output stream, or (3) convention that commands bypass global mode for simple output.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T10:08:42.543Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:47.870Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAVYRDBQYJEAK4Z8E5QMQXA\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task was cancelled prematurely by automation (01KEZ9DSD3). The automation cancelled the task after initial investigation notes, but actual implementation work was completed successfully. The code changes were made and tested, but the task was marked as cancelled before completion could be recorded. This suggests the automation may be too aggressive in cancelling tasks that appear to be in research/investigation phase.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T10:14:08.043Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:48.302Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAVYYD7GKN0VXBP67B4CR8G\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Successfully improved YAML formatting consistency by switching from js-yaml to modern 'yaml' library. The new implementation provides deterministic formatting that won't randomly change between saves, addressing the core DX issue. While not preserving exact original formatting/comments, this is a pragmatic solution that significantly improves the developer experience without requiring complex CST manipulation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T10:14:14.183Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:48.734Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAY1AB5CT6KEJ2J9NY37WQX\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Complete YAML library migration completed successfully. Initial implementation had critical bug (timestamps round-tripping as Date objects), but review subagent caught it before merge. Fixed by migrating both read and write operations to yaml library. PR reviewed, fixed, and merged in same iteration. This demonstrates the value of: (1) Launching review subagents for own PRs, (2) Acting on review feedback immediately, (3) Complete testing before declaring done.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T10:50:29.093Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:49.163Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAY1FS7QHBMV350A899878F\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task automation cancelled 01KEZ9DSD3 prematurely during investigation phase, but work was actually completed. The automation should be more lenient with tasks in early research/investigation phases, or have a way to detect when implementation is actually progressing even if lots of notes are being added.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T10:50:34.663Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:49.658Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAY281BQT8BGFP3YRF6SYXF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Full iteration workflow executed successfully: Task pickup → Implementation → PR creation → Review subagent finds bug → Fix implementation → Re-review → Merge. The review-before-merge workflow prevented a production bug. Total time: ~40 minutes for complete feature delivery including bug fix.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T10:50:59.500Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:50.042Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAY7NM46JVAJ0JAKEDHAH0C\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Research spikes captured in task notes provide durable artifacts. Task 01KF9G22 demonstrates pattern: comprehensive research findings documented directly in notes, preserving context even when temporary files (scratchpad) don't persist. Notes become the source of truth for future spec/task creation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T10:53:57.252Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:50.446Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAY7ZXQ0P119X3S9N42KZVW\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task 01KF9G22 was cancelled in previous iteration but appeared in ready_tasks list. When attempted to complete after adding research notes, got error 'Cannot complete task with status: cancelled'. The ready_tasks filter should exclude cancelled tasks, or there should be a way to reopen/uncancell tasks that get picked up again.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T10:54:07.799Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:50.887Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFC3BCB8B8F2GXW0GGNCNRT4\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"Bulk import design question: What makes it 'work well'? The cancelled @task-bulk-import had a design for simplified YAML input. Challenges identified: format flexibility vs strictness, error handling mid-import, preview accuracy, integration with existing workflows. What's the core use case - rapid spec capture during design? Plan-to-spec translation? Importing from external sources?\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T21:42:36.136Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Resolved via batch JSON approach: Generic kspec batch command accepts JSON array of CLI args. Skills handle translation from flexible input to batch JSON. See inbox 01KFC3SV.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T21:50:38.514Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFC3BM2YJSZ56MFSS8MA8WM6\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Plan mode required multiple back-and-forth cycles. Missing upfront: output type (spec vs code), standalone requirements check, display/UX needs. Review subagent ran AFTER trying to exit plan mode instead of as a step before finalizing. Suggests plan mode needs structured phases or checklist.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T21:42:44.062Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFC3BVA0WNT6FV2B74DY270A\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Subagent review of spec caught 3 blocking issues (AC collision, undefined JSON structure, display contradiction) that would have caused implementation problems. Pattern: review specs with critical eye before finalizing, not just for completeness but for internal consistency and edge cases.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T21:42:51.457Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFC3C23Q4DX7APJEXFEKY1FN\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task notes template for standalone implementation context worked well: Scope (what this task covers), Prerequisites (dependencies), Files (to modify/create), Patterns (code examples), Tests (where to add). Prevents 'see parent for context' band-aids.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T21:42:58.423Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCPF1T45VEVDP6PHNY9D6SC\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Exit code fixes completed efficiently using TodoWrite to track all 6 individual changes. The todo list helped ensure no fixes were missed and provided clear progress visibility through the task.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T03:16:39.364Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCQ0SQ1RJ3HTD5FBE2N90RA\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR workflow (#96 → #97) demonstrates smooth iteration loop: review existing PR → merge → pick next task → implement → submit → create PR. The pending_review state effectively gates work and ensures each PR gets proper review before merge. Task @01KFC1GKG scope was well-defined (foundation only) which made it easy to complete in one iteration.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T03:26:20.898Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCQZKW4NF7Z3BA49P9NGQHF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review workflow with dedicated subagent worked well - caught missing test coverage before merge. Strict review guidelines (AC coverage required, no fluff tests, E2E preferred) ensure quality standards are maintained across iterations.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T03:43:10.724Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCR87QM94J4S6CKYCV9Z1B3\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"YAML migration task was straightforward - clear scope, no dependencies, simple find-replace pattern. This type of refactoring task is ideal for automation: well-defined changes, easy to verify with tests, low risk.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T03:47:53.205Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCS35ZYSCC5209668HWBZDA\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test-first debugging workflow effective: Added debug output to failing tests to identify root cause (invalid ULID format), then fixed and removed debug code. Faster than guessing.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T04:02:36.159Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCSQFV6TA8SM8ZPKNVHK09T\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Traits field validation implementation followed clean pattern from existing ref validation. Adding to REF_FIELDS array and extending validateRefs() was straightforward. The test pattern from parser.test.ts made writing comprehensive tests easy. All 5 ACs covered in 6 tests.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T04:13:41.606Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCTE16XZGRDSEGMFFZFWTJ3\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop PR review workflow proved effective: dedicated review subagent correctly identified missing E2E tests as BLOCKING issue, prompted fix, re-review confirmed resolution, and merge completed successfully. The strict review criteria (AC coverage, E2E priority, test isolation) caught important gaps before merge.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T04:26:00.285Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCTR3VVRA9ECADDRDYEGPMR\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Following established code patterns (ReferenceIndex, AlignmentIndex) made TraitIndex implementation straightforward. The bidirectional mapping pattern and constructor-based indexing approach worked well for trait-spec relationships. Test structure with AC annotations provides clear traceability.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T04:31:30.684Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCVFM07FH8DHYPV3AA3TTJ8\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Trait display implementation completed efficiently by reusing TraitIndex foundation. Integrating into buildIndexes() made trait data available throughout CLI. Text and JSON output handled cleanly with separate formatting logic. Test fixtures required valid ULIDs - good validation caught this early.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T04:44:20.872Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCW3TDDPB6G1G8DFS10NAEE\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"ULID validation in tests requires Crockford base32 alphabet (excludes I, L, O, U). Common test ULID patterns like 01TRAIT10... or 01TASK10... are invalid because they contain 'I'. Should document this in test helpers or provide a utility function that generates valid test ULIDs with readable prefixes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T04:55:22.797Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Added testUlid() helper function to tests/helpers/cli.ts that generates valid Crockford base32 ULIDs. Also added documentation at top of file explaining ULID character restrictions (no I, L, O, U). Example: testUlid('TASK') produces valid '01TASK00000000000000000000' - invalid chars are auto-replaced.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-22T19:37:28.386Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCWZ8SEY6Z49V14D2X73ZGE\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"loadSpecFile() only parsed first YAML document when multiple documents present (--- separators). Root cause: YAML.parse() vs YAML.parseAllDocuments(). This broke tests that appended traits to files using document separators. Fix was straightforward once identified, but debugging took time because manual tests worked (single document) while multi-document tests failed silently.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T05:10:22.255Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"This was a code bug that was fixed. loadSpecFile() now correctly uses YAML.parseAllDocuments() for multi-document files.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-22T19:37:51.390Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCX5DYS83R2SYQ1SNCNY03P\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Systematic debugging approach: When implementation code looks correct but tests fail, investigate test infrastructure first. Created isolated debug scripts to replicate exact test scenario, which revealed YAML parser only reading first document. This pattern of creating minimal reproduction scripts in scratchpad is valuable for debugging test failures.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T05:13:44.153Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCXGBQSPN7XYPRTV625E1TZ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Trait AC coverage validation implementation went smoothly by building on existing infrastructure. The TraitIndex and checkCompleteness() architecture made it straightforward to add inherited AC checking - just scan trait ACs the same way we scan direct ACs. The existing test coverage scanning and ref validation already handled most of the heavy lifting. Clean separation of concerns paid off.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T05:19:42.330Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCXQH9GZ4330JWEHD9QVXVT\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review workflow caught test quality issues before merge - the automated subagent review identified fluff tests and missing documentation that would have degraded test quality patterns in the codebase. The strict review criteria (MUST-FIX vs suggestions) worked well.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T05:23:37.393Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCXY2PK61MY006C48874R44\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Full PR review → fix → merge cycle completed successfully in one iteration. The Ralph Loop workflow of dedicating review subagent, fixing issues, waiting for CI, and merging is working smoothly. Key: strict review criteria and blocking on CI checks before merge.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T05:27:11.828Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCXYZYP9E8CJMRS7TJMW29G\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"CI checks can take 3-4 minutes to complete, which can consume a significant portion of an iteration when waiting for merge approval. Consider: (1) Starting CI early if possible, (2) Using wait time productively for reflection/documentation, (3) Maybe implementing a timeout strategy in Ralph Loop for when CI takes too long.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T05:27:41.782Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCYH1P91QYPT0Q1WKW9JJZE\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Trait CLI implementation followed clean separation: parser infrastructure (TYPE_TO_CHILD_FIELD, NESTED_ITEM_FIELDS) before CLI commands. This pattern worked well - infrastructure changes enabled CLI to use existing patterns (addChildItem, buildIndexes) without special cases. E2E tests caught integration issues early (traits not loading from manifest).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T05:37:33.385Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCZ3SHZSW2RDA6CCNTAPE5W\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"trait-cli tests fail in vitest despite implementation working correctly in manual testing. All 12 failing tests involve trait list/get/item commands. Manual replication of exact test scenarios works perfectly. Tests use same CLI dist files. Issue is test infrastructure related, not implementation. Need to investigate vitest test execution environment differences.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T05:47:47.647Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"This was a test infrastructure issue that was resolved. Trait CLI tests now pass.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-22T19:37:56.472Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCZ4SK76NHJM1N4YT2RHS4Y\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Used dedicated review subagent to identify critical schema bug in PR #104. The subagent's strict review caught that ManifestSchema was missing the traits field, causing Zod to strip traits during parsing. This was a blocking bug that made all functionality fail. Fixed the issue and verified through extensive manual testing. Pattern: Always use review subagents before merge, they catch bugs that aren't obvious from code inspection alone.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T05:48:20.455Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFD0A2TX3WZFG6RQMN45Y8CR\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Test fixture anti-patterns found: (1) Naive YAML string manipulation breaks structure - use CLI commands or proper YAML parsers instead. (2) Tests creating invalid kspec structures - spec items must be nested under module items in type-specific fields. (3) Slug collisions with existing fixtures - tests need unique identifiers. (4) Missing test dependencies - tests assuming entities exist without creating them. These issues compound and hide real implementation bugs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T06:08:42.334Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Added documentation to tests/helpers/cli.ts header explaining: (1) Don't use JSON.stringify for YAML fixtures (2) Use setupTempFixtures() with pre-built fixtures (preferred) (3) Write YAML strings directly with template literals (4) Use yaml library stringify for programmatic creation. Also added testUlid() helper to avoid invalid ULID issues.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-22T19:37:35.380Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFD0A8HPBCD40WAZSF3GMZRX\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Systematic test debugging approach worked well: (1) Run tests to see failures, (2) Isolate root cause through manual reproduction, (3) Fix fixtures to match actual kspec requirements, (4) Verify all tests pass. Using manual CLI invocations in temp dirs helped identify structural issues that weren't obvious from test code alone.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T06:08:48.182Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFD0DWVHZJSMHVAQY11HFPEF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review feedback loop worked well: (1) Subagent identified test quality issues with clear MUST-FIX verdict, (2) Systematic debugging traced root causes (YAML structure, slug conflicts, missing deps), (3) Fixed all 12 test failures, (4) All 695 tests pass locally, (5) PR updated and CI re-running. The strict review criteria (E2E tests, temp dirs, AC coverage, no fluff) ensured high quality implementation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T06:10:47.281Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFD0VXY441EVBG6HA85HNYBT\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Merged PR #104 (trait CLI commands) successfully. Review subagent found 0 blocking issues, 100% AC coverage (8/8), all tests passing. Production-quality implementation with proper isolation and AC annotations.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T06:18:27.140Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFD15XE0W20ZA8M475J43TKY\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Test-driven development revealed implementation bugs in trait edge case handling. AC-2 (cycle detection) and AC-3 (broken ref detection) both show validation passing when should fail. This pattern (write tests → discover implementation incomplete) is good but slows progress when implementation gaps are large. Consider: (1) Review implementation completeness before writing E2E tests (2) Add unit tests for validation logic first (3) Use TDD for new features but integration-test existing features differently\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T06:23:54.304Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"This is expected TDD behavior - discovering implementation gaps through tests is part of the process. Not a problem to fix but a useful pattern to be aware of.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-22T19:38:07.580Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFD1TCR2MSTXEQE6TJD3ETG7\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Bug investigation pattern: When validation passes unexpectedly, check item counts in output. 'Items checked: 3' vs expected 5 revealed traits weren't being loaded. Count mismatches are powerful debugging signals for data loading issues.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T06:35:05.346Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFD2G0RJ53P1Z0YQWBTF7WEM\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Testing git operations in isolated test environments - git clone --mirror fails in vitest with 'repository does not exist' despite source repo being properly initialized with commits. Same commands work when run manually. May be related to how vitest sandboxes processes or handles child_process spawn. Need to investigate if this is a PATH issue, git config issue, or test isolation problem. This pattern will affect any future commands that need to test git cloning or repository manipulation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T06:46:53.970Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Known vitest environment issue. initGitRepo() helper handles basic git setup. Complex git cloning scenarios may need simpler approaches in tests.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-22T19:38:01.946Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFD2YKYFJ9WB1EX5R8D38WD1\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test helper pattern clarity - integration.test.ts showed the correct pattern of importing kspecOutput as kspec for string output. When tests fail due to type mismatches (expecting string, getting object), check imports against working test files.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T06:54:52.367Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFD2YSFK15FSYZC7X4J9GPX3\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Optional positional parameter order in CLI commands can create usability issues. [source] [dest] signature made it impossible to provide dest and default source. Changed to [dest] [source] which better matches common usage patterns. Consider: use named options (--source, --dest) for commands where both parameters are truly optional and order-independent.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T06:54:58.035Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFD2YYTAEEPDQ6CA3P6WSJ9H\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Systematic debugging approach worked well: (1) Verified git clone works standalone, (2) Added debug output to trace actual parameters, (3) Discovered output was empty not error, (4) Checked test helper return types, (5) Found pattern in working tests. Each step narrowed the problem space until root cause was clear.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T06:55:03.498Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFDPKZC956WTYA4BA7Q7SDQB\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Shadow branch worktree gets removed when checking out branches. After merging PR and checking out main, .kspec/ worktree was removed. Attempting to recreate with 'git worktree add .kspec kspec-meta' created nested .kspec/.kspec/ worktree breaking kspec. Fix required absolute paths and manual cleanup. Root cause: git worktree add interprets paths relative to CWD which may be inside .kspec. Consider: (1) kspec commands that detect missing worktree and auto-repair (2) fix spawn error in 'kspec shadow repair' (3) prevent nested worktree creation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T12:38:35.146Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFDPM7VF7ZGE02MCP3JB7131\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph Loop iteration completed successfully: (1) Checked for open PRs per instructions (2) Found PR #106 with failing tests (7/8) (3) Launched review subagent to identify issues (4) Fixed all 3 blocking issues (worktree metadata cleanup, test setup, helper usage) (5) Verified locally (8/8 tests + full suite 707 passing) (6) Pushed and waited for CI (all green) (7) Merged PR and completed task @01KFBBTT (8) Captured 4 observations. Full workflow from PR review to merge completion in single iteration.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T12:38:43.824Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFDZBXCJQWP1CHC0277JAA0V\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Completed first task in spec review sequence (@01KFDYAW). Simple cleanup task (removing non-existent file reference) was straightforward. Shadow branch auto-commit worked correctly - no manual commit needed for .kspec/ changes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:11:28.146Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFDZC1RFZFR8FEHBFCEQ9S7G\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Easy to accidentally stay in .kspec/ directory after checking git log and then run kspec commands, which fail. The error message is clear ('Cannot run kspec from inside .kspec/ directory'), but would be better to avoid this by being more careful about pwd or using absolute paths.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:11:32.624Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Documented in AGENTS.md 'Important: Always Run from Project Root' section with troubleshooting guidance\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T05:13:29.247Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFDZGT05N02FNX2HXM4CRT8H\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"E2E validation workflow effective for confirming system readiness. Created test data, verified behavior, cleaned up - all within single iteration. Trait system confirmed production-ready without needing to create permanent test fixtures.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:14:08.518Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFDZVK4MA028H031BR26YZCE\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Manually editing .kspec/kynetic.yaml to add traits requires:\\n1. Understanding ULID format constraints (no I, L, O, U chars)\\n2. Manually generating valid ULIDs\\n3. Working around shadow branch auto-commit restrictions\\n\\nThe kspec trait add command would have handled all this, but for bulk creation of 8 traits with detailed AC, manual YAML editing was more practical. Future improvement: support adding AC during trait creation, or bulk trait import from YAML file.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:20:01.941Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFDZVT1Z2HBAY7D8T3M1JEE2\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Debugging approach for YAML loading issues:\\n1. Used node scripts to test individual components (initContext, extractItemsFromRaw, SpecItemSchema)\\n2. Isolated the failure point (ULID validation regex)\\n3. This incremental debugging approach was much faster than adding console.logs to source code\\n\\nPattern to remember: when kspec commands don't work as expected, test the parser/schema layers directly with minimal scripts.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:20:09.024Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFE03DTPTD76XA5J8DH6H5KM\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Systematic AC addition workflow worked efficiently: grouped items by category (schema types, task types, relationships, YAML), added 2 AC per item following given/when/then format. Pattern: each AC should test a specific aspect of the item's behavior. For type definitions, one AC validates structure and one validates usage/purpose.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:24:18.647Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFE0E736KWBTZDRA1M01W1W8\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Shadow branch auto-commit pattern works seamlessly for spec changes. Modified cli.yaml (spec file) and all changes were automatically committed to shadow branch via kspec commands (task note, task complete). No manual git operations needed. This confirms the design - spec changes live in shadow branch, auto-committed by CLI.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:30:12.199Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFE0EM48X85MQSJDCJJMDWPR\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Trait application pattern for CLI commands: (1) All commands get json-output, semantic-exit-codes, error-guidance. (2) Batch operations add multi-ref-batch. (3) Destructive operations add confirmation-prompt. Applied consistently to 7 task lifecycle commands. Pattern is clear and repeatable for remaining commands.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:30:25.545Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFE0RJTKJG04MGEVZ5NFJZ6G\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Shadow branch auto-commit workflow: File changes made via Edit tool are automatically committed when kspec commands (like task note) run. No manual git add/commit needed for shadow-tracked files. This is the expected behavior and works well.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:35:51.892Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFE0RS0XE3AYATECAMNNPN2X\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Directory context confusion: When running git/bash commands that cd into .kspec, subsequent kspec commands fail with 'Cannot run from .kspec directory'. Need to be explicit about returning to project root or use absolute paths. Mitigated by using 'cd /absolute/path && command' pattern.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:35:58.237Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Documented in AGENTS.md - use absolute paths or check pwd before kspec commands\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T05:13:31.492Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFE13K905B3263M48Y7Z4M19\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Spec review task series completed efficiently. Breaking down large spec updates into 7 focused tasks (trait creation, AC addition, trait application by command category) enabled systematic progress tracking and validation at each step. TodoWrite tool helped track progress within each task.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:41:52.801Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFE13RKXKERPMTNPY7PJHGJN\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Working directory confusion: Agent tools (Read, Edit, etc.) can change working directory during exploration, but this isn't always obvious. When pwd shows .kspec/, kspec commands fail. Need to be more aware of current directory before running kspec commands. Pattern: always use absolute paths or check pwd before kspec commands.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:41:58.270Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Documented in AGENTS.md 'Important: Always Run from Project Root' section\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T05:13:34.013Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFE1BE12S5W2TCJAC1K6DN1E\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Fixed spec-implementation mismatch by updating the spec to match working implementation. Key insight: When spec and implementation diverge, evaluate which is more useful before blindly 'fixing' code to match spec. In this case, task dependency checking was more actionable than spec hierarchy checking, so updating the spec was the right choice. The tests validated that the implementation was correct for what it does.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:46:09.570Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFE1BKDZXAFHWFZE855VF9HR\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Working directory kept changing to .kspec/ during the session, requiring multiple 'cd ..' commands. This happens when reading files in .kspec/ or checking git status. Should be more mindful of pwd before running kspec commands, or establish a pattern of always returning to project root after .kspec/ operations.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:46:15.104Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Documented in AGENTS.md - always return to project root after .kspec/ operations\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T05:13:36.432Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFEYT39MFQGBH9YY7K8GSH8K\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Subagent review of specs before implementation caught 4 missing ACs and 2 missing flag behaviors. Worth doing for non-trivial specs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T00:20:58.804Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFEYT8CH48P6B4WGKTCM7627\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Breaking monolithic feature into requirements before deriving tasks produces self-contained tasks with proper dependencies. One feature with 14 ACs became 4 requirements with 4-6 ACs each.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T00:21:04.018Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFEZ86NHX1SYXX38DJBN44A8\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Spec-plan session validated guided workflow design - the manual process of creating the guided-workflow-execution spec followed exactly the pattern the feature would automate: requirements → exploration → design → review → spec creation → derive. Dogfooding opportunity once implemented.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T00:28:41.009Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFM7NAN2GW0BEXX6JZR5MV5\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task reset implementation went smoothly. Following existing patterns from task.ts (cancel, complete, block) made implementation straightforward. Comprehensive test coverage (15 tests for 6 ACs) caught no issues. Shadow commit verification simplified by trusting commitIfShadow success rather than parsing git internals. All 783 tests pass on first try.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T06:35:23.349Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFMRZ746PMVGB00TDS532GR\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task scoping from retrospective notes works well - the task notes from the ralph loop retrospective provided clear, actionable improvements that translated directly into implementation steps.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T06:44:50.533Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFMS3G3EZ6PGSN7DV8WGJ76\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR CI waiting pattern - when CI is pending on a PR, better to move to next task rather than blocking iteration. The PR will be picked up in a future iteration once CI completes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T06:44:54.915Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFN7TYV4VEBM6J47RWDRQYV\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review workflow validated: spawned subagent for strict review before merge, identified blocking issues (spec field name mismatch, fluff test), fixed them, then merged. Review agent correctly flagged AC-5 test as not validating its criterion.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T06:52:57.691Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFN7ZAX6FD7G6EC21N9M15X\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Merged PR #114 before pushing fix commit (66010b6) that addressed review feedback. Had to create new PR #115 with the fixes. Should push all commits before merging PR.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T06:53:02.174Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Historical incident - lesson learned: always verify fix commits are pushed before merging PR\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T05:13:41.217Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFN83NCYJACXVPC2A0EA0RZ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test improvement strategy: AC-5 test was fluff (admitted in comments it didn't test the scenario). Rewrote to actually set up dependency scenario and validate via tasks ready command. Understanding how dependency checking works (at query time, not start time) was key to writing correct test.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T06:53:06.604Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFP5DB5QDZT8HR91XN8C7SQ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"CI workflow implementation pattern: GitHub Actions with github-script action provides clean GraphQL API integration without custom tooling. For review thread resolution checks, the isResolved and isOutdated fields are exactly what's needed - filtering for \\\\!isResolved && \\\\!isOutdated gives accurate results. Excluding outdated threads prevents false positives from force-pushed commits.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T07:09:06.789Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFPWAAGAH865DKPYBR5W63E\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"CI workflow implementation was already partially complete from previous session - checking git status and existing files before starting work prevented duplicate effort. The workflow uses GitHub GraphQL API to query review thread resolution status, which is more robust than REST API approach for checking unresolved comments.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T07:21:37.360Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFPWFJXA1Y2ZFA3FG4BJAN1\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop PR workflow is working well: started iteration by checking for open PRs, reviewed and merged PR #115 (fixing spec trailers), then picked next priority task. PR review → merge → task selection creates natural workflow cadence.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T07:21:42.749Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFPY13M7AWHEQSM6Z3HKB0C\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review workflow working well: Claude review posted actionable feedback (null check for comment.author), fix was straightforward (optional chaining), all checks passed after fix, and merge proceeded smoothly. The automated review catch prevented a potential production bug.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T07:22:33.460Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFPY60ZHYYCHBA3PB3E7HD6\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Skipped test was actually ready to run - validation infrastructure improvements had resolved the original issue. Worth periodically reviewing skipped tests to see if they can be unskipped. Test passed immediately when .skip was removed.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T07:22:38.495Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFQQAFR8FZY9EBESFK1MFBZ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test fixture management pattern: Using setupTempFixtures() + removing .git + git init creates clean test environment with kspec structure but no commits. More reliable than manually constructing YAML. Pattern used successfully in AC-2 and AC-5 tests.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T07:36:22.264Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFQSB85FCJJK5MBENJ2GW7M\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR creation workflow smooth - auto-generated branch name from task slug, moved commit from main to feature branch, created comprehensive PR body from task/spec context. Task notes provided all context needed for PR summary.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T07:37:28.581Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFR8HXWQ2TS9R6TGDCY90R0\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Iteration 8: Successfully implemented @01KFC3AR (--description flag for task add) from start to PR creation. Pattern that worked well:\\n1. Read spec to understand all ACs\\n2. Check existing schema (description field already existed)\\n3. Add CLI option and wire to TaskInput\\n4. Write comprehensive tests FIRST with AC annotations\\n5. Fix shell escaping issues in tests (not implementation bugs)\\n6. All 792 tests pass on first implementation try\\n7. Created PR with full context\\n\\nTotal time: ~15 minutes for feature + tests + PR. Clean handoff to next iteration.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T07:45:46.941Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFRD1Q9A8Q1M2YE5VK8R8CD\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"CI test failures can occur when tests don't configure git user.name/email before running git commit in temp dirs. Pattern to follow: Always add 'git config user.email/user.name' commands after 'git init' in tests that create fresh repos and commit. Found in PR #118 - test passed locally but failed in CI.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T07:48:14.185Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFRDEN1V6A68Y2RSDFPX84V\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Iteration 8 complete - accomplished multiple tasks:\\n\\n1. Reviewed PR #118 (log empty repo fix) - comprehensive review passed\\n2. Implemented @01KFC3AR (--description flag) with full AC coverage\\n3. Created PR #119 for --description implementation\\n4. Fixed failing CI test in PR #118 (missing git config)\\n5. Captured observations (success + friction patterns)\\n\\nKey patterns:\\n- PR review workflow with subagent worked well\\n- Implementation -> tests -> PR flow is smooth\\n- CI failures often reveal env config issues (git user.name/email)\\n- Test patterns: always configure git after init in temp dirs\\n\\nBoth PRs now ready for merge once CI completes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T07:48:27.426Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFS1A3YTHSJ31GK245P75VC\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review subagents worked excellently in parallel. Spawned two review agents simultaneously - both produced comprehensive, strict reviews identifying issues (PR #119 had failing test, PR #118 was clean). The parallel approach saved time and both reviews were thorough with proper AC coverage validation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T07:59:18.142Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFS1G84GSYKT6AFWVA8R0GM\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Shell escaping in tests is tricky across environments. The $'...' syntax worked locally but failed in CI. Using printf with double-escaped newlines ($(printf 'Line 1\\\\\\\\nLine 2\\\\\\\\nLine 3')) is more portable and explicit. Tests should prefer printf over $'...' for multiline string handling in bash commands.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T07:59:24.421Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFS1PAWEHVW5E4JA8FXJ2BD\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"RALPH_LOOP_INSTRUCTIONS.md PR review workflow is well-designed: check for PRs first, spawn review subagents, use decision tree (pass→merge, fail→fix). Following this process caught issues before merge and ensured quality. The --merge flag (not --squash) preserves kspec trailers which is critical for kspec log @ref functionality.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T07:59:30.652Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFS6VWQ8CAA2Z4S238YWXRR\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Successfully completed full PR review cycle in single iteration: reviewed 2 PRs in parallel, merged 1 immediately (PR #118), fixed failing test in other (PR #119), waited for CI to confirm fix, then merged. Both tasks (@01KFBPQA, @01KFC3AR) completed. The --watch flag on gh pr checks was useful for waiting on CI completion.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T08:02:20.183Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFSGAE5R6B49N4G4P52NQDD\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Spec status audit revealed that implementation often outpaces spec updates. ULID shortening, cascade updates, and YAML conventions were all implemented but marked not_started. The cascade feature in item set updated 18 child items automatically, demonstrating the value of hierarchical status propagation. Shadow branch separation meant no main branch PR was needed for metadata updates.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T08:07:29.989Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFT1E7G0FE9P83PPAJAQ0WJ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"State enforcement implementation went smoothly - clear spec with detailed ACs made implementation straightforward. Breaking existing tests was expected and fixing them reinforced the new workflow.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T08:16:50.929Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFT1JE45D0FKYAESH496GWV\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test helper pattern (kspecWithStatus vs kspecError) worked well once I found the right function. The cli.ts helper exports are well-structured for different test needs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T08:16:55.236Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFT481GRXPVSQJ0T63D2S1R\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR creation workflow smooth: auto-generated branch name from task slug, created branch, reset main, pushed, created PR with comprehensive summary including AC coverage checklist. The /pr skill handled the complexity well.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T08:18:22.896Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFTRJSKQ48241MWX3GR7VFJ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"JSON output audit revealed mostly good patterns - only one inconsistency found (clone-for-testing had its own --json flag). The systematic approach of searching for JSON.stringify, checking stderr handling, and documenting envelope format conventions was effective. Key insight: envelope format variation is intentional and serves different use cases (raw data vs success confirmations vs errors vs hook-specific formats).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T08:29:29.267Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFTSZW5903HK4XPN6J5Q6C6\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop iteration 13 completed successfully: Reviewed and merged PR #120, then completed task @01KFBDM8 (JSON output consistency audit). The PR review workflow worked smoothly with automated CI checks. The audit task was well-scoped with clear notes about what to investigate. Created PR #121 for the fix. Key efficiency: Using TodoWrite to track sub-tasks within the larger audit task helped maintain focus.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T08:30:15.430Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFVC7840GWEQVAE422SRD8H\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task @01KFBDQE 'Add spec-schema drift detection' needs clearer scoping. The original note mentions three issues but #2 appears to be a misunderstanding (already handled by --staleness check), and #3 (fixture conflicts) lacks concrete examples. Tasks derived from retrospective observations should include specific examples or reproduction steps, not just abstract descriptions of problems.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T08:40:12.805Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFVEK1FMH6M89DZJRGQYSSP\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop iteration 14: Successfully merged PR #121 (JSON output consistency), researched drift detection task (found it under-specified), and started well-defined task-set-batch task. Pattern: When a ready task lacks concrete examples or clear scope, checkpoint it with observations and move to a better-defined task rather than spinning on requirements gathering.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T08:41:30.415Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFVG0YMGCGHMCBRPPE67CGT\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Stop hook successfully caught incomplete session cleanup. Ralph loop should always checkpoint in-progress tasks before ending iteration, even if not completing them. The hook reminder ensures continuity for next session.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T08:42:17.428Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFW9Q828XCGG5B6HH1KWHEB\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Batch operation pattern in batch.ts worked well for task set implementation. executeBatchOperation() handled all the complexity of partial failures, ref deduplication, and output formatting. Helper function extraction (setTaskFields) allowed clean code reuse between single and batch modes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T08:56:19.459Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFWAJYXXY0SY7M12YAA4CT9\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test-first implementation worked well for task set batch. Writing all 15 tests first (based on spec ACs) provided clear targets and caught issues early. The 'write tests → implement → fix → repeat' cycle was faster than trying to implement and test simultaneously.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T08:56:47.837Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFWR2MPFXFF5BJ0VE5MNCCB\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop PR review workflow successful: spawned review subagent for pending_review task, agent performed comprehensive AC coverage check (13 ACs validated), test quality assessment (E2E strategy, isolation), and edge case verification. Review found no issues. Waited for CI, then merged with --merge flag to preserve trailers. Pattern: pending_review task -> spawn review agent -> wait for CI green -> merge -> complete task. This workflow ensures systematic quality checks without human intervention.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T09:04:09.879Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFWV250GFXWADZX4VW2ARSW\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task @01KFBDR7 'Improve Result type enforcement' has unclear scope. Initial investigation shows current Result pattern (discriminated unions with 'ok' field) is well-implemented and consistently used. Most code properly checks .ok before accessing success fields. Task note suggests multiple improvements (branded types, lint rules, never throw library) but unclear which is actually needed or would provide value. Without concrete examples of bugs or near-misses from this pattern, hard to prioritize improvements. Recommendation: Block task pending concrete evidence of problems, or pivot to documentation task.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T09:05:47.681Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFX1B8F3QJB5HCX8TKY0V7C\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Iteration 16: Successfully completed full PR workflow - reviewed and merged PR #122 (task set batch), blocked unclear task @01KFBDR7 (Result types), completed and shipped @01KFBJFE (dedupe formatRelativeTime) via PR #123. Pattern: PR review -> merge -> pick new task -> implement -> commit -> PR. Task selection improved: skipped manual_only task, blocked ambiguous task, picked clear tech-debt task. Total: 2 PRs processed (1 merged, 1 created).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T09:09:13.615Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFXTYEDSFF82Q1JXGX8CGME\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"KSPEC_TEST_TTY pattern works well for testing interactive prompts. By adding an env var check alongside process.stdin.isTTY, we can simulate TTY in tests while preserving real TTY detection in production. This pattern can be reused for other interactive commands.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T09:23:12.461Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFXV389J8EPW2ZJXQF6CEYR\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test error message checking pattern: When commands fail, error messages can be in either stdout or stderr. Using 'const output = result.stdout + result.stderr' and checking that combined output is more robust than checking just stdout. This worked for all 4 initially failing tests.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T09:23:17.386Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFYBZ4Z6V0DQQBYTJ4XCJYA\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Test helper API mismatch: kspec() expects string args but wrote tests using array syntax. Need to convert ['item', 'delete', '@ref'] to 'item delete @ref'. Should have checked helper signature before writing all tests.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T09:32:30.239Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Test helper API is documented - kspec() takes string args. Check helper signature before writing tests.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-22T19:38:17.603Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFYC3N6H7K8XPZ26MKMAAQV\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"findChildItems already existed in items.ts with correct implementation - avoided duplicate code by discovering existing helper. Good pattern: search for existing helpers before implementing new ones.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T09:32:34.854Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFZ0F443X3JG15DVT86TQS9\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test helper API documentation was critical for fixing tests. The kspec() helper signature (string args, not array) wasn't obvious from test file alone. Reading tests/helpers/cli.ts revealed correct usage pattern. Future: consider adding JSDoc examples in helper file showing common patterns.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T09:43:41.957Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFZF7C18HAJ6GR2RP69V6W6\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Git handling of files with newlines in filenames is extremely difficult. Standard commands like 'git rm' with shell quoting don't work. Even null-terminated operations struggle with escaping. Solution: Python script with subprocess.run() successfully handled the special characters where shell commands failed. This type of git corruption should be prevented at commit time if possible.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T09:51:45.537Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFZFCVXFDTXRZJMNVNTC5GP\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review subagent workflow is effective. Spawning a dedicated subagent with strict review criteria caught the critical file corruption issue before merge. The subagent provided detailed analysis including: blocking issues prioritized, test coverage gaps identified, code quality assessment, and specific fix commands. This caught a problem that would have been difficult to spot in manual review.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T09:51:51.165Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFZFHSEJXS6CW39BN7CMF7Z\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Interactive rebase with automated editor worked well for fixing historical commits. Using GIT_EDITOR with sed to automatically mark commits for editing eliminated manual intervention. Pattern: GIT_EDITOR='sed -i \\\"s/^pick <hash>/edit <hash>/\\\"' git rebase -i <base>. This allowed scripted fixes to commit history while maintaining full control.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T09:51:56.206Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFZG3YZZGRCGKG93MM087C1\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop PR review workflow successfully prevented corrupted code from being merged. The iteration followed RALPH_LOOP_INSTRUCTIONS.md: (1) Checked for open PRs, (2) Spawned review subagent, (3) Fixed blocking issues found, (4) Re-verified tests locally, (5) Merged with --merge to preserve trailers, (6) Completed task with proper documentation. This systematic approach caught and fixed a critical issue that manual review might have missed.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T09:52:14.815Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFZSMSZMRKN2SQKZS42QC6F\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Tech debt cleanup pattern: When finding duplicate logic, check if the duplication serves a purpose (e.g., specialized behavior) or is truly redundant. In this case, inbox.ts had a local shortUlid() helper that was functionally identical to .slice(0,8) used elsewhere. The 'smart' ReferenceIndex.shortUlid() method wasn't needed for ephemeral inbox items without slugs. Solution: remove helper, use direct string slicing consistently. This makes code more maintainable and easier to understand.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T09:57:26.975Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFG0GWZC73H2GXDA2E5DDEJG\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Vitest v1 to v4 major version upgrade required only minimal changes: single async/await fix in test file. Breaking changes were well-contained. The vitest v4 warning message ('Promise returned by expect(actual).rejects.toThrow(expected) was not awaited') was clear and pointed directly to the issue, making the fix trivial. Major version upgrades don't always require extensive refactoring if the codebase follows best practices.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T10:10:09.005Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFG13F217CN26AT45BAW7VBR\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review and merge workflow is efficient - spawned parallel review subagents for both PRs, got clear recommendations, merged both immediately, completed tasks, pulled changes, and started new work. The review agents provided comprehensive analysis including local test verification and CI status context.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T10:20:17.345Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFG1CXNHG6X3V5B5W2KAHZ6Q\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task reset command workflow: Reset cancelled task to pending, then start/submit/complete with proper documentation. Fixed @task-yaml-formatting status efficiently using task reset flow.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T10:25:27.218Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFG1JNM235TJ78BTXQZJYKN2\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task @extract-test-helpers was already completed before being picked up. The workflow correctly handled this by verifying implementation (tests/helpers/cli.ts exists with all helpers, no duplicates in test files, 841 tests pass) and documenting findings in task notes before marking complete. This demonstrates good verification practices when tasks may have been completed out of band.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T10:28:35.586Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFGRVJPBP5HS9S19ENFGS448\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Spec-first with traits: Creating spec, adding traits, then deriving task immediately surfaced what tests were needed (trait ACs). Applied to --clear-deps feature.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T17:15:24.748Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFHJP6MKVAJ7653KC87J8C6Q\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR automated review catching AC test coverage gaps - the Claude reviewer on PR #141 identified two missing test assertions (--clear-deps and --automation author validation) that I'd missed. The strict AC coverage requirement in CLAUDE.md combined with automated review provides good safety net.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T00:46:51.539Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFHYJ9DH26CRPRFWZJYXKPJP\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"When debugging opaque CI/auth errors, search GitHub issues early. A quick search for 'npm trusted publishers OIDC' would have found the npm version bug immediately, saving significant iteration time.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T04:14:26.225Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJ636YGAN4ACZ8D1HVT10HQ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Workflow run foundation implementation demonstrates good schema-first development pattern. Defined all Zod schemas first, then storage operations, then CLI commands, then tests. This ordering prevented type errors and made the implementation flow smoothly. The type safety from Zod schemas caught issues early in compilation rather than at runtime.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T06:26:00.785Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJ63DA38WC8GVKEQ4W0G2Q0\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"E2E test fixture setup requires understanding of proper YAML formatting. Using JSON.stringify() to create YAML files doesn't work - produces invalid YAML syntax. Tests need either: (1) setupTempFixtures() with pre-built fixtures, (2) manual YAML strings, or (3) yaml library stringify. This pattern repeats across test files - consider documenting test fixture patterns in testing guide.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T06:26:07.300Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Documented in tests/helpers/cli.ts header: Don't use JSON.stringify() for YAML - use template literals, yaml library stringify, or pre-built fixtures.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-22T19:37:40.972Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJ6YNZMPF5YKAJWVDRFP1K1\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Test fixtures with invalid ULIDs (e.g., 01TEST000...) silently fail schema validation. Error only visible when parsing logic is instrumented with debug output. Should add test helper that validates fixture data before use, or use ulid() to generate proper test IDs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T06:41:00.916Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Added testUlid() helper that generates valid Crockford base32 ULIDs and auto-replaces invalid characters (I->J, L->K, O->0, U->V). Also documented common invalid patterns in tests/helpers/cli.ts header.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-22T19:37:45.999Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJ7AGSPNACKH2TCY9SZT5E8\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test fixture ULID validation issue was quickly identified through systematic debugging. The root cause (invalid ULID format in test fixtures) was found by examining validation failures and understanding that ULIDs must match proper regex format. Fix was straightforward: import ulid() and generate valid ULIDs. This pattern of using valid test data that matches production validation rules is important for reliable tests.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T06:47:28.823Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJ7APXVT6TXJH0CCEVY64XB\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Tests should use non-shadow mode setup (files in project root) unless specifically testing shadow functionality. The .kspec/ directory is ONLY used when shadow branch is properly configured. This keeps test setup simple and matches how kspec actually discovers files in non-shadow environments. Pattern: create kynetic.yaml, kynetic.meta.yaml, project.tasks.yaml directly in temp root directory.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T06:47:35.099Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJ7SAGTW27KKHS2RSXV019H\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"When fixing bugs with AC coverage: First read the code to understand the implementation, then identify the exact function/logic that needs updating, then add tests that validate the AC before implementing. This workflow ensures the fix is correct and properly validated. For AC-15, updating getParentTaskRef() to filter cancelled tasks was straightforward once the problem was identified.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T06:55:33.914Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJ8J51FZP9DQY25PYYS3Y3Y\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Systematic approach to code cleanup - created comprehensive mapping document before making changes, built automated sed script to handle bulk replacements, then manually verified and fixed edge cases. This pattern of 'map-script-verify-fix' worked well for 72 annotations across 9 files with zero regressions (all 874 tests pass). Script-first approach with manual verification is effective for large-scale mechanical refactoring.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T07:09:07.503Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJ8JBSB7WR6M3VD2HAW3B32\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review-merge flow worked smoothly: spawned subagent for comprehensive review, verified CI checks passed, checked for review comments, merged with --merge to preserve trailers, then completed task. The strict review requirements (AC coverage, test quality, isolation) caught in advance prevent merge issues. Subagent review before PR creation + automated CI review + manual merge checks = robust quality gate.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T07:09:14.411Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJ97VFR4WDPKNCVQJ9QMKAE\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review workflow is effective: spawned review subagent found 3 incorrect spec references that would have been missed. The strict review caught that annotations referenced @shadow-init instead of @shadow-init-remote for remote detection code. Fixed before merge, maintaining proper traceability.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T07:20:58.616Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJ9NFZ64QGSJZ61VSZ5ATRH\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Workflow step navigation implementation went smoothly. The existing workflow foundation (AC tests, error patterns, helper functions) made adding the next command straightforward. Test-first approach caught edge cases early (e.g., inferring run when exactly one active). Pattern of checking spec ACs against test coverage helped ensure nothing was missed.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T07:28:25.575Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJ9YR00XGX63F4Z2KYZA5KE\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review and merge workflow executed successfully. Used Task agent for comprehensive review (AC coverage, test quality, E2E strategy, test isolation all verified). All CI checks passed, automated reviews found no issues. Task completed cleanly with proper trailers and spec sync. Total time from PR creation to merge: ~4 minutes. The structured review process caught no issues because implementation quality was excellent from the start - comprehensive E2E test coverage, proper AC annotations, perfect test isolation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T07:33:28.704Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJ9YY8VPR4G1VVQK20H092C\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Workflow step navigation implementation demonstrates excellent code-to-spec traceability. AC annotations used throughout both implementation and tests. Run reference inference (auto-detect single active run) provides great UX. Error messages include actionable guidance with exact commands. Summary output on completion (duration, step counts) matches spec requirements exactly. This is a model implementation for future workflow features.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T07:33:35.131Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJA21CHKVD52598EQ9994FS\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Added comprehensive E2E tests for shadow hook functionality. Tests verify: 1) Hook installation during init copies from hooks/pre-commit to .git/hooks/pre-commit with executable permissions, 2) Hook blocks unauthorized commits (verifies commit count stays at 1), 3) Hook allows commits with KSPEC_SHADOW_COMMIT=1 env var (verifies commit count increases and message is correct). Used real hook file for tests 2 and 3 to ensure accurate behavior. All tests run in isolated temp directories. Task notes captured implementation approach before coding.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T07:35:16.626Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJA3PTYEPFHK8XHNEQGCRJV\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Iteration 8 completed: Merged PR #157 (workflow step navigation), then completed task @01KFJ4VT (shadow hook tests). Created PR #158. Workflow: reviewed and merged open PR first (per RALPH_LOOP_INSTRUCTIONS), then picked highest priority ready task. Task had clear 3-case scope from notes. Added tests to existing shadow.test.ts file, all 61 tests pass. PR created with /pr skill - auto-generated branch name test/shadow-hook-tests from commit message and task context.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T07:36:11.358Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJAVEGVBTYJ38PFTP30V5C2\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test-driven workflow implementation pattern worked well: wrote comprehensive E2E tests covering all ACs before refining implementation. The tests caught a subtle ordering issue (exit criteria must be checked before entry criteria) and a logical issue (skipping should bypass entry criteria for next step). Having 15 tests covering edge cases (strict/advisory modes, skip/confirm/force combinations) gave confidence that the implementation was correct. All 915 tests passing confirms no regressions.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T07:49:09.276Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJBNXX3C7PDGBTJ3PH4S070\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Automated PR review (Greptile) caught critical bug where entry_confirmed was never recorded - only exit_confirmed was working. The review identified that entry_confirmed remained undefined in all cases. This demonstrates the value of automated code review in catching semantic bugs that pass tests. The fix involved creating stub step results when advancing to the next step to capture entry_confirmed, then updating those stubs when the step completes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:03:36.995Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJBP2QJF9JV14331T8YGTF8\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Test failures from architectural changes can be misleading - when implementing stub step results, tests failed because they expected specific array lengths. The failures looked like bugs but were actually correct behavior - the architecture changed. Need to carefully evaluate whether test failures indicate bugs or just outdated expectations when making architectural changes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:03:41.938Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Expected behavior during architectural changes. Test failures from changed expectations (not bugs) are part of refactoring.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-22T19:38:12.290Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJBZJXM7ETYK1NKSY5S7CKW\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Workflow advanced features implementation completed smoothly. Key success factors: (1) Read existing workflow implementation first to understand patterns, (2) Extended schema before implementing CLI commands, (3) Followed existing test patterns for comprehensive coverage, (4) All 13 new tests passed on first run without fixes needed. The incremental approach (schema → commands → tests) worked well for this feature.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:08:53.429Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJC23TKBA6EQKETRSY3BP91\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"The /pr skill workflow (auto-generate branch name from context, move commits from main to feature branch, create PR) worked seamlessly for shipping completed work. The skill correctly derived 'feat/workflow-advanced-features' from the task reference, handled the branch creation and main reset cleanly, and created a comprehensive PR. This pattern is efficient for the ralph loop where work completes on main and needs to be shipped via PR.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:10:16.275Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJC2AA94N276JWH542F5RYD\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task state transition worked well: pending_review status held the completed work until PR was created, then completing the task after PR creation provides clean separation. This matches the RALPH_LOOP_INSTRUCTIONS.md pattern: task submit → PR creation → task complete after merge. However, I completed the task immediately after PR creation rather than after merge - should verify if this is the intended workflow or if completion should wait for merge.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:10:22.921Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJC2TSMBR0T2VDH5Y4CPNBH\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Completed task @task-workflow-advanced-features immediately after PR creation, but RALPH_LOOP_INSTRUCTIONS.md line 20 specifies task completion should happen AFTER merge. The correct workflow is: task submit → /pr → review → merge → task complete. Need to follow this sequence in future iterations to maintain proper task state. There's no way to 'uncomplete' a task once marked completed.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:10:39.796Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Lesson learned - workflow documented in AGENTS.md: submit → PR → review → merge → complete\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T05:18:17.949Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJCFDD4RMTAP9TSVRK20KYQ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Complete iteration 12 workflow executed successfully: Found pending_review task → Created PR #160 with /pr skill → Spawned review subagent → Review approved with 100% AC coverage → Merged PR with --merge strategy → Pulled merged changes to local main. The automated review subagent provided excellent quality checks (AC coverage, test quality, code patterns). Total time from pending_review to merged: ~8 minutes. Key learning: Task should stay in pending_review until AFTER merge (I completed it prematurely after PR creation).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:17:32.069Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJCFN0Q9KV5C0YFHYKP4KWX\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Review subagent pattern from RALPH_LOOP_INSTRUCTIONS.md worked exceptionally well. Single Task tool invocation with focused prompt ('check code quality, test coverage, alignment with spec, be strict about AC coverage') produced comprehensive review in table format covering: AC coverage (100%), code quality (excellent), test quality (E2E, no fluff), CI status (passing), files changed summary, and clear merge decision. The strict AC coverage requirement caught that all 4 direct ACs + 6 inherited trait ACs were properly tested. This automated review quality rivals human PR reviews.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:17:39.864Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJCZ4TFV7MBRTD896F4GR30\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Using spawnSync instead of execSync for test helpers provides better control over stdio streams. Key insight: execSync only returns stdout on success - stderr is lost. spawnSync captures both stdout/stderr in separate properties regardless of exit code. This pattern is more predictable for testing CLI tools that write warnings to stderr.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:26:07.567Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJCZB7A5PA8KMX4WMPJP840\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test-first verification for infrastructure changes: after making the helper change, ran full test suite to verify no regressions. The failing tests revealed a subtle stdin handling bug (empty string vs undefined) that would have been hard to catch otherwise. Full test coverage paid off immediately.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:26:14.122Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJDBDPNEMGRRJVXJZ830ADQ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Biome initialization process worked smoothly - the auto-init command detected the repo structure and configured appropriate excludes (dist/) and VCS integration automatically. Only manual change needed was adjusting indentation style from tabs to spaces to match existing code.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:32:49.877Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJDE8NKD0G9BGR94RDYJYND\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop PR workflow is now well-established: create PR for pending_review tasks, wait for CI, review comments, merge if clean, then complete task. This iteration demonstrated the full cycle twice (PR #161 merged, PR #162 created).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:34:23.027Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJE2DD8ZNRFCAS86J3QVEBB\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task @01KFJ52W completed smoothly using proper workflow: read real implementation first (src/cli/commands/ralph.ts), understood the protocol format, implemented matching behavior in mock. Reading the production code before implementing the test mock ensured format compatibility.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:45:23.240Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJENJNKYQABQ67HVNHQ7MTP\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review workflow caught missing test coverage - the automated review correctly identified that new mock functionality had zero tests, blocking merge until tests were added. Added 6 comprehensive tests by spawning the mock subprocess and using ACPClient to validate the full JSON-RPC protocol flow. The review requirement to test through the actual mock process (not just unit testing the logic) ensured we validated the complete integration.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:55:51.219Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJENS73FRJ811YBX4TGAD7K\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Successfully executed ralph loop PR review workflow: spawned review subagent → identified MUST-FIX issue (missing tests) → added test coverage → pushed to PR branch → waited for CI → verified all checks pass → merged with --merge flag to preserve trailers. Review agent correctly identified the gap between stated goal (catch format bugs) and reality (no tests exercising the code).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:55:57.924Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJF6NH0EF6DWG9EYGSGQ607\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Implementing validation warnings follows a clear pattern: 1) Add warning type to interface, 2) Add check logic in validation function, 3) Add formatting in display function, 4) Add E2E test. The existing staleness checks provided a good template to follow.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T09:05:11.201Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJF6V40XSX7CDANPJWWY5GA\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR workflow from main branch with unpushed commits: create feature branch, reset main to origin/main, push feature branch. This cleanly separates completed work from main without losing commits.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T09:05:16.928Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJFVX5KC3R69Z10BAJ0FSAX\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Type safety improvements catch bugs at compile-time: Adding typed response methods (respondReadTextFile, respondWriteTextFile) to ACPClient prevents runtime bugs by enforcing correct response structures. The pattern of replacing 'unknown' with SDK types (ReadTextFileRequest, etc.) provides IDE autocomplete and catches errors early. This approach worked well - build caught all type mismatches immediately.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T09:16:47.155Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJFZ1AQ5YT0NRGR3SDPAE8T\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop iteration completed two tasks efficiently: First reviewed and merged PR #164 (validation warning), then picked up next ready task (@01KFJ571 ACP type safety) and completed it with PR #165. The loop workflow (check PRs → merge if ready → pick next task) worked smoothly. Key pattern: Complete one task fully (including PR creation) before loop ends.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T09:18:29.720Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJGQE47HFDMZZEZATGWM73E\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"E2E test pattern for multi-entity search worked well: tested each entity type individually first (inbox, observation, agent, workflow, convention), then attempted combined test. When combined test had issues, individual passing tests proved core functionality works. This approach provides both comprehensive coverage and clear failure isolation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T09:31:49.255Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJHA3H4EEANVVSC0HY4GHQY\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Pattern for adding new validation types: Created separate validation module (validate-skills.ts), integrated into validate command with dedicated flag (--skills), added comprehensive tests in matching test file. This modular approach makes validation extensible without bloating the main validate.ts file.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T09:42:00.996Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFKR87J5A4R0M5JYH1D7GXWH\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Session context commands work smoothly\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T21:02:34.053Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Tested during workflow evaluation session\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-22T21:04:15.970Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFKRBGPJ2C29V6ZD0YH4SBM2\",\n    \"type\": \"idea\",\n    \"content\": \"Add step editing to workflow add command\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T21:04:21.714Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": \"@01KFKRBN\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFKSGWR6SK7A59EVY54X7V34\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Hybrid skill-workflow model works well: skill as entrypoint providing context, workflow for structure and tracking. Reduced reflect skill from 215 to 152 lines while adding progress tracking.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T21:24:46.470Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFKA4RTKVTQ54AQF7Z2NTKDQ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop analysis: 5 parallel subagents (iterations, PR compliance, reflections, commits, review feedback) provided comprehensive audit coverage efficiently. Pattern: split analysis by concern, run in parallel, synthesize results.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T16:56:00.595Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFKA4S7HXXSY0PNQY1ZCKJB9\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Branch deletion without content verification: compared commit messages but didn't diff actual file contents. Should always run git diff <branch>:<file> <main>:<file> before concluding content is merged.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T16:56:01.009Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFM8HP1XACBQW6BK85EBXRNW\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Plan mode + subagent review workflow - Having a Plan agent review the plan before presenting to user caught several issues (exit code semantics, missing AC coverage, CLI signature mismatch) that would have caused rework. Worth replicating for complex specs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T01:47:21.022Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFMFTX4BNF58A29ZC7ZT0ESP\",\n    \"type\": \"idea\",\n    \"content\": \"Test shadow commit fix\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T03:54:43.211Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Test resolution for shadow commit\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-23T03:55:08.924Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFMH5SZGA6WF6TB75825DV6V\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Trait-based approach for cross-cutting concerns - creating @trait-shadow-commit made implicit shadow commit behavior explicit, testable, and documented. Subagent exploration before planning caught 6 additional missing commits beyond initial 4. Spec-first implementation ensures AC annotations in code reference back to spec.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T04:18:09.008Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFMP6TAMDM2Q9CRV1ZSD0PEE\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Plan mode with subagent exploration before spec creation. Using Explore agent to gather context from related projects (kynetic) and Plan agent to review/refine plans caught gaps early.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T05:46:05.012Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFMP73J7CY0QJYHN34BT1J15\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Detailed task notes with code snippets, file paths, and AC mappings. Makes tasks self-contained for automation and future sessions without needing original context.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T05:46:14.472Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFN35C6AHD2DW8N31ZN1F1T7\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"PR merge blocked by unresolved review threads requiring manual UI action. GitHub API doesn't support programmatic resolution of review conversations - they must be clicked 'Resolve conversation' in the UI. The check-unresolved-comments CI workflow blocks merge even when all issues are fixed and acknowledged by the bot.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T09:32:29.258Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Accepted limitation - GitHub requires manual 'Resolve conversation' clicks in UI, documented in AGENTS.md\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T05:18:21.704Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFNAT4N61CEP3GHFQZ328T28\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR merge workflow with review resolution: Successfully merged PR #189 using @pr-review-merge workflow. All CI checks passed (tests, claude-review). Greptile feedback was addressed in code but threads weren't programmatically resolvable - documented in PR comments instead. Workflow enforced systematic review before merge.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T11:46:09.702Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFNKFR78AJY6J1MMY42J1H2M\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Interactive CLI tools block automation loops. Encountered with 'sv add tailwindcss' and 'shadcn-svelte init' - both require user input even with --yes flag. This forces either: (1) finding alternative non-interactive installation methods, (2) manual configuration, or (3) pre-scripted answers via expect/stdin. For automation-friendly workflows, prefer tools with true --yes/--no-interaction flags or configuration files over interactive prompts.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T14:17:46.472Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFP01QSX0DB7EQBWW7S7ZFR0\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Daemon serve tests failing in both main and feature branches with 'Daemon failed to start within 5 seconds'. Manual daemon start works fine, suggesting test environment issue. Path resolution fix committed (7dd2106) but underlying timeout issue remains. May need to increase timeout or add stdio logging for test debugging.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T17:57:18.782Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Obsolete - daemon-serve.test.ts was refactored into multiple smaller test files (daemon-server.test.ts, daemon-api-*.test.ts, etc.)\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T05:18:24.199Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFP9AJAJKHTZ005GYT1E017V\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel subagent research for planning - Launching multiple explore agents simultaneously (one for best practices research, one for existing codebase patterns) provided comprehensive context quickly. Combined with Plan agent review, caught issues early before implementation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T20:39:25.266Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFP9ANG7QFQNWC7WNPEDGRES\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"AC-driven test design - Reading spec file directly and mapping tests to acceptance criteria ensured 100% coverage. Table format (AC | Test) made gaps immediately visible.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T20:39:28.519Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFPH3X3Z8YK2GVVKATAEKVHF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Investigation-first approach for bug fixes - reading task context, exploring code to understand root cause before proposing solutions. Found test failures were separate bug from the actual task issue.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T22:55:35.551Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFPH3ZV73P7FA5V1A4EX5N89\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Documenting findings in task notes before implementing - created clear audit trail of decisions (daemon bundling approach) that future sessions can reference.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T22:55:38.343Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFQ38Z76KSABGCHE44P4662G\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Test fixture ULID creation was error-prone - manually crafted ULIDs had wrong length or invalid Crockford chars. testUlid() helper exists but isn't mentioned in fixture documentation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T04:12:55.911Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Documented testUlid() helper in AGENTS.md Test Fixture Patterns section\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T05:13:26.859Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFQ3ADC1GRARE3BAZZWDS9CF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Detailed task implementation notes made E2E infrastructure setup straightforward - step-by-step guidance with verification checklist reduced ambiguity\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T04:13:43.170Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFQ59D0DBN8A654QA0Q2MG6Y\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"E2E debugging: Playwright error-context.md files with page snapshots are invaluable for understanding what browser actually sees vs what code expects\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T04:48:07.181Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFQ59KETY6PT8FA6YKZT332Q\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Same-origin architecture: daemon serving both web UI and API on single port simplifies CORS, WebSocket setup, and eliminates cross-origin complexity\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T04:48:13.787Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFQ8VZQC8J2VNDVXXWGZAG5N\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Subagent research pattern: Delegating architecture research to a subagent produced comprehensive findings with code examples, references, and concrete recommendations - more efficient than inline research\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T05:50:41.900Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFQ8W7Q3TWT541VNMTYNQ38M\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Capturing scope expansion immediately: When debugging revealed architectural issues beyond task scope, captured to inbox then promoted to proper task with full research context. Prevented context loss.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T05:50:50.083Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFR0M0HQEPB9ZJ80HSF1H4R9\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Iterative question-based design with AskUserQuestion tool - asking one design question at a time during spec work (X-Kspec-Dir header choice, PID location, etc.) kept decisions focused and got clear answers. Better than presenting all options at once.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T12:45:46.424Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFR0MBH2Z9GKP96DPTW9J5HN\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Subagent plan review before spec finalization - having a Plan subagent review the spec plan caught gaps (missing error cases, race conditions, path validation) that would have been harder to fix after writing the spec. Worth making standard practice for architecture specs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T12:45:57.667Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFR0MNJTDJ7SGWN2PWCPY5BA\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Didn't know about existing CLI features - wrote 36 ACs inline in YAML instead of using 'kspec item ac add', ran 29 individual 'task set --automation' instead of using --refs batch mode. Need better CLI feature discovery or habit of checking --help first.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T12:46:07.963Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Learning experience - established pattern of checking --help and using batch operations\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T05:18:26.718Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFRAKC9HG1YD6192H0XJNFBW\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Plan-Review-Revise cycle with subagents: Having a Plan agent design specs, then a second Plan agent review for gaps with full user constraint context, then fixing issues before presenting to user. Caught critical issues like ambiguous subagent spawn trigger.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T15:40:11.442Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFRAKVW1Q6E5FY9PTRFHXGA6\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Incremental question-based requirements via AskUserQuestion: Asking one focused question at a time (task selection order, subagent model, skill invocation, error tracking) kept decisions clear and avoided ambiguity in spec design.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T15:40:27.393Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFRCQHCS2Z9Y0XCKFYKT1K8Z\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Using testUlid() helper for test fixtures prevents silent failures from invalid Crockford base32 chars (L, I, O, U). The helper auto-replaces these with valid chars. PR #210 adds documentation for this pattern.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T16:17:24.889Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFS6AX4BHF071F63S4PTPGMS\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"E2E test creation workflow worked smoothly. Pattern established in project-selector.spec.ts provided clear template for documentary tests. Using test.skip() for pending implementation is effective for capturing expected behavior before UI exists. All 17 tests passed structure validation on first run.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T23:44:53.899Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFS6P9Q1GDVYAXF1E3ZGJTPZ\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Workflow runs accumulate without lifecycle management. 34+ active runs exist with no clear way to complete/cancel old runs. Need: kspec workflow complete/cancel/cleanup commands to manage run lifecycle and prevent stale run accumulation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T23:51:07.233Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFST4YEZ7C3FYCFXAFTGKP09\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Subagent audit pattern: Spawn agent to analyze multiple tasks → get structured findings → act on findings. Effective for task/test audits where parallel exploration needed.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T05:31:10.176Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFST50NYXR9Q7TB9A3JC92F8\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task reframing pattern: Change 'Write tests for X' to 'Implement X (AC-N to AC-M)' with implementation steps, required testIds, and 'No test.skip()' in Definition of Done. Prevents documentary test anti-pattern.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T05:31:12.447Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFST52N598B4EQ4P2F2G2K2M\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Documentary test anti-pattern: Agents write test.skip() tests that pass CI but don't verify anything. Task framing as 'write tests' enables this. Root cause: tests treated as goal rather than validation mechanism.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T05:31:14.469Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFT1Q5Y5RNBFXXCB7DA8RGDF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Subagent delegation for git history recovery: Pattern of spawn agent → search git log -p -S → extract lost content → report structured findings worked well for recovering 12+ lost notes from merge. Effective when content exists in history but was overwritten.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T07:43:27.686Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFT1QE8X64CFNDSJ9ATEEB1Y\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Shadow branch divergence lacks guided resolution. When local and remote kspec-meta diverge significantly (61 vs 362 commits), kspec shadow sync just fails with no guidance. Manual git merge-tree diagnosis and conflict-by-conflict resolution required. @yaml-merge-driver would help but was cancelled.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T07:43:36.221Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTESK40ED91F97SCD76JP6W\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test-first development pattern: Writing comprehensive tests before integration implementation catches edge cases early and provides clear specification. Pattern used in loop-mode-error-handling task: (1) Created test file with 23 tests covering all 9 ACs, (2) Implemented utilities to make tests pass, (3) Integrated into ralph.ts. Benefits: TypeScript compilation errors caught immediately, edge cases identified before integration, tests serve as executable documentation. This approach is especially valuable for complex logic with multiple edge cases (failure tracking, progress detection, escalation thresholds).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T11:31:58.208Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTFWFZ6370BPQ1GMZRVMTN3\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Automation-eligible tasks lack time/scope estimates. All eligible tasks in iteration 4 were large-scope (10+ ACs, 30-60+ min work). Automation loops work best with 10-15 min tasks but selection mechanism doesn't filter by estimated effort. Existing eligibility system addresses complexity/clarity but not time dimension. Result: loops start work that can't complete in single iteration. Suggest: add estimated_effort field (small/medium/large) to tasks, --max-effort flag for automation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T11:51:01.863Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTFWS69M8GSAXS7TJZBKMEA\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task Definition of Done (DoD) not visible during task selection. Task @01KFP84N had DoD requirement 'All E2E tests pass - no skips' in notes but wasn't surfaced during ready task selection. Workflow enforced DoD strictly at completion but constraint wasn't visible upfront. Created situation where task appeared eligible but became non-completable mid-work. DoD criteria are critical constraints that should influence task selection, not just exit validation. Suggest: extract DoD to structured field, show in task list, filter tasks by DoD compatibility.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T11:51:11.305Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTFX1MSXCMTBTYC05WD8NSY\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Partial progress commits valuable in automation loops. Iteration 4 on @01KFP84N: added test IDs to components (fd70b86d) even though DoD required fully enabled tests. Committing partial work provided value: (1) next iteration can continue from checkpoint, (2) incremental progress visible in git history, (3) work not lost if task abandoned. Better than all-or-nothing approach. Pattern: commit meaningful increments even if task incomplete, document remaining work clearly in notes and commit message.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T11:51:19.962Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTFX9SDQQ7ZP5BC7E8SB821\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Comprehensive session-end notes enable clean task handoffs. Final note on @01KFP84N documented: what's done, what remains, estimated effort, specific next steps, blockers, recommendations. This level of detail makes continuing work in next iteration frictionless - no context rebuilding needed. Pattern: when leaving task in_progress, include (1) completed work summary, (2) remaining work list, (3) effort estimate, (4) next concrete steps, (5) blockers/considerations. Especially valuable in automation loops where next iteration may be hours/days later.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T11:51:28.301Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTGC48BJC0A13Q7NW8SVJKX\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"E2E test verification blocked by daemon requirement in automation loops. Pattern encountered in @01KFP84N and @01KFP84S: (1) Adding data-testid attributes to components is automatable, (2) Removing test.skip() is automatable, (3) Verifying tests actually pass requires daemon running + test execution + debugging failures which exceeds single loop iteration scope (est 30-60+ min). This creates a 3-phase workflow where phase 3 blocks automation. Tasks remain in_progress at ~70% completion awaiting human verification. Solutions: daemon auto-start infrastructure, task splitting (separate test ID addition from verification), or DoD adjustment for automation eligibility.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T11:59:34.155Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Addressed by task @01KG5VSF\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-29T21:51:19.232Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTGKVRXEEV5MBV1XH1XQ39T\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Loop iteration 6 encountered systematic blockers: All eligible P2 tasks are web UI E2E tests requiring daemon startup + test verification, exceeding single iteration capacity. Both in-progress tasks (@01KFP84N, @01KFP84S) hit same blocker (daemon requirement) and now at failure count 2. Attempted @01KFMMXF (export command) but ~300-500 line implementation scope also exceeds capacity. Pattern suggests: (1) Web UI E2E tasks incorrectly marked automation:eligible - should be automation:needs_review until daemon automation exists, OR (2) Tasks should be split: 'Add test IDs' (automatable) + 'Verify E2E tests pass' (manual), OR (3) DoD should be relaxed to 'Tests enabled, pending verification'.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T12:03:47.613Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTGRPJXF2K3EW6RRR2WY3WD\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Loop mode failure tracking not queryable: [LOOP-FAIL:N] notes exist but no CLI command to check task failure count. Had to manually grep task notes to determine if @01KFP84N and @01KFP84S hit 3-failure threshold (both at count 2). Needed for automation decision: should loop retry task or escalate to automation:needs_review? Suggest: kspec task get @ref --loop-failures or similar to return failure count.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T12:06:26.141Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTH5GC9955K0HDD6V0MXSGT\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Loop error handling protocol (PR #243) executed correctly in iteration 7: [LOOP-FAIL:N] notes tracked failures per task, failure count visible across iterations, auto-escalation to automation:needs_review triggered at threshold 3. Pattern enables clear visibility into which tasks are struggling in automation and systematic escalation when human intervention needed. Tasks @01KFP84N and @01KFP84S hit 3rd failure (daemon requirement blocker) and were properly escalated.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T12:13:25.769Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTHK60JWKZKH928E6QVZ6TF\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"E2E test tasks hit systematic blocker in automation loops: Cannot run daemon (npm run serve) + E2E tests (npm run test:e2e) within loop constraints. Pattern affects all web UI E2E test tasks. Results in [LOOP-FAIL] notes and automation:needs_review escalation. Encountered on tasks 01KFP84N, 01KFP84S, 01KFP84X in iteration 8. Implementation completes successfully (test IDs + test files), but verification step requires human-driven session with long-running daemon.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T12:20:53.906Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTHKCY5R1K8N136P1HH3Y3J\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Session checkpoint hook blocks exit when in_progress tasks have automation:needs_review status. Hook expects all in_progress tasks to either complete or have handoff notes. However, tasks marked automation:needs_review are intentionally paused for human review. Workaround: manually add comprehensive handoff notes before exit. Pattern suggests automation:needs_review should either auto-add handoff notes or be recognized as valid exit state.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T12:21:00.997Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTHKM3WR00TD31129KQEMAF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task-work-loop workflow provided effective structure for automation. Clear steps (filter eligible → select → verify → start → work → commit → submit → PR → exit) prevented skipped steps. Workflow state tracking enabled clean handoffs. Successfully completed inbox view implementation (01KFP84X) following all steps systematically.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T12:21:08.348Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTJNAK1HV8NJKQCSB767QS5\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Automation loop cannot verify E2E tests that require daemon running. Pattern: Tasks add data-testid attributes and create E2E tests, but verification requires manual session to start daemon (npm run serve -w packages/web-ui) and run tests. Repeated across @01KFP84N (tasks view), @01KFP84S (items view), @01KFP84X (inbox view) in session 01KFTDBQB3Z0PA5Y0GQD8T1RW3. Tasks marked automation:needs_review and stall at ~70-80% complete. Potential solutions: headless daemon fixture for E2E tests, mock API layer, or split tasks (implementation + verification).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T12:39:32.705Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTJNJYX2PHTGXCAG3KA0M7Y\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task-work workflow (@task-work-loop) successfully enforced complete task lifecycle in automation loop: task selection from eligible list, verification before start, implementation with notes during work, DoD validation, commit with trailers, submit to pending_review, PR creation. Session 01KFTDBQB3Z0PA5Y0GQD8T1RW3 iteration 9 completed @01KFP850 (command palette E2E tests) from start to PR without friction. Workflow prevented common mistakes: starting without verification, skipping notes, missing DoD checks.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T12:39:41.277Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTKCK1P5GTM073CM64X5WTM\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task verification pattern: Before starting test-only task (01KFP854 - E2E tests), verified WebSocketManager implementation existed. Read manager.ts to confirm AC coverage (ac-28 to ac-32) before committing to E2E test creation. This prevented wasting iteration on tests for non-existent features. Pattern: For tasks scoped as 'write tests for X', verify X implementation exists first. Especially valuable in automation loops with limited iteration budget.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T12:52:15.031Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTMKWW95BXAHA9TF79XT9MR\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Batching related E2E test tasks into a single PR branch: Completed 3 tasks (@01KFP85D observations panel, @01KFP85G error handling, @01KFP85M navigation) on feature branch feat/observations-panel-e2e-tests. All tasks involved E2E tests and data-testid attributes for web UI. Benefits: (1) Avoided multiple PR context switches and branch overhead, (2) Shared commits across tasks (e.g., error-message testid used by all 3), (3) Coherent scope for review. Pattern works when tasks are tightly related, share common files, and can be reviewed together. Session completed 4 tasks total efficiently using this approach.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T13:13:43.049Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTP0GJKNPDMH60GSPXD95P0\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Automation loop cannot handle daemon-dependent E2E test verification. Pattern: Tasks get to ~80-85% complete (implementation done, test IDs added, tests enabled) but then block on daemon startup + iterative test debugging. Three tasks hit this in session 01KFTDBQB3Z0PA5Y0GQD8T1RW3 (iteration 14): @01KFP84N, @01KFP84S, @01KFQAGY. Root cause: Daemon requires manual 'npm run serve', E2E failures unpredictable, debugging cycle exceeds single-iteration capacity. Workaround: Mark automation:needs_review and exit loop. Impact: Web UI E2E testing tasks systematically blocked from automation completion. Potential solutions: (1) Automate daemon lifecycle in loop, (2) Split tasks into 'implementation' + 'E2E verification' phases, (3) Add automation:daemon-required tag for better categorization.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T13:38:05.012Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTPN91A5V1A3NBC088WA5QE\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task-work-loop workflow lacks exit condition for 'eligible but unsuitable' scenario. When eligible tasks exist but all exceed single-iteration capacity (e.g., 5 P3 tasks requiring 300-500 lines each), workflow continues to step 4 (start task) with no clean exit path. Had to manually cancel workflow in iteration 16. Exit conditions defined (no eligible tasks, already done, work complete) but not 'all eligible tasks too complex'. Affects ralph when only complex work remains in eligible pool.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T13:49:25.418Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTPNH9WXC0G77CB9JDSM5C8\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task automation eligibility assessment happens too late in workflow. Tasks get marked automation:eligible without scope assessment. Automation loops then waste iterations doing [LOOP-FAIL:1], [LOOP-FAIL:2], [LOOP-FAIL:3] assessments before marking automation:needs_review. Example: task @01KFMMXF assessed in iterations 6, 7, 14 as too complex (~300-500 lines) but stayed in eligible pool causing repeated evaluation. Assessment should occur BEFORE tasks marked eligible, not after automation attempts them. Related to @task-automation-eligibility but focuses on pre-eligibility workflow gap.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T13:49:33.884Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTPYK46Y190SQJC6RTA7HAA\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Automation loop graceful exit: When tasks require daemon/multi-file coordination exceeding loop capacity, system correctly escalated 3 tasks to automation:needs_review with comprehensive handoff notes. Clean exit without attempting incomplete implementations. Session 01KFTDBQB3Z0PA5Y0GQD8T1RW3 iteration 17.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T13:54:30.663Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTPYVEK0ZQTH006HH1H5F1M\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Zero-completion automation sessions: Loop iteration 17 completed with 0 tasks finished, all 3 in_progress tasks escalated to automation:needs_review. Distinct from prior successful Ralph loops. Root cause: Tasks marked automation:eligible but require daemon E2E testing (2 tasks) or multi-file coordinated implementation (1 task). Gap between 'eligible' tag and actual automation feasibility in single iteration. Affects task selection heuristics.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T13:54:39.187Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTQJ62852K34N95AFCKX5SC\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Loop iteration 19 assessment: Correctly identified that all 4 eligible GitHub Pages export tasks (@01KFMMJ4, @01KFMMXK, @01KFMMXR, @01KFMMXW) exceed automation loop capacity. Marked all as automation:needs_review with clear reasoning. Tasks form a coordinated feature set requiring multi-hour focused implementation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T14:05:12.649Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTR8FDCNMBT7P0VNN8SDBSW\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Repetitive checkpoint notes across automation loops: Tasks stuck in automation:needs_review state get identical checkpoint notes added every iteration. Example: @01KFP84N received 36 notes, with notes 27-36 being nearly identical 'Loop Iteration N - Session End Checkpoint' messages. Creates noise without adding value. Possible solutions: (1) Skip checkpoint notes if last note is recent and task state unchanged, (2) Update most recent checkpoint note instead of appending, (3) Add checkpoint command that manages session-end state separately from progress notes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T14:17:23.116Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTR8ZK3WJV841Y8F7C3KN9P\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Loop iteration 21 efficiently completed pending_review task @01KFP85M in first action by checking task status, validating work was already merged, and immediately completing it. Demonstrates value of prioritizing pending_review tasks over in_progress tasks - they're usually closest to done and just need verification/completion. Pattern: pending_review > in_progress > ready.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T14:17:39.684Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTRRAAF4852S6F5H249P78G\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Automation loop iterations consumed even when zero eligible tasks exist. Pattern observed in iteration 23: loop checked 3 in_progress tasks (all automation:needs_review), found 0 eligible ready tasks, added checkpoint notes, then exited. No actual work possible but iteration budget still used for status quo documentation. Systemic issue - will recur whenever queue is fully blocked on manual work. Potential improvement: early exit detection before iteration starts, or iteration budget exemption for no-op sessions.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T14:26:02.191Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Resolved by @01KFV6CZ (PR #247). Ralph loop now filters both ready AND in_progress tasks by automation:eligible. Session 28 demonstrates clean exit when no eligible tasks remain - zero redundant iterations.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-26T01:13:03.331Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTRY6ASB4AHM7D0ZTP2HX68\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Loop mode runs redundant iterations when no progress possible. Iterations 22-24 added identical checkpoint notes with no state changes. All 3 in_progress tasks marked automation:needs_review, no eligible tasks available, but loop continued for 3 iterations adding duplicate 'no progress possible' notes. Suggest: early exit condition 'if no state change in last N iterations AND no eligible tasks, exit immediately' to avoid redundant work.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T14:29:14.713Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Resolved by @01KFV6CZ (PR #247). Exit condition now checks automation eligibility for both ready and in_progress tasks. Session 28 exited immediately when finding no eligible work.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-26T01:13:09.905Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTSQQSAEJ0HXNEQJ209YCRZ\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Workflow system lacks early exit mechanism. When workflow determines no work is possible (e.g., no eligible tasks), must still step through all remaining workflow steps providing skip reasons. Attempted 'kspec workflow complete @ref' which does not exist. Would benefit from 'workflow exit' or 'workflow skip-remaining' command to cleanly terminate when continuation is impossible.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T14:43:11.786Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTSR2MBYJQ6GAS3Y8Z4DBV4\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Automation loop adds repetitive status notes to stalled tasks. After 27 iterations of ralph automation, same 3 in-progress tasks (@01KFP84N, @01KFP84S, @01KFQAGY) accumulated 27+ nearly-identical notes documenting 'Loop Iteration N - No Eligible Tasks'. While notes provide audit trail, they create significant noise obscuring substantive progress notes. Consider: batch note update mechanism, dedicated status/stall-reason field, or suppress iteration notes when status unchanged.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T14:43:22.891Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTSWYG75X3E38BWWRK8HBWQ\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop ran 28 iterations with identical outcome (no eligible tasks, same 3 tasks documented each time). After 2-3 consecutive iterations returning no eligible tasks, the loop should recognize the pattern and exit early. Current behavior wastes API calls and adds redundant notes. Need early termination logic: if last N iterations (N=2 or 3) all exited with 'no eligible tasks' and same task set, stop the loop.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T14:46:02.504Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTTA3TFQ6MBC3CZ2Z1V740J\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Structured loop iteration note template pattern: Used consistently across 30 automation iterations to document why progress wasn't possible. Template format: '## Loop Iteration N - [Status]' followed by Exit Reason, Task Status (with ✅/❌ checkboxes for completed/incomplete work), specific blockers, and clear next actions. Creates audit trail showing automation decision-making and prevents false 'why is nothing happening' concerns. Makes it obvious when automation is correctly identifying blockers vs stuck in broken logic.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T14:53:13.935Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVPXSZXJE3FNK50A1M0MYN8\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"E2E tests in packages/web-ui timeout after 2+ minutes with no progress indication or diagnostic output. Makes debugging test failures extremely difficult - cannot iterate rapidly. Tests may be waiting on daemon startup that never completes, or Playwright fixtures have configuration issues. Blocked work on @01KFP84N and @01KFP84S in loop iteration 2.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T23:13:19.358Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Addressed by task @01KG5VSF\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-29T21:51:17.744Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVPY36ARRRWYKQZTRXC8CAX\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Loop mode task verification gap: Multiple iterations accepted task notes claiming 'already implemented' or 'tests exist' without independent verification (running tests, checking code). Iteration 1 concluded UI was incomplete based on test failures; iteration 2 found UI components actually exist with proper test IDs. Real issue was E2E infrastructure, not missing implementation. Task notes are context, not proof of completion.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T23:13:28.778Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVPYB4RSBEGW5GF5Z7W1WY8\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Reading actual source code to verify task claims proved more reliable than trusting notes. When @01KFP84N notes said 'UI incomplete', reading TaskList.svelte revealed all required test IDs were present. Verification approach: Read components -> check test IDs -> run tests (if possible) -> only then accept completion claims. This prevented false conclusions about missing implementation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T23:13:36.921Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVQKD22NWCRJFJWRBKPNDR0\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"E2E tests via Playwright for daemon API endpoints: Using packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/*.spec.ts for real HTTP integration tests (not vitest mocks) aligns with project architecture documented in AGENTS.md. This session: created api-projects.spec.ts with 5 passing tests making real fetch() calls to running daemon. Pattern: Start daemon via test fixture, make HTTP requests, verify responses. More reliable than mocking and tests actual behavior.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T23:25:07.010Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVQKFHX5SX08ZQZDX25MKJS\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task DoD conflict with project conventions: Task @01KFQAF9 DoD said 'write real HTTP tests' and 'no documentary/stub tests remain' but AGENTS.md documents that daemon API routes use documentary tests (static analysis). Had to resolve conflict by checking existing patterns in daemon-api-*.test.ts files. Resolution: Created E2E tests in packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/ and updated documentary test to reference them. Friction point: When DoD contradicts documented patterns, unclear which is authoritative.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T23:25:09.566Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVQYR778DPEYXP93M0JKW0V\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Loop mode error handling AC-5 not working: Tasks @01KFP84N, @01KFP84S, @01KFQAGY all have [LOOP-FAIL:3] notes but remain automation:eligible instead of being auto-escalated to automation:needs_review as specified in @loop-mode-error-handling AC-5. Implementation in PR #243 claims to handle this but actual behavior shows automation status not being updated after 3 failures. Verified in session 01KFVN3DDTKEQF1DAF8V3KV48V iteration 4.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T23:31:18.887Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVRK63DF261C4ZNK9NWQJJX\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Loop iteration 5: Accountability in action - instead of immediately marking tasks as needs_review, actually debugged E2E infrastructure issues. Fixed real problems (Vite proxy configuration, API client URL handling) that were blocking all E2E tests. Committed working code (c24fd694) that moves the project forward. Loop failures should document genuine investigation and progress, not just 'this is hard, skipping.'\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T23:42:28.461Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVSBZ9AKZY33E0SAYB9KJEK\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"E2E test infrastructure debugging pattern: When E2E tests fail, work backward through the stack systematically. Session 01KFVN3D example: test timeout → Vite proxy missing → API client hardcoded URLs → daemon fixture loading issue. At each layer, verify the fix (tests connect successfully) before moving to next layer. This methodical approach identified root cause (daemon ContextManager path handling) after fixing intermediate issues (Vite proxy + relative URLs in commit c24fd694).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T23:56:00.682Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVSKKCZVQ2K2BRJMT0A86WP\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Loop mode automation tag disconnect: Across 8 consecutive loop iterations, task notes documented 'marked automation:needs_review' but the actual command 'kspec task set @ref --automation needs_review' was never executed. This suggests a pattern in autonomous loops where intent is documented in notes but the corresponding state change command is not run. Root cause: loop documenting WHAT should happen without executing HOW to make it happen.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T00:00:10.655Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVTBAYZ7S0403M97E2XG31T\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop iteration without progress: Loop ran 12 consecutive iterations with zero code changes or git commits. All iterations exited with 'no automation-eligible tasks' message. Tasks remained in_progress state throughout despite being marked automation:needs_review. Each iteration added near-identical checkpoint notes documenting 'no work attempted'. Pattern indicates need for circuit breaker that detects repeated no-progress iterations and either auto-escalates tasks or stops the loop. Related to @01KF554T circuit breaker concept but captures actual observed behavior rather than theoretical design.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T00:13:08.448Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVTBKBKDNJ0HJ6VMJ9AXQMH\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Session checkpoint hook enforcement prevented task abandonment: Stop hook detected 3 in_progress tasks without recent meaningful progress and blocked session exit until checkpoint notes were added. All tasks received documentation of current state, blockers, and next steps. This pattern ensures tasks don't silently stall - they either get documented or completed. Hook runs automatically on session end with no manual intervention needed. Particularly valuable for automation loops where task state must be explicit for next iteration.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T00:13:17.043Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVTYSJECRND016ZATZ25N3A\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop continues iterating when all active tasks are automation:needs_review. Observed across 15 consecutive iterations: each iteration runs 'kspec tasks ready --eligible', finds 0 tasks, then adds repetitive status notes to all escalated tasks. Exit condition correctly identifies no eligible work but doesn't trigger early exit before status documentation. Result: unnecessary API calls, note bloat (45+ notes across 3 tasks), slower session completion. Ideal: exit immediately when no eligible tasks remain without adding iteration notes to needs_review tasks.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T00:23:45.998Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Resolved by @01KFV6CZ (PR #247). Ralph loop now correctly exits when all in_progress tasks are automation:needs_review. Verified in session 28.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-26T01:13:16.392Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVTYW9TT5NNV7JNR0PHRM0R\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task escalation with comprehensive rationale prevents false automation work. Pattern observed: when tasks blocked or require human decisions, automation loop adds multi-paragraph notes documenting: (1) WHAT blocks the work, (2) WHY it's not automatable, (3) WHAT human needs to do next. Tags task automation:needs_review. Result: zero false work attempts across 15 iterations, clear handoff context for human sessions. Quality over speed: better to escalate with context than attempt inappropriate work.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T00:23:48.795Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVVATF0YA11E7EB88TAHP3X\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph automation loop ran 10+ iterations (7-17) with zero implementation work after all tasks marked needs_review. Loop exit logic only checks task existence, not progress stagnation. Should detect: N consecutive iterations with no file changes, commits, or task status transitions → early exit with diagnostic.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T00:30:20.128Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVVB2KHS3P06SR1X42DFW7Q\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Session checkpoint notes (iterations 7-17) consistently documented: task state, what's complete, what's blocked, required resolution steps, investigation files, automation status. This pattern provides excellent continuity for next session and clear audit trail of escalation reasoning.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T00:30:28.466Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVVBBE6ED70C0ZKXW32Q97Z\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Daemon fixture loading blocker affected 2/3 tasks across 10 iterations with no alternative approach attempted. Pattern: E2E test harness starts daemon with --kspec-dir pointing to temp fixtures, daemon returns empty data instead of YAML content. Should have tried: run daemon manually with debug output, inspect ContextManager code paths, create minimal reproduction case, or escalate infrastructure debugging to separate focused task.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T00:30:37.511Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Promoted to task @01KG5VSF\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-29T21:51:11.063Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": \"@01KG5VSF\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVVHGHH2Q71ECC19CF59E4E\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Loop mode escalation discipline working as designed: Session 01KFVN3D ran 18 iterations with 3 in_progress tasks. All tasks marked automation:needs_review in iterations 7-8 after assessment. Loop correctly exited when kspec tasks ready --eligible returned empty array. No thrashing, no shortcuts attempted, no improper completion claims. Tasks stayed in_progress with comprehensive checkpoint notes providing human handoff context. This validates the automation system recognizing its limits and delegating complex/blocked work appropriately.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T00:33:59.346Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVXSQF1YH0J7X5HPQHJDR8D\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop exit condition working correctly: Session 28 demonstrated clean exit behavior after @01KFV6CZ fix. Loop checked 'kspec tasks ready --eligible', found empty array (all 3 in_progress tasks were automation:needs_review), and exited immediately with zero redundant iterations. This resolves the overnight session issue where loops ran 30+ iterations with no progress. Exit condition now filters both ready AND in_progress tasks by automation:eligible status.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T01:13:25.730Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFXTADHRF0ZBX4E0HR7H11AS\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Tasks created via 'kspec derive' have auto-generated notes that just copy spec content. For standalone tasks, needed to manually add structured sections: Background (why this matters), Reproduction steps, Concrete examples, Open design questions. This structure makes tasks actionable without conversation context.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T18:51:07.192Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFXTAKKXZ27TMK4SA7TQMAFG\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Subagent plan review caught CLI command syntax issues (missing --as and --id flags) before execution. Using a reviewer subagent after writing a plan prevents wasted iterations.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T18:51:13.405Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFXVK5QBFCN3A3BTXME0G86C\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"dist/daemon/ can become stale without warning - packages/daemon/src changes aren't reflected until root 'npm run build' is run. E2E tests can pass web-ui build but fail because daemon code is outdated. Wasted debugging time on what appeared to be runtime error but was actually stale build.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T19:13:22.667Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Fixed in PR #276 - added daemon staleness detection that warns when dist/daemon is older than source\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T02:03:06.384Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFXVKJJE3JWG67VFYNM64ZC8\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Comparing dist/ vs source when debugging daemon issues - immediately revealed the stale build problem when runtime debugging was going in circles\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T19:13:35.823Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFYAH1CQ6FP9V5MJ4MMB33AW\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Debug element technique for Svelte reactivity: Adding conditional debug elements like `{#if state}<div data-testid=\\\"debug-...\\\">{state}</div>{/if}` quickly verifies whether state is actually true at runtime vs expected. Useful for diagnosing reactivity issues where console logs show updates but UI doesn't reflect them.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T23:34:21.335Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFYAH9ABXKZNRAWVN8G751YF\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"bits-ui Sheet/Dialog Portal reactivity broken in Svelte 5: Props passed to child components through bits-ui Portal don't update reactively. PresenceManager.shouldRender returns false even when open=true. Workaround: use native elements or custom components instead of bits-ui Dialog for Svelte 5 projects. See task @01KFP84N notes for full investigation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T23:34:29.452Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Resolved by using $state object pattern + flushSync. See @01KFZ708 and /svelte-5 skill for documentation.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-27T07:52:07.714Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFZ3YG03R29D6MYRHFT5WV5S\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task notes from loop mode sessions can become noisy/unreliable, requiring manual cleanup or user warning to ignore recent notes. Example: @01KFP84N had 26 noise notes removed and user warned remaining notes might be incorrect.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-27T06:58:36.675Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFZ3YNHQWZFZ6MMWBR81H6Y6\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Using Explore subagent for deep analysis before making changes provided comprehensive understanding (file locations, line numbers, root cause, impact analysis) that enabled confident parallel fixes via multiple subagents.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-27T06:58:42.360Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFZ708S00S4EA95C1A57HHD2\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Svelte 5 reactivity solution: Use $state object pattern + flushSync() for reactive conditional rendering. Separate $state variables may not trigger {#if} block re-renders; wrapping state in object (panel = $state({ open: false, task: null })) and using flushSync(() => { panel.open = true }) ensures synchronous DOM updates. Also documented in /svelte-5 skill. Resolves friction @01KFYAH9.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-27T07:52:00.544Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG031N6WQM6BM3S0J2YFEF0H\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"bits-ui Select onValueChange in Svelte 5 returns array of characters plus new value (e.g., ['a','l','l','in_progress'] instead of 'in_progress'). Workaround: extract last element from array when Array.isArray(value).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-27T16:02:06.172Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Incorrect diagnosis - bits-ui Select works correctly; issue was likely misuse of spread operator or other code error\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T05:14:58.910Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG031Y246EC054DSQ2CEX9SF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Console log capture in E2E tests revealed exact bits-ui callback values, making the array quirk immediately visible. Adding console.log to component handlers during debugging is highly effective for understanding Svelte 5 reactivity issues.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-27T16:02:15.236Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG0J4H7FFW05RZP39YDBM2YF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Reading reference tests (tasks.spec.ts) before writing new tests - understanding existing patterns informed structure and avoided reinventing conventions\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-27T20:25:49.040Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG0J4XRDKQ7Z6Y7FBP2TX1K8\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Documenting blocking issues with specific symptoms, likely causes ranked by probability, and debug commands - makes next session pickup much faster\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-27T20:26:01.869Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG0N4V90NDXX0MVSYXWWTN2M\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Schema validation (safeParse) failures in extractItemsFromRaw are silent - items just don't appear in results with no error or warning. This caused significant debugging time when trait had invalid enum values and module had nested items in traits field. Consider adding validation error logging or a strict mode that throws on parse failures.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-27T21:18:25.056Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG0ZHY1QR402HYBSWCMZJ9Z5\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Dedicated E2E fixtures pattern - creating packages/web-ui/tests/fixtures/ separate from shared tests/fixtures/ cleanly isolates E2E test data from unit tests, preventing cross-contamination\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-28T00:20:19.639Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG17R6Y5MEF5DPZ1Z73YFJEW\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Using /e2e skill patterns immediately caught ULID validation issue (Crockford base32 excludes I, L, O, U). Invalid ULIDs in fixtures fail silently - the skill's warning helped debug quickly.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-28T02:43:33.957Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG17RDSGDZB9X9XTRXN4458K\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Session context is loaded from .kspec-session file (not kynetic.meta.yaml). This caused debugging time when E2E tests couldn't find session focus. The API (fetchSessionContext) and file location should be documented in /e2e skill or AGENTS.md.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-28T02:43:40.977Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG17RKW385KB2RXRV8KCAVWV\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"TaskSummary interface was missing depends_on field, needed for dashboard to compute blocked task count. Had to add to shared types + daemon routes. API contracts should include all fields needed for common UI computations.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-28T02:43:47.203Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Fixed - depends_on field added to TaskSummary interface and daemon routes\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T05:13:39.126Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG1GNQJZRR2F3TH526VHVA3A\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"E2E skill has incorrect selector guidance for bits-ui Select: recommends getByRole('option') but bits-ui uses data-slot attributes. Correct pattern: await dropdownContent.locator('[data-slot=\\\"select-content\\\"]'); then dropdownContent.locator('[data-slot=\\\"select-item\\\"]').filter({ hasText: 'value' }).click(). Update e2e/SKILL.md line 15 and lines 162-164.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-28T05:19:29.888Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Fixed in PR #256 - updated E2E skill with correct bits-ui Select selector pattern\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-28T05:24:34.861Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG2FM29NVPRY5BF8DW52FQ00\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"isStaticMode() guard pattern worked well for conditionally disabling features without major refactoring - single check at API layer propagates through entire app\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-28T14:20:21.173Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG4M2HRF76XZRXKVAMDZFDP2\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Investigation-first debugging: When tests pass but docs say they shouldn't, investigate WHY before closing. In this session, discovered skill documentation was outdated rather than tests being wrong - prevented false task closure and led to fixing actual issue (stale docs).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-29T10:16:38.927Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG4M2R8569QYJMCB8GJ6XR9C\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Throwaway inspection tests: Writing quick, disposable tests to inspect actual DOM/state is effective debugging. DOM inspection test revealed bits-ui elements have both role='option' AND data-slot attributes - concrete evidence in minutes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-29T10:16:45.573Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG4M2YJ6TSAQ52TWWK1F2337\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Skill documentation can become stale without detection: /e2e skill claimed getByRole('option') doesn't work with bits-ui when it actually does (bits-ui added proper ARIA roles). No mechanism flags skill docs as potentially outdated when dependencies change. Task @01KG1H91 was created based on incorrect assumption from stale docs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-29T10:16:52.039Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG5SGK089902EVXG1FPKPX0S\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Explore+Plan parallel subagent pattern for implementation tasks: Before implementing a task with existing spec/notes, launch two subagents in parallel - (1) Explore agent to gather codebase context (file locations, interfaces, test patterns) and (2) Plan agent to design the implementation approach. Both complete before coding begins, providing thorough context AND a concrete plan. Used successfully for ref normalization task - all tests passed first try.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-29T21:10:56.264Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG64RZ0E5YPAMRYH81851MJA\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"CLI --force flag pattern works well for agent/script use. inbox delete --force skips confirmation. Same pattern could apply to other commands needing non-interactive mode.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-30T00:27:45.039Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG6WJZFBGPPPMSNQ2H5C8Q8E\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Observation triage session efficiently resolved 12 friction observations by: (1) batch retrieving all observations, (2) cross-referencing AGENTS.md documentation, (3) categorizing into resolvable/keep-open/historical before acting, (4) verifying obsolete items (like deleted test files) before resolution\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-30T07:23:54.731Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG7A7ZSDZCK6RD639Q7Q02AS\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Test1\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:22:34.669Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Batch test\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:22:46.874Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG7A84F9WX9KXDKSQKJ6X3MX\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Test2\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:22:39.465Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Batch test\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:22:46.980Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG7A867AR8FGM6WE8EXM64QT\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Test3\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:22:41.259Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Batch test\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:22:47.048Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG7A8T9GCNWNEF22DX5P6Z15\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Debug1\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:23:01.808Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Test\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:23:08.702Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG7A8W996JYVJ9BGNHBRAZC3\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Debug2\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:23:03.849Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Test\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:23:08.817Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG7ACHTW9P6R0G5GD49WP4DY\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Batch1\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:25:04.220Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Test\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:25:12.344Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG7ACKM3GYQPQ6RHY81BXW72\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Batch2\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:25:06.051Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Test\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:25:12.456Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG7AD09XV1EJFAN1DSW4XS4F\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"ShellA\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:25:19.037Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"ShellTest\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:25:26.717Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG7AD2AXC4ZZBNMZW62K516P\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"ShellB\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:25:21.117Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"ShellTest\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:25:26.831Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG7ARFWPEDQZE6FH3A9RYZ1A\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test pattern: when creating multiple items in quick succession for batch operation tests, use JSON mode to capture full ULIDs instead of parsing 8-char prefixes from human output. ULID prefixes can collide when items are created within the same millisecond, causing test deduplication to produce unexpected results. Full ULIDs are always unique.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:31:35.447Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG8PFDENWCZK15W036ZB8CX9\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Following existing patterns (task-limit marker) made implementing new feature (end-iteration) straightforward. Same file paths, detection mechanism, and cleanup lifecycle.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-31T00:15:35.381Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG8RAYQJPYB4KBVHQMMGKXPV\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Review feedback loop (Greptile + Claude) caught real bugs: async race condition in signal handler and no-op test. Worth keeping mandatory.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-31T00:48:06.387Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG8RB42RY7YS3283JZJ40EGS\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"User edge-case questions ('what about Ctrl+C?', 'does it work on Windows?') led to better implementation. Don't rush to close - invite scrutiny.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-31T00:48:11.864Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG95K29ERJ12XFDWW44P0MPF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"kspec search command exists and works well - found it during reflection when checking coverage. Searched 'multi-ref' and got comprehensive results across specs, tasks, inbox. Should use this more proactively during work.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-31T04:39:43.662Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGG9KZQ5XXJ44RMQ0MW52RBF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Multi-codebase exploration via parallel subagents: Spawning 4-6 explore/research agents simultaneously to analyze kspec and kynetic-bot for gap analysis, architecture comparison, and Rust migration planning was highly effective. Each agent focused on one domain (CLI stack, bot ecosystem, ACP, context mgmt, migration strategy) and the results synthesized into comprehensive documentation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-02T23:04:49.125Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGG9M76B5N03Z660P2B7NVH3\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"kspec bootstraps greenfield projects well: Initialized kynamo (Rust rewrite project) with kspec to track its own development. Shadow branch, spec items for 6 implementation phases, and inbox items all created smoothly. Demonstrates kspec's value beyond self-hosting - can bootstrap any new project with structured planning.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-02T23:04:56.779Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGK93JZGTRSRBEB2NHW6ERBF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task notes with root cause analysis and specific file list made implementation straightforward - this pattern should be replicated when creating reflection-based tasks\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-04T02:53:35.088Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGKVNV4ZXHE1AYD8ZWA11HRF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Spawning a Plan agent to review completed spec/task work against the original plan catches gaps (like missing traits) that the primary agent overlooked. Useful pattern for quality assurance on spec creation work.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-04T08:18:07.647Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGKYG2XXQ4GG2X6S87CP4HJM\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Bulk AC add missing: Adding 33 ACs required 33 individual kspec item ac add commands. Would benefit from kspec item ac add-batch @ref --file acs.yaml or stdin JSON support.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-04T09:07:24.733Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Batch command system exists (PRs #321/#322). Friction is documentation, not capability.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-02-06T10:34:37.210Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGKYGDYSYSF0WC2KEJN5P66S\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Parent relationship not persisted: item add with under flag creates items but parent field is null. Also spec says parent flag but CLI requires under flag.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-04T09:07:36.025Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGKYGFQX8G25Q2ZACE340CHD\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Spec split for automation eligibility: Splitting a large spec into focused child specs made task-to-AC mapping clear and enabled granular automation eligibility assessment.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-04T09:07:37.854Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGM07N5F047VJTWK2R3QJZW4\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Test reference ambiguity with @01 prefix - When writing integration tests that create plans/tasks, using generic references like @01 fails when test fixtures already contain items with ULIDs starting with 01. Must use explicit slugs (--slug test-plan-1) for test isolation. Affected cli-plan.test.ts and task-plan-ref.test.ts - all references needed slugs added.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-04T09:37:45.647Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGM07QTQKAAQTMWERMMZHJ65\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Schema-first implementation pattern - Defining schemas (Plan, PlansFile) first, then parser functions (loadPlans, findPlanByRef), then CLI commands (plan add/get/set) created clean separation. Each layer had focused tests. Pattern worked well for both plan CLI (23 tests) and plan_ref field (8 tests).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-04T09:37:48.375Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGM07T7QV2VV9Z6PY0TJEBHX\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Validation ordering for better errors - When validating references, check type mismatch (isTask/isSpecItem) before checking existence. Gives 'Reference X is not a plan' instead of 'Plan reference not found' when user passes wrong type. Applied in task add and task set --plan-ref validation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-04T09:37:50.839Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGM1RX4NR7ADX19G2FTPF0S2\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Pattern-following implementation: When implementing new CLI commands, examining similar existing commands (e.g., derive.ts for task creation patterns, plan.ts for command structure) and reusing their patterns leads to consistent, correct implementations. This approach worked well for plan derive - imports, error handling, slug generation, and bidirectional updates all followed established patterns, resulting in clean first implementation with no structural issues.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-04T10:04:39.445Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGMX3K0D0104A8JD0NWRP526\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test-driven regex debugging proved effective: wrote comprehensive tests for plan document parser's markdown section extraction (## Specs, ## Tasks, ## Implementation Notes), which immediately caught regex pattern bugs (^## anchors failed to match). Fixed patterns before integration, avoiding late-stage debugging. Pattern: write tests first for parsing/extraction logic, especially when dealing with complex patterns or unfamiliar APIs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-04T18:02:21.069Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGP14AGQRQ3QZFEHGY66T89J\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Test fixtures use @test-core module but many example commands in docs/tests assume @cli exists. Caused global find/replace in tests when module reference didn't match. Consider: (1) standardizing fixture module names to match common examples, (2) documenting fixture module structure in test helpers, or (3) adding @cli as an alias/additional module in fixtures.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T04:31:53.879Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGP14D6DF0APPMFXGEZ8EJS6\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Using createdSpecsMap to track specs during import solved parent reference resolution elegantly. Specs created in topological order could reference earlier-created specs by slug lookup in the map, working in both dry-run and real modes. Pattern: track created entities in a map keyed by slug for multi-step operations with interdependencies.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T04:31:56.621Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGP14G3BD89YS91J02VH3M01\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Acceptance criteria schema requires 'id' field but this isn't obvious when writing test plans or spec YAML. Parser validation fails silently - spec just doesn't appear in parsed output. Better error would be: 'AC missing required field: id' at parse time. Or make id optional and auto-generate if missing.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T04:31:59.595Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGP16HK67C30T8A8KMYGDFCR\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"kspec validate output is noisy with pre-existing reference errors and alignment warnings (22 ref errors, 152 alignment warnings). Makes it hard to verify whether a specific change introduced new issues. A --diff or --new-only flag that shows only issues not present in the previous commit would help.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T04:33:06.662Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGP16KZRYRE4Z921QG9WE8MC\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Plan with exact file paths, line numbers, and 'nature of change' descriptions translates directly to precise edits. The plan for ralph loop fixes had a table mapping files to changes — each row became one Edit tool call with no ambiguity.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T04:33:09.112Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGP40S7D4KXBDQ38542G9ZH7\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Vitest replaces console.log with its own implementation that doesn't flow through process.stdout.write. Tests that capture stdout.write won't see console.log output. When testing code that wraps both console.log and stdout.write, spy on console.log directly (vi.spyOn) and test stdout.write capture separately.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T05:22:23.597Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGP40YN2T598YCSXZWJWWG5T\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Tracing output flow (console.log → stdout.write chain) quickly revealed the doubled prefix bug. When debugging output duplication, mapping the full write path through all wrappers/interceptors identifies where multiple layers add the same content.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T05:22:29.154Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGP3JBQP3XWSQSW83VS8YZB4\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Commander.js optional argument pattern: When a command has an optional argument like .command('help [topic]'), the action handler signature must use (topic: string | undefined, options) NOT (topic?: string, options?). The optional TypeScript syntax breaks Commander's argument passing - options becomes an empty object. Pattern seen in task.ts commands works correctly.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T05:14:31.030Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGP3JJEWMA65YMH03YMY9XKP\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test-first implementation with AC annotations: Writing tests with AC annotations (// AC: @spec-ref ac-N) before implementation ensures complete coverage and creates clear traceability. Pattern used in help.test.ts covered all 5 ACs systematically and caught the --json flag issue early.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T05:14:37.916Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGPHG6D6WFE5AYE4V49AKBE8\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Review agent (opus subagent) caught a real validation bug - missing required 'id' field in plan document AC example. The schema check against actual parser code was the key insight. Always verify examples against actual schema definitions.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T09:18:00.102Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGPHG81NE1BNP4RX9Y7Z6YM8\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Committed directly to main forgetting branch protection requires PRs. Had to create branch after the fact and reset. Should always create feature branch first in this repo.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T09:18:01.781Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGQVA9RFHA4J4BEN5EAAMRJJ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Subagent delegation pattern: using Explore agent for codebase survey + general-purpose agent for PR review kept main context clean and session efficient during daemon strict-mode fix\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T21:28:47.119Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGQY6YCTSAKEY4FKBJTVHXEZ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Workflow run mining before prune: /reflect captured 99.4% of run content into durable artifacts. Out of 181 runs with ~100 meaningful notes, only 1 contained unique info not already tracked. Validates reflection-based knowledge capture approach.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T22:19:22.907Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGQY7097397E46Q8T1WZADDF\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"task-work-loop has 69% abort rate (11/16 runs) — almost entirely because no eligible tasks existed when started. Workflow works fine when work exists (5/5 completed all 9 steps). Root cause: ralph orchestrator starts workflow without pre-checking kspec tasks ready --eligible.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T22:19:24.839Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGQY72Q4C5V3GNRWKCJGY2MZ\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"session-reflect-loop runs too aggressively in ralph loops — 72 runs (40% of all runs), chains of up to 31 consecutive executions, vast majority capture zero new items. 113 min spent (19% of total workflow time) with questionable marginal value in consecutive chains. Should be conditional on whether preceding task-work-loop actually completed work.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T22:19:27.333Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGQY75ANKENZMWPXRNYWJYYP\",\n    \"type\": \"idea\",\n    \"content\": \"Workflow run telemetry: Before pruning old runs, mine them for aggregate stats (abort rates, durations, sequencing patterns). Consider keeping aggregate statistics even when pruning individual records to enable trend analysis. First mining found: 9.9 hrs total, PR review 36%, reflect 46%, task-work-loop 6.5%.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T22:19:30.006Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGQY77CSM15MQWKTJS05N14P\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"pr-review-merge consumes 36% of all workflow time (215 of 594 min). Step 1 (CI check) bimodal: 30 runs under 30s but 9 over 5 min. No fast-path for trivial PRs that pass all gates immediately. Consecutive chains of up to 14 suggest batch PR processing needs a dedicated workflow.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T22:19:32.121Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGQYECS40M7NHKZKJPKKEK9Y\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel subagent mining pattern: spawning 3 specialized agents (notes, patterns, gaps) to analyze the same dataset from different angles. Each found complementary insights the others missed. Effective for pre-prune data extraction.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T22:23:27.012Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGR0NMTJDKB72NAP0YEENDF3\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Subagent-driven holistic review for spec-plan design: Launching a general-purpose subagent with structured review criteria (completeness, consistency, spec coverage, edge cases) caught 2 blockers and 7 should-fix items before plan import. Pattern: write plan doc, then have subagent review against existing codebase patterns before committing.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T23:02:21.778Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGR0NPZC3QHBRCAQBQX7KV92\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Plan import drops ACs and writes malformed trait refs: Two bugs in kspec plan import discovered during batch-exec plan import. (1) ACs from Specs YAML block not written to created items. (2) Trait refs written without @ prefix causing schema errors. Both required manual workarounds. Tasks created: @01KGR0K2, @01KGR0K5.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T23:02:23.980Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Both bugs fixed in PR #319: createSpecItem() now preserves acceptance_criteria, and trait refs are normalized with @ prefix during import.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-02-06T00:25:02.261Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGR5CVAAHCBBX27FD0ZN3SVQ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Precise plan with exact file paths, line numbers, and code diffs made the plan-import bug fix session trivially fast. Plan → implement → test → PR → merge in one smooth pass with zero rework.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T00:24:56.394Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGRP6D35N9WE3EKT2KBEBC5W\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Plan-import scoped notes fix: well-scoped plan with specific line numbers and code changes led to zero-iteration implementation (all tests passed first try). Good pattern for future fix plans.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T05:18:31.013Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGS4Y7YZCP10F4FR6V38DYW5\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"WeakMap<Command, T> annotation pattern works cleanly for adding metadata to Commander commands. Avoids monkey-patching internals, is type-safe and GC-friendly, chains naturally with .command() calls (markMutating(cmd.command(...))), and integrates with extractCommandTree() by reading annotations during traversal. Reusable for future annotation types (e.g. requires-auth, idempotent). See src/cli/command-annotations.ts for reference implementation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T09:36:12.255Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGS89MKMBN56RX8RRGZBB50K\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Subagent-reviewed AC drafts: Pattern of drafting ACs → subagent review → revise → apply caught 5+ real issues (--count+--json interaction, partial success gap, missing optional flag ACs, scope creep in AC-10, missing multi-trait remove symmetry). Prevented rework during implementation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T10:34:51.380Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGTF4QA30P761909YYA8KHVK\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex CLI as external PR reviewer: running 'codex exec -m gpt-5.3-codex --sandbox danger-full-access --full-auto' with a code review prompt caught a real positional-arg-ordering bug that the implementing agent missed. Two independent reviewers (Codex + Claude CI) found complementary issues — Codex caught the arg order bug and temp dir naming, Claude CI caught the validation count mismatch and finally-block safety. Worth making this a standard part of the PR review workflow.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T21:53:44.771Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"01KGTF4Y\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-02-06T22:30:50.992Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGTF4YT5Y2233BHBFZ3S8N75\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex sandbox can't reach api.github.com: when running codex exec with --sandbox danger-full-access, network access to GitHub API was blocked, so the review comment had to be posted manually. This required reading codex output, extracting the review text, and posting via gh ourselves. A wrapper script or skill that handles the 'codex review then post' pattern would eliminate this manual step.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T21:53:52.453Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Addressed by /codex skill (PR #325). Using danger-full-access sandbox gives Codex full network access including GitHub API.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-02-06T22:30:56.697Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGTF57CRAX3CDYVTGBRS5NTV\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Atomic copy-back was a design gap caught by reviewers, not by tests. The plan described 'copy-back' as straightforward fs.cp, but both reviewers independently flagged that delete-then-copy is not safe under I/O failure. Future plans involving filesystem atomicity should explicitly call out failure modes in the design — the happy path isn't enough.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T21:54:01.240Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGTF5E6S42VZ1FWESSMX2QZS\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Plan-driven implementation with spec-first ACs: having 22 acceptance criteria defined before coding made both implementation and testing systematic. Each test was annotated with its AC reference, and the review could verify coverage by checking annotations. The plan→spec→implement→test→review pipeline worked well for this medium-complexity feature.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T21:54:08.217Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGTH928DVA2CEA4FHH93M8MN\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex self-review loop is effective: had Codex review its own skill file, it found 4 MUST-FIX issues (invalid CLI flags, sandbox conflicts, malformed API payloads). Then had Codex review the PR with inline comments — it found 2 more issues (flag ordering, nested fences). Each round of review caught real bugs that would have caused runtime failures.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T22:31:04.206Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGTH995FGYBH7S0Z0FCRJCTC\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex exec review subcommand has different flag parsing than codex exec: -s must go before the review subcommand (codex exec -s danger-full-access review ...) not after (codex exec review -s ... fails). This flag ordering quirk isn't documented in codex --help and caused a runtime failure that required a fix commit.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T22:31:11.280Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGTH9GNRYXV1P230AB1KWJPH\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"GitHub PR review API with --input JSON file works reliably for inline comments. Pattern: write structured JSON to /tmp/codex-pr-review-body.json with {event, body, comments[{path, line, body}]}, then post via gh api repos/{o}/{r}/pulls/{n}/reviews --method POST --input file. Codex figured out the line vs position issue on its own (first attempt used line numbers which mapped to null, then corrected to diff positions).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T22:31:18.968Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGTM42H2M0WPJGE9X7CHS7MX\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex PR review as documentation quality gate: /codex pr caught real arg-name bugs in batch JSON examples that would have caused user failures. The review→fix→push cycle was fast. Worth using on all docs-heavy PRs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T23:20:46.370Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGTNY96A6TMC4J1Y4V786JMM\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex plan review as pre-import quality gate caught trait ref format bug and compound AC issues. Worth making standard practice for plan imports with 3+ specs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T23:52:33.738Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGTNYAQNT0KVK3YTF5E7ZKYD\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel subagent research (two Explore agents) during spec-plan design phase efficiently gathered session infrastructure context in ~60s instead of sequential exploration.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T23:52:35.318Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGVCEFG5NP47A9K33GS192PD\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex PR review on self-authored PRs creates review threads that trigger check-unresolved-comments CI gate. Requires manual GraphQL thread resolution + CI re-run before merging. Codex skill should either skip inline comments on own PRs or auto-resolve threads after posting.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-07T06:25:53.158Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGVCENXDGQ8QVSC7V21SDFQT\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Tracing ACP bugs through the chain (framing.ts → client.ts → spawner.ts → ralph.ts) was efficient because the codebase has clear layering and the override mechanism (methodTimeouts) was already in place. Minimal change (18 lines, 3 files) for the fix.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-07T06:25:59.725Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGVDDPDMPZ9008WHBJHGHZN6\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task @01KGVARW had excellent root cause analysis in its notes (specific file, line numbers, all call sites, exact reproduction). This made the fix trivial — under 10 minutes from start to merged PR. Detailed bug reports with root cause are high-leverage.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-07T06:42:56.052Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGVK9K0AR02A2MJBXWBFE5DH\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Batch triage workflow: categorize inbox by theme first, quick-win deletions, then one-at-a-time promotion with AskUserQuestion showing What/Why/How context. Cross-reference against git log and completed tasks to catch already-done items. This pattern processed 61 items efficiently.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-07T08:25:32.938Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGVK9MH4RRSZT8JZP7E3089F\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Implementation notes at promotion time: adding concrete implementation notes during inbox promote (not after) makes tasks self-contained for future agents. Include: which files to modify, patterns to follow, approximate scope.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-07T08:25:34.500Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGVK9P011GDQGTW9TJRE8FA9\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Automation triage forces context switch to spec creation: when assessing eligibility, discovering a task needs a spec means switching from assessment mode to authoring mode (find module, find parent, create item, add ACs, link task). Consider a guided flow or --create-spec flag on task set --automation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-07T08:25:36.001Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGWG8W1A9ZHHWCKVNVAFQM6B\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex PR review caught silent bug in session log list — tasks_completed metric searched for non-existent event type. Real task completions use session.update tool_call events with rawInput.command containing 'task complete'. Without review, feature would ship reporting 0 tasks for all real sessions.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-07T16:51:58.122Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGWG8YSAFS6GG225AV0AXPHW\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Session event data payloads are untyped — EventTypeSchema defines the type enum but data field is z.unknown(). Had to grep through real JSONL files to discover that Ralph records task completions as session.update events with sessionUpdate: 'tool_call' and rawInput.command. This caused a bug that was only caught by Codex reviewing against real data.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-07T16:52:00.939Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGXHNDY3R4AC24TS1R4Q54CA\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Commander's .option() parse function (e.g. parseInt) silently pre-coerces values before the action handler runs. When replacing inline validation with shared helpers, the helper never sees the raw string. This caused a bug in PR #347 where derive/plan-derive still accepted '3abc' as priority 3. Fix: never use Commander parse functions for options validated by shared helpers.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-08T02:35:32.675Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGXHNR4TWC7Z8V6FB5NR72XF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Using Codex (/codex pr) as an automated second reviewer caught a real bug (Commander parseInt pre-parse bypass) that manual review missed. The review-fix-re-review cycle completed in one session. Worth using for every non-trivial PR.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-08T02:35:43.130Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGXN2YYMYG5EEFQDM5CA6C2A\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Documentation tasks that update README/AGENTS.md should also check skill files (.claude/skills/) for staleness on the same topics. Easy to miss because skills are a separate concern. A validate --skills --docs check could catch this.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-08T03:35:21.813Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGXN2Z5DF52R8XHKHYFV9XE1\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Running 4 parallel Explore/Bash subagents to research README structure, AGENTS.md structure, full CLI catalog, and recent git features simultaneously saved significant time and produced comprehensive input for the docs update.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-08T03:35:22.029Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGXN2ZATMXN5QJJQSMJVJZWC\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"AGENTS.md task state transitions documented task complete as working from in_progress/pending, but CLI actually requires pending_review (or --skip-review). Pre-existing inaccuracy that propagated to README. Codex caught it via runtime spot-checks that I did not do.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-08T03:35:22.202Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGWZ26Q5N99GVBCSF23HM253\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Stale index mutation pattern: when mutating items in a loop with a pre-built refIndex, track created slugs in a parallel Set since refIndex won't see loop-created items. Pattern: importReservedSlugs Set alongside refIndex.isSlugAvailable(). Applied in plan-import to prevent cross-namespace slug collisions within a single import run.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-07T21:10:28.325Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGWZ26T7QDNKSE0F0GSX0W5T\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex iterative review as convergence loop: codex review → fix → re-review converges on correctness. 4 rounds on PR #346 found progressively deeper cross-namespace slug collision gaps (duplicate_slug handling → plans missing from refIndex → stale index for import-created specs → spec creation not checking importReservedSlugs). Each round caught a real bug.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-07T21:10:28.423Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGWZ26WJB8X4S3SN7GPF881Q\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex review depth insufficient on first pass: 4 review rounds were needed to fully validate plan-import slug safety. Each fix introduced or revealed the next gap. Root cause: Codex reviews surface-level patterns first (wrong API check) before deeper ones (stale index across mutations). Need a way to prime Codex to reason about mutation-staleness and index invalidation upfront, possibly via a review checklist or system prompt addition to the codex skill.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-07T21:10:28.498Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGY73W0M9YD0PKC74CW5NSFR\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test-first doc editing: building eval scenarios before trimming AGENTS.md prevented info loss. 15 scenarios + 8 stress test recall questions validated the trimmed doc (14/15 PASS, 6/8 PASS). Pattern: build test suite → make changes → validate → fix gaps.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-08T08:50:25.940Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGY73W3NX1Q0AV6KA9TZB2E9\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Stress testing with real codebase exploration is more effective than synthetic padding for finding doc gaps. Agent reads actual code (building 30k+ tokens of context), then answers recall questions. Found 2 real degradation points (PR workflow steps, scope expansion) that were reinforced.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-08T08:50:26.037Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGY73W66K9NASKQBHSKY2ZHG\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex as second reviewer on doc PRs caught a real inconsistency (scenario expected answer vs AGENTS.md rule) and a non-existent file path. Worth running on documentation PRs, not just code PRs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-08T08:50:26.118Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGY73W872YHXWQ8VNBAQF5DD\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"GitHub PR review thread resolution requires GraphQL mutation (resolveReviewThread). REST reply endpoint posts replies but does not resolve threads. Had to discover thread node IDs via GraphQL query first.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-08T08:50:26.183Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHAAN8DMG4HYPXCQY05R9QT9\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Re-baseline research findings against current code before creating specs. In CLI agent-UX session, 7 of 21 recommendations from telemetry analysis were already implemented. Verifying each against the codebase with parallel explore agents before speccing saved significant overhead (would have created 7 unnecessary specs and 7 unnecessary tasks).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-13T01:43:14.612Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHCYW7KKRGN2MV594S8YZMXH\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Commander.js parent-action option routing: when parent and subcommands define the same options, Commander doesn't cleanly route them. Tried passThroughOptions (requires global enablePositionalOptions, breaks --json global option), ended up using allowUnknownOption + temporary Command re-parse. Pattern works but is non-idiomatic. If more command groups need default actions, consider extracting this into a shared utility.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-14T02:15:03.539Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHFCMD893TQMFJWQY84RR59C\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel subagent research pattern: launching 4+ research agents simultaneously on different aspects of the same question (cross-project audit, usage patterns, external ecosystem, install story) produced comprehensive non-overlapping findings in ~6 minutes. Much more effective than sequential investigation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-15T00:53:56.105Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHFCMDBFRWBZ1P7NFFH8J7RA\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Dual-reviewer pattern for plans: having both an internal holistic reviewer (Claude) and an external reviewer (Codex) independently review the same plan catches complementary issues. Internal finds code-level integration problems, external finds architectural concerns. Both agreed on the same critical issues (compound ACs, inline YAML). Three revision cycles (v1 reviewed v2 reviewed v3) produced significantly stronger output.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-15T00:53:56.207Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHFCMDEATQ0R2Q4WW4979DQA\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Iterative clarifying questions with ask tool: asking one question at a time with 3-4 concrete options (each with descriptions) before synthesizing research into a plan led to well-informed decisions. User could respond quickly because each question had enough context from the research. Better than presenting a full plan and asking for feedback.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-15T00:53:56.298Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHFPVSVMKQTR0DZCVVZ2QS6J\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"CLI commands targeting main project files (like .claude/skills/) must use ctx.rootDir, not ctx.specDir or path.dirname(ctx.specDir). The specDir is the spec content location (.kspec/ in shadow mode), while rootDir is always the project root. Using dirname(specDir) fails in shadow mode because .kspec/ is a worktree at the project root level. Encountered in skill render command where files were written to /tmp/ instead of project root.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-15T03:52:44.148Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHHR77A38WS28NJSMWG2FN0R\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Structured interview (one question at a time with pro/con analysis) before planning leads to well-reasoned architecture decisions. User engagement is higher when they see trade-offs laid out clearly.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-15T22:54:55.811Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHHR77CK3KME4QHCS62H0JFH\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Running both internal Plan agent review AND Codex review-plan on the same plan catches complementary issues. Internal review finds code-level gaps; Codex finds spec quality issues.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-15T22:54:55.891Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHHR77EW34VT6EEW1NZHK6YF\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"kspec batch uses kebab-case args (depends-on) but schema fields use snake_case (depends_on). Inconsistency causes trial-and-error on first batch use.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-15T22:54:55.964Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHKTQNHA07MZXGVJQHQAW7CA\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel subagent review of ralph loop: 5 agents reviewing different PR ranges (371-376, 377-384, 385-393, 394-402, test suite) completed in ~3min wall clock. Independent agents finding the same duplication issues confirms real problems vs noise. Effective pattern for post-loop quality review.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-16T18:17:20.683Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHKTQNN38FSK8SAEJ34G0P6F\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop PR-by-PR review process misses cross-PR duplication accumulation. PR #381 added rendering utils, #383 duplicated them in a new file, #394 consolidated render functions but missed the utilities, #401 added more dead code. Each PR passes review individually but the aggregate drift is significant (24 inbox items from one loop). Consider adding a consolidation/cleanup iteration every N PRs or at loop end.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-16T18:17:20.803Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHQXGWG6BEEQBJ0VZ32NX2T1\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Background PR review agent can act on stale context: agent added 172-line test file for a spec that was deleted during review. When running review agents in background while making spec/task changes in foreground, the agent does not see those changes. Required a follow-up cleanup PR.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-18T08:23:01.894Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHQXGWQJGKKY7H3KKRDXT5HQ\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex PR review skill always demands // AC: @spec-ref ac-N annotations, even for infrastructure/cleanup tasks where ACs describe absence of code. Should skip AC annotation checks when task has no spec_ref or when spec type is not user-facing behavior.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-18T08:23:02.130Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHRP78K7727DMKA224B3ZZ9Y\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Running kspec setup during development creates kspec-agents.md and .claude/skills/ in project root. These are test artifacts for the kspec project itself (which uses AGENTS.md, not kspec-agents.md). They trigger repeated stop hook warnings about uncommitted changes. Need either: (a) test isolation so setup tests dont leak into project root, or (b) cleanup step in bootstrap/dev workflow.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-18T15:34:40.999Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHRP78PDNPQAKZCPHR5XZV86\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Multi-model PR review (Claude + Codex in parallel) caught issues that single-model review missed. Codex found missing debugLog in outer catch and weak test assertions. Worth continuing this pattern for non-trivial PRs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-18T15:34:41.101Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHRYZ569SCKS1HAFJK71Y2Z7\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel dual-reviewer strategy (Claude agent + Codex) is effective: Claude validates correctness, Codex catches spec-alignment gaps. Use both for PRs with spec ACs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-18T18:07:32.554Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHSG0CSF18QF1S4MMMEM3S8Y\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex PR review (gpt-5.3-codex) caught a real correctness bug in drift detection (hash-gating for sidecar changes) that the implementing agent missed. Codex reproduced the issue locally with a concrete script. High value for code review.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-18T23:05:18.896Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHSKZDW60J9YF6XTJ2WZDDE5\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Refactoring tasks without spec_ref have AC traceability gap — task-level ACs in notes aren't discoverable by standard // AC: @spec-ref ac-N annotation pattern. Codex review flagged this on PR #411. Options: (1) allow // AC: @task-ref ac-N, (2) require spec items even for refactoring, (3) teach reviewers to check task notes. Related: @task-skill-module-split had no spec_ref but defined 3 ACs in notes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-19T00:14:41.542Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHT79F7K2QV2HKNRTD0JQTJ1\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Guard script bash code embedded in JS template literal makes quote escaping painful — single quotes inside tr/sed cause parse errors. Consider extracting guard scripts to standalone .sh files loaded at setup time instead of inline template literals.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-19T05:52:13.555Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHT79FAZJZ43QN3BZA28KQYM\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Running codex review in parallel with PR review agent caught a real security bypass (split-quote git \\\"reset\\\" --hard). The dual-reviewer pattern (code-level + quality-gate) provides meaningful coverage overlap.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-19T05:52:13.663Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHVE714TTNEME761Y1783EYC\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Shared test fixture fragility: tests/fixtures/kynetic.meta.yaml is used by multiple test files. Tests that append YAML keys (like meta.test.ts appending conventions:) collide when the fixture gains new top-level keys. Caused real regression in PR #413. Consider per-test fixture isolation or fixture composition helpers.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-19T17:12:28.058Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHVE7189BCM4HWW9PXWAFP37\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel agent reviews (Codex + /pr-review) found complementary issues: Codex caught test annotation gaps, review agent caught shared fixture regression. Multi-reviewer pattern is high-value for quality.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-19T17:12:28.169Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHVYHKAVN1G54X8C2BJYMK3X\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Invoked /spec-plan skill but wrote implementation guide instead of plan-import-format document. User had explicitly said /spec-plan. Lesson: invoking a skill is not enough — must follow its output format from the FIRST write. When /spec-plan is invoked for plan mode, write the plan file in kspec plan import format (# Title, ## Specs with YAML code block, ## Tasks, ## Implementation Notes) from the start.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-19T21:57:51.579Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHVYHKEBF6AHDDXVQZJAZV5H\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Dual review pattern before plan import: running both an internal plan review agent and Codex in parallel caught YAML quoting failures and substantive spec gaps (batch mode, worktree detection, remote type algorithm). Reviews converged on same must-fixes, giving high confidence. Always dual-review complex plan documents before importing.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-19T21:57:51.691Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHVYHKH7J728F29ZS1SGF2PM\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel consumer project exploration: launching 3 agents to explore kynetic-bot, imgen, comfy-ecaj-nodes simultaneously produced convergent findings (same Quick Start pattern, same hooks, same skill drift) that were far more convincing than exploring one project. Use parallel exploration when researching cross-project patterns.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-19T21:57:51.783Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHW3CC8V4PDG1R22S5229TA4\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Dual review pattern (internal Plan agent + Codex review-plan) catches complementary issues. Internal agent finds architectural concerns, Codex finds format/structure issues. Convergent findings give high confidence. Worth standardizing for all plan imports.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-19T23:22:23.387Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHW3CCBSNYH48BKQX2Q2CNAC\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Post-import verification agent catches data integrity issues that dry-run misses (null spec_ref, missing implementation notes). Should be part of standard plan import workflow.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-19T23:22:23.481Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHWVQNZV7NDDTQB5ADP4FPCW\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"GitHub blocks REQUEST_CHANGES on own PR. Ralph review subagents operate under the same GitHub credentials as the PR author, so they cannot post REQUEST_CHANGES reviews — only COMMENT. The pr-review skill instructs posting APPROVE or REQUEST_CHANGES, but REQUEST_CHANGES will always fail in self-authored PRs. Need either: (1) a separate GitHub bot account for review agents, or (2) the skill should use COMMENT event with structured review content instead of REQUEST_CHANGES.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-20T06:27:59.612Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHWVQP3NBA0YYME4FY9K2T0W\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Dual-reviewer pattern (Claude agent + Codex) for PR review. Running both in parallel on PR #424 gave convergent findings on the critical branch-lookup bug (independent discovery by both). Codex also caught input validation gap that Claude missed. Different models find different issues — convergent findings give high confidence, divergent findings expand coverage.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-20T06:27:59.733Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHWVQP6YEJ0241DN6F4QA54J\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel review audit pattern: spawning 4 specialized subagents (worker process adherence, review process adherence, code quality, spec/AC coverage) to evaluate a ralph session. Each agent had a focused lens and found complementary issues. Total wall-clock time ~2 min for what would have been 15+ min of sequential analysis.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-20T06:27:59.838Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHYTNNGG0B44BK1QJMRGNYZA\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Dual review convergence: running both pr-review subagent and /codex review in parallel catches different issues and convergent findings give high confidence. Both flagged dead verifyTaskCompleted code independently.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-21T00:47:53.872Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHZ6H8YSJYW5Z9TDSA3PSRJX\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Convention vs template mental model clarified: Templates carry kspec-generic content (shadow branch, task lifecycle, ralph loop — same for ALL kspec projects). Conventions carry project-specific rules (testing gotchas, dev setup, CI limitations — unique per project). When porting content from AGENTS.md, ask: does this apply to every kspec project? Template. Only this project? Convention.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-21T04:15:12.858Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHZBEEVJXMQ6TYQCP2584JKT\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Spec-before-implement pattern: adding ac-6 to @agent-instruction-gen before coding the noop behavior made test coverage natural and caught the right contract upfront.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-21T05:41:03.474Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHZHZAQJE6KF7GHBEK2E79PK\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"task get not showing descriptions meant had to grep raw YAML to verify task content after batch creation. Critical gap for agents working on tasks — they cannot read the description via CLI.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-21T07:35:07.762Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ1A32GV14R9ZSDBQYCKFW3V\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Platform behavior assumption: PR #440 added namespace rendering (.claude/skills/kspec/<id>/) without verifying Claude Code actually discovers nested skill directories. It does not. Future platform integration work should verify discovery behavior (e.g. create a test skill, check if Claude Code lists it) before building rendering pipelines around assumed directory structures.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-21T23:55:50.683Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ1RW3898SCWYZN358637199\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Meta vs manifest confusion: skill render reads from meta (shadow branch), not template manifest. Changing manifest ID without updating meta has no effect. Need to delete+re-add skill via CLI.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T04:14:10.697Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ331N2YAJ66MXHK1W9J9HQX\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel subagent research pattern: launching 3+ research agents simultaneously to investigate different aspects (code state, git history, task completions) builds comprehensive evidence in ~3 minutes vs 15+ sequentially. Critical for large triage sessions (95 items). Each agent gets a focused investigation scope and returns structured findings.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T16:31:12.990Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3M13X05B558KQ58AXRM1K1\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Zod superRefine pattern for status-dependent field requirements (e.g., triaged requires reasoning/decided_by, acted_on requires acted_at). Should be the default approach for any schema with status lifecycle — flat .optional() misses state invariants. First used in triage.ts, should apply to plan.ts and similar.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T21:28:01.184Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3T9X36SS737DYRWW9QE9ZV\",\n    \"type\": \"idea\",\n    \"content\": \"Spec gap test\\n\\nReasoning: needs spec\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T23:17:40.582Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3X7D52RR2R6N3MS45Y7EE6\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"CI timing race: when Codex posts a review comment after CI check-unresolved-comments has already run, the check fails because the new thread is unresolved. Requires manual re-run after resolving. Consider: (1) make check-unresolved-comments a required-last check, (2) have the review workflow auto-re-run the check after resolving threads, or (3) add a gh run rerun step to the codex review skill.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T00:08:44.450Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4SJP2673H5V8NHJPMNNN7X\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"[spec-gap] Include triage records in static snapshot (kspec-snapshot.json). Currently the snapshot format (KspecSnapshot type) doesn't include triage records, so the triage page in static/GitHub Pages mode shows an empty state with a notice instead of displaying existing triage decisions read-only. AC-8 of @interactive-triage-ui expects read-only display. Needs: add triage records to export snapshot, update KspecSnapshot type, add fetchTriageRecordsStatic to read from snapshot.\\n\\nReasoning: There's a spec gap here\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:24:14.150Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4SJP5TREMPX687MHBW8Y2Q\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"[spec-gap] Cross-feature requirement pattern: How to express that core features (search, validate, export) must support all entity types. When new entity type added, should automatically imply tasks for core features. Options: (1) applies_to field on feature specs, (2) trait on entity types like @trait-searchable, (3) validation warning for missing coverage, (4) parent spec that entity types must satisfy. Surfaced when realizing search doesn't cover inbox.\\n\\nReasoning: first item reasoning\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:24:14.266Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4SNE9GHZMFEE49D3P4CKJZ\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"[spec-gap] kspec validate @spec or @task — targeted validation that checks a single spec/task's AC coverage against codebase. Not full approval, just verifies each AC has at least one // AC: annotation in test files. Would make trait AC gaps immediately visible during task-work. Could be used by local-review skill as a concrete check instead of relying on agent diligence.\\n\\nReasoning: Must-have but needs spec design - targeted kspec validate for single item\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:25:44.496Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4SNFHF46MCSST52ZMWXJ1R\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"[spec-gap] Design section configuration for agents generate — allow projects to control which sections appear (skills table, conventions, workflows, static templates). Key questions: where does config live, include vs exclude list, defaults, custom sections, ordering, data vs template distinction, migration path. See plan doc for full requirements.\\n\\nReasoning: Must-have but needs spec design - section configuration for agents generate\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:25:45.775Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4VDK8ECG1W5T95TPP1KVF6\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Pre-analyzed triage report (HTML artifact) combined with kspec batch made processing 107 inbox items efficient. Record-then-act pattern provided good audit trail. Pattern: analyze offline, port decisions via batch.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:56:24.590Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ50B8SFBX6C1E9XRYBXZ22Q\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"settings.json written by 3 independent subsystems during setup (installClaudeCodeHooks, seedPermissions, enablePluginInProject via modifyJsonAtomic). Makes skip-when-unchanged optimization impossible without either a shared coordinator or consolidating all mutations into one function. Each writer reads, modifies, writes independently — interleaving prevents simple content comparison.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T10:22:31.215Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ51NBSJR7R8ZRT4RM8Q26DT\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Post-merge branch state: When inheriting a session where a PR was already merged, the working directory may be on main. Always check branch (git branch --show-current) before committing, and create a feature branch first. Recovering from an accidental main commit requires creating a branch from HEAD and resetting main.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T10:45:30.546Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ5B3SSRXMPW76HE43H15EKS\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex PR review caught a real type drift bug (Convention.validation schema mismatch) during web-ui type deduplication PR. The shared-type approach works well: define in @kynetic-ai/shared, re-export from web-ui, enforce with static analysis test. Dual review (Codex + CI) catches complementary issues.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T13:30:40.824Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ63RW7JFBTJ7FWG6MQR3W71\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel subagent audit pattern: launching 4+ agents in parallel for deep-dive review of ralph loop work (PR quality, functional verification, loop behavior, process adherence) produced comprehensive results in ~90 seconds. Effective for post-loop quality assessment.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T20:41:37.266Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ63RWAKZWYCWNNG68KFBHBX\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Dual review pattern (internal agent + Codex) for plan review catches different issue categories. Internal agent found consistency gaps; Codex found concurrency risks. Convergent findings give high confidence before implementation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T20:41:37.364Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ71CSSQNCH8KAP3YRSQT4GY\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"@trait-semantic-exit-codes ACs hardcode exit code numbers (ac-2: 'exit code 1', ac-3: 'exit code 2', ac-4: 'exit code 3') that don't match kspec's actual EXIT_CODES scheme (ERROR=1, USAGE_ERROR=2, NOT_FOUND=3, VALIDATION_FAILED=4). Every command adding trait AC test coverage needs clarifying comments explaining the mapping. Fix: update trait ACs to use semantic descriptions ('non-zero exit code indicating validation failure') instead of hardcoded numbers, or update to match kspec's actual codes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T05:19:18.839Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ731A1QK5ZZG40DNSERD1MD\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex review caught fail-open bug in getBudget() — corrupt budget.json was silently treated as 'no budget', effectively disabling enforcement. Changed to fail closed (only ENOENT returns null, parse/validation errors propagate). Pattern: for security/enforcement code, always default to the restrictive path. Codex consistently catches error-handling path issues that internal review misses.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T05:47:59.416Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ73MEZ9BFMX73JFB0ZDSJVM\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph task-limit-guard hook blocks gh pr create even when finishing current task work. The guard treats all Bash commands equally — it can't distinguish 'creating a PR for completed work' from 'starting new task work'. Result: branch pushed but PR not created, requiring next iteration to finish. Consider whitelisting gh pr create or detecting PR creation context in the guard.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T05:58:27.050Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ75K21W6FB80AB5567TBKAX\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"task set --depends-on replaces all deps rather than appending. When setting multiple deps in separate batch commands, only the last one survives. Must provide all deps in a single call. Consider adding --add-depends-on for append semantics (similar to --relates-to on item set which appends).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T06:32:38.204Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ75RQEGNKHH82MGZK6Z4NXC\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Dual plan review (internal agent + /codex review-plan) catches complementary issues: internal finds design gaps and terminology problems, codex finds code-level feasibility issues (missing APIs, wrong method names, breaking consumers). Convergent findings indicate high confidence. Used successfully for session-start-redesign plan.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T06:35:43.952Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ77DA9VYBRRT8BCTVGAJC0T\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Budget enforcement in task start integrates cleanly: check before transition, increment after save, resume case handled by existing early return. The library functions (checkBudget/incrementBudget) do the heavy lifting — CLI handler just wires them together. Good separation of concerns between store.ts and task.ts.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T07:04:27.195Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ82GPNAENV2SH3Q8XYJBQA9\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel agent spawning for session log audit: 5 agents analyzing different log files simultaneously gave comprehensive coverage. Pattern worth replicating for any multi-file analysis task.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T14:58:09.706Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ8EE76AQYX301F9A34XXPWK\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"setupTempFixtures() returns a flat dir where tempDir IS the specDir — no .kspec/ wrapper. Agents that assume nested structure (path.join(tempDir, \\\".kspec\\\")) get silent test failures. AGENTS.md test helpers table should note this.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T18:26:31.242Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ8J44C5EXHEAAPHTVC71R0B\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Mock ACP agent pattern (tests/fixtures/mock-acp-agent.mjs) enables fast behavioral testing of ralph subprocess orchestration. Tests real env injection, budget cleanup, and signal handling in ~2s each. Key enabler: --adapter-cmd flag + spawnRalphUntil helper that watches output markers then kills the process.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T19:30:54.981Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ8J44G2VMVX31VYM83FP9TN\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph CLI uses --max-loops but internal variables and log messages say iterations. Minor naming inconsistency that causes confusion when writing tests or debugging. Example: --max-loops 1 but logs Starting ralph loop (max 1 iterations).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T19:30:55.106Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ8NDTX3WCBCC198CJAQQSZN\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex PR review caught exec()+unref() not actually preventing event loop hang (stdio pipes still buffered). Validated that /codex review-pr adds real value beyond rubber-stamping.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T20:28:38.691Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ8QR2WD5BSVEMKJ4R4K0JET\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Pure function pattern for hook/guard commands: exporting the core logic as a testable pure function (e.g. evaluateWorktreeGuard) with stdin/process handling in the CLI layer enables fast unit testing (44 tests, no I/O) while keeping the CLI integration tests minimal (7 tests for protocol compliance). Replicate this pattern for future hook commands.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T21:09:11.693Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ8R05R2GJBCGFQHY966GDD8\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Plan-derived tasks with depends_on sometimes become no-ops because the dependency task already implements all shared spec ACs. Seen in iteration 3: @update-setup-with-migration-cleanup (all 6 ACs done by @implement-native-worktree-guard) and @add-multi-harness-env-injection (all injection ACs done by @implement-session-create-command). Wastes budget starts and discovery time. Potential fix: plan import could warn when multiple tasks share a spec and one depends on the other, or task start could auto-detect 'AC already covered' and offer to close.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T21:13:36.770Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ8X527NACE7S92M7120K6A3\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Session checkpoint hook fires repeatedly on research-only sessions with pre-existing uncommitted changes from a different task. No way to signal this is a read-only investigation session.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T22:43:39.893Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ8XQFTK1B2Y3CVE6XBQ2WP0\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Cross-cutting skill updates need checklist: When a concept spans multiple skills (e.g., spec context discovery in codex, pr-review, local-review, review template), updating one skill without checking all related ones leads to inconsistency. Codex review on PR #511 found 4 findings where the dig-deeper pattern wasn't applied uniformly. Consider: a way to tag related skills, or a pre-commit check that flags partial updates to skill groups.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T22:53:43.636Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJA6SXWS8W28JRSS5B1D227N\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel audit agents pattern: spawning 4 specialized agents (code quality, test quality, non-test code, process quality) in parallel gives comprehensive coverage in ~2 min wall clock. Each agent needs clear scope boundaries and structured output format.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-25T10:51:35.193Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJA9BTHR62240G32RM5P0VBP\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex skill silently exits with no output when OPENAI_API_KEY is not set. The skill documents gh auth preflight but not API key validation. Agents waste time discovering this. Skill should check for API key and fail fast with clear message.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-25T11:36:18.744Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJAAGK1RK0N21TTF843NZWV6\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Session test helper extraction (task @01KJ9ZDE) went smoothly. The all-fields-optional SessionContext pattern works well for tests that each need a different subset of fields — TypeScript structural typing handles it naturally. Reduced ~315 lines of duplication across 6 files into 2 shared modules. The inbox helpers needed a tempDir parameter change (closure → explicit arg) which was the main mechanical transformation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-25T11:56:23.481Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJB02BPX9CYWJV8MKWKAG10R\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"testUlid('PREFIX') returns identical values across calls without explicit sequence argument — deterministic with default sequence=0. Caused false-positive test pass in session-checkpoint-scoping tests where mySession and otherSession were identical. Fix options: auto-incrementing counter, require sequence param, or rename to testUlidDeterministic to make behavior obvious. testUlids() works correctly but is easy to overlook.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-25T18:13:05.885Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJBJX00DRJV7AG07Q57HQY2Y\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Self-validating task pattern: created a P1 automation-eligible task whose acceptance criteria IS verifying the fix works. Ralph picks it up, the task checks its own session_id stamp, and the result documents whether the fix works end-to-end. Useful for testing harness-level integration that can't be verified from inside an active session.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-25T23:42:13.006Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJBTMZJE38BW62X2QG6CMYYK\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Elysia body schema validation returns 422 (not 400) before the handler runs. When writing E2E tests for daemon endpoints that have body schema validation (t.Object(...)), missing/invalid body fields return 422. If the handler also has manual validation that returns 400, the schema check fires first. Account for this in test assertions — do not assume 400 for missing body fields on Elysia-validated routes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T01:57:39.023Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJBW3RSM37ERH1SJ37DYHRB3\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"GitHub PR thread resolution requires GraphQL mutation (resolveReviewThread), not REST API. REST API only supports replies. Pattern: get thread node IDs via graphql query on pullRequest.reviewThreads, then loop resolveReviewThread mutations. Reliably resolved all 7 threads in one pass.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T02:23:12.180Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJBW3RXM0JGWW5GP8KBE53C6\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"scanTestCoverage() only scanned rootDir/tests/ — missed packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/ where Playwright E2E specs with AC annotations live. Fixed by extending scan to also cover the E2E directory and .spec.ts/.spec.js file extensions. Risk: any future E2E test directory additions would silently miss coverage until the scan list is updated. Consider making E2E scan paths configurable or convention-documented.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T02:23:12.308Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJC3JSTA7DXYJ8QRZJ341KS8\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Trait N/A annotations placed inside JSDoc block comments are not machine-parseable — the '* // AC:' pattern (where * is the JSDoc line prefix) does not match the scanner's '// AC:' regex. Must use standalone // AC: line comments OUTSIDE any /** ... */ block. Occurred in api-meta.spec.ts E2E tests, caught by Codex review, required fix commit.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T04:33:44.778Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJCVXZYRRDSMSAA2AN5TPVWR\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"AC annotation verification gap: Tests annotated with wrong AC refs (e.g., Elysia 422 tests annotated as ac-23 when ac-23 requires 400+{error,details}; POST body validation annotated as ac-5/6/7 when those are for X-Kspec-Dir header). Fix: always run kspec item get @spec-ref and read AC text before annotating tests.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T11:39:17.337Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJCXMR5S7ZZJ2DYQR7FEHXSA\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex retrospective PR review workflow: /codex pr on merged PRs surfaces real issues. Found stale dist/ bug via retro review of PR #547 that live review missed.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T12:09:11.609Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJD309GMRXFSRKWNJ6KD3MTY\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"JS date validation gotcha in E2E tests: new Date(\\\"invalid\\\") returns Invalid Date but does NOT throw. Tests using expect(() => new Date(x)).not.toThrow() or try/catch will always pass even with malformed timestamps - false positive. Always use isNaN(new Date(x).getTime()) for timestamp format validation. Caught this in api-websocket.spec.ts timestamp assertion (AC-29/@trait-websocket-protocol ac-3).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T13:42:52.692Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJD309N30QVB8RRSD7A9J3CV\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"CI check-unresolved-comments timing race in review fix cycle: When Codex posts inline review comments on a PR, we push a fix commit which triggers CI immediately. The check-unresolved-comments job runs BEFORE we resolve the Codex threads via GraphQL, causing it to fail on the new commit. Then requires manual workflow re-run. Mitigation: always resolve all review threads BEFORE pushing any fix commits during a review cycle.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T13:42:52.835Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJD309R4M9JR7EDRZPE91AEA\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"window.__testWs pattern for Playwright WebSocket E2E: Store native browser WebSocket in window.__testWs via page.evaluate() and access it across subsequent evaluate() calls. Browser context maintains the global between calls. Enables clean helper functions (connectWebSocket, sendAndWaitForAck, subscribeAndWaitForBroadcast) without needing Playwright WebSocket interception. Used successfully in packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/api-websocket.spec.ts.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T13:42:52.932Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJD6M8MHMH09W8NJ504S0D0R\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"When deleting test files that cover spec ACs, kspec validate does not warn that AC annotations are being removed. This means coverage regressions are only caught during Codex review after the PR is up — requiring an extra fix commit. A pre-delete validate or a local-review gate that checks 'these AC annotations would disappear' would catch this earlier. Observed during task-delete-static-analysis-tests (PR #558): deleted web-ui-triage.test.ts removed all @interactive-triage-ui ac-1..ac-8 coverage; Codex caught it, required creating triage.spec.ts to recover.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T14:46:12.882Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJD933WJ6W0FBY150BET1PZN\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"PR merged by review subagent while worker agent still editing files on same branch — local branch switches to main automatically, all pending Edit tool changes silently lost. Caused significant rework this session (re-applying all triage.spec.ts changes on new branch fix/triage-ac6-session-close-error). The review subagent and worker agent operate concurrently on the same branch in a fix cycle, creating a race condition. Potential mitigations: (1) worker agent checks for branch changes before editing, (2) ralph serializes review subagent after worker fully stops, (3) worker agent uses a local patch/stash before any branch changes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T15:29:16.691Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDFFJGEQ0R6JST5PR2JZVN4\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Dual review pattern (internal plan review + /codex review-plan) catches complementary issues — format vs substance. Worth standardizing for all plan imports.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T17:20:56.334Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDFFJK5FZ5DBANYTJEVH6Q9\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Shadow branch merge driver handles complex YAML conflicts (project.tasks.yaml with 38 divergent commits) automatically during rebase — reliable for ralph parallel sessions.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T17:20:56.421Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDN04RM1EHW2FKD5SRD3Y95\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Dual review pattern (plan agent + Codex) catches complementary issues. Plan agent validates design, Codex validates contracts and test coverage. Worth keeping as standard practice for non-trivial PRs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T18:57:22.197Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ0ZTHNQF93KHS4516B8C6\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"[spec-gap] Merge driver: auto-resolve .kspec-agents-hash file conflicts (deterministic hash, should always take latest)\\n\\nReasoning: Merge driver for hash file — low frequency conflict, manual resolution works\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:47.057Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ0ZZPZZY4TE3CX11Q65BP\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"[spec-gap] Plan import: generate richer task descriptions from Implementation Notes section — include file paths, what to change, verification steps instead of generic 'See plan...' text\\n\\nReasoning: Plan import richer descriptions — improvement, not blocking\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:47.222Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ114YVRSMJQSKZ2P4CQW0\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"[spec-gap] Triage ac-5 says sets result_ref but delete action may not produce one. Verify behavior and update spec or add test assertion.\\n\\nReasoning: Triage ac-5 result_ref for delete — spec may be wrong, needs verification\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:48.414Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ119THNSN93R18BVCPZSN\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"[spec-gap] Triage API spec says ac-4 and ac-5 use PUT method but implementation uses POST /:ref/override and POST /:ref/act. Spec needs updating to match reality.\\n\\nReasoning: Triage API spec PUT vs POST mismatch — spec needs updating to match implementation\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:48.570Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1281SE4DYG57NR127DKN\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"[spec-gap] @cmd-validate spec is stale — missing flags: --completeness, --staleness, --drift, --alignment, --skills, --conventions (all already implemented in code). Pre-existing drift, not introduced by trait AC task.\\n\\nReasoning: @cmd-validate spec is stale — missing 6 flags already in code. Spec drift.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:49.537Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ14VW0MD9YQ077ZM45MVQ\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"[spec-gap] kspec meta set convention: add --update-rule and --remove-rule flags. Currently the only way to fix a rule is to delete the entire convention and recreate it. Surfaced during skill CLI lookups task when codex review caught a wording issue in one rule.\\n\\nReasoning: Convention --update-rule — DX improvement, workaround is delete+recreate\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:52.221Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDR3S3ZJRMAB0M35SQEGXRM\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Triage record-then-act pattern with UI review works well at scale: batch-record 41 decisions, user reviews/overrides in web UI, batch-act on confirmed. Clean separation of agent proposals from user decisions. 12 overrides out of 41 shows useful agent-human collaboration.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:51:47.071Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDV6RXJE25G2B3QRF02MYW3\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex two-pass review pattern effective: implement → codex review → fix bug found → re-review clean. Caught missing previousValue in injectCodexEnv that would have broken Ralph cleanup.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T20:45:50.899Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDXCB7E87A4EYJKK009VQ2K\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Well-decomposed task descriptions with exact files and verification criteria make implementation fast — the per-adapter-auto-approve task took one focused session from start to merged PR.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T21:23:50.639Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDXCBBHHBBKXDKV5Z74BX7B\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"MOCK_ACP_VERIFY_ARGS_FILE pattern extends the existing env var verification pattern cleanly — behavioral test infrastructure for ACP agent spawning is now solid.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T21:23:50.769Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDZV06SJXM9RG4YPXRXHBHQ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex PR review as iterative second reviewer catches real bugs. Two-round pattern (review → fix → re-review) provides high-confidence quality gate for ralph adapter/env code.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T22:06:48.025Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDZV0AJP3K3RNTZ3A9ZXQFC\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Plan-derived task descriptions with exact line numbers and numbered change steps make implementation fast and focused. The plan-to-task pipeline produces high-quality work items.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T22:06:48.146Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJEVM2Y2ZXMSY10GNP2CMBCV\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"When posting content containing $ and angle-bracket placeholders via shell-wrapped commands, interpolation can silently mutate task/PR notes; prefer literal-safe quoting or file-based payloads.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T06:12:21.570Z\",\n    \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJEVMQJJZ127WW5CHM0KQK16\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Portable {skill:<id>} tokens with renderer-side platform resolution reduced template duplication and kept Claude/Codex invocation guidance consistent across SKILL.md and supporting markdown.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T06:12:42.706Z\",\n    \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGAE26H74N8C0ZTZ6HH5V2N\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel plan review (Plan agent + Codex) catches complementary issues: architectural concerns vs format/structural issues. High convergence on edge cases gives confidence. Worth standardizing as a dual-review step.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T19:50:27.281Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGAE2A5KKANQDY4KRZWFM9W\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Plan-derived tasks need manual follow-up (batch set tags + note) to be automation-ready. The derive step should produce standalone tasks.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T19:50:27.397Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGAKM10AY9KFR9JXBWFFCGX\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Core skill update UX gap: kspec skill update is version-gated, so same-version template edits are skipped and require kspec skill install-core. This is non-obvious during local template iteration. Improve guidance (update vs install-core) or adjust command behavior to detect local template changes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": \"@session-reflect\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T19:53:29.377Z\",\n    \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": \"@01KJGQVK\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGFKJ79GAK3QF33QHRMYWJW\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Holistic plan review (plan + derived specs + tasks + traits together) before any code is written caught 6 spec gaps in @plan-auto-close-stale-active-sessions including missing targeting semantics, liveness guard, corrupt events handling, and task dependency ordering. Pattern: evaluate the full derivation tree, not just individual specs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T21:20:50.410Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGQCA1DEK15Y59X5M8N5HR5\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex PR review threads require manual GraphQL resolution + CI re-trigger before merge. Multi-step dance every time codex posts inline comments.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T23:36:41.261Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGQCA7649GZMT2HA0Z5CXQA\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Iterative codex review loop (review → fix → re-review) converges well. Three rounds on PR #582 caught duplicate label, spec alignment drift, and missing test branch.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T23:36:41.446Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGQKPWM32W85246H3VAWDD0\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Targeted dry-run + focused test loop quickly exposed core-skill source-of-truth drift; package-distribution test caught stale plugin artifact path immediately.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": \"@session-reflect\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T23:40:43.797Z\",\n    \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGW8ZB984E1QZHMGGCHSRXR\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"CLI tests that execute dist artifacts can produce misleading failures when dist is stale; this creates avoidable debugging churn before the real code behavior is evaluated.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T01:02:14.889Z\",\n    \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGW8ZFQ697G7Z8T81MTXN35\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Using a focused validate mode matrix (schema/refs/alignment/completeness/staleness + combinations) quickly verified scoped semantics and prevented regressions while keeping turnaround fast.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T01:02:15.031Z\",\n    \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJJHARH9G3CT7R978K6AEBZ4\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Isolated worktree + backup branch pattern for shadow branch recovery. Creating a backup branch before destructive ops, then using /tmp worktree for experimental rebase, then patching the result back as a normal commit avoided force-push entirely. This pattern should be documented for future shadow branch divergence scenarios.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T16:29:27.977Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJJHARMST4YEMPE7PYSVXSCA\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Merge driver silent data loss when --non-interactive flag missing from git config. No error, no warning — just hangs on stdin and leaves files unmerged. 12 task completions lost silently. Root cause: shadow.ts registration code path diverged from actual git config. Fix tracked in @01KJJGJ1.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T16:29:28.089Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJJT519QTQXSJWRM17W06HH6\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex PR review takes 10+ minutes because npm test subagent polling is inefficient. Consider instructing Codex to skip full suite and rely on CI, or use test shards instead of full npm test.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T19:03:37.528Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJJT51HXZZBH71BXK6VXKM15\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex PR review cannot distinguish pre-existing test failures from regressions. Flags false positives (e.g. session-budget-integration flakiness on PR #590). Could pre-seed known-flaky test list or compare failure counts against main baseline.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T19:03:37.790Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJJT51PHNAYJRJFMW7HQHMXH\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex-then-fix cycle on PR #601 was tight: review posted, ac-9 gap caught, fixed in 1 commit, thread resolved, CI passed, merged. Total turnaround ~15 min including CI.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T19:03:37.937Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJK7F4JXEBF205YJ30MK5XS0\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task budget guard blocks needs_work fix cycle transitions. kspec task start @ref fails with budget exhausted even when the task is in needs_work state (an existing fix cycle, not a new task start). needs_work → in_progress should be exempt from the budget guard since it is resuming prior work, not starting new work. Had to skip task state transitions and create PR without proper submit flow.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T22:56:20.063Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJK7F4T0JVSCB40JEAN9PHGP\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Minimal floating-promise fix pattern: storing async function result in a variable and attaching .catch(() => {}) before Promise.race is the clean way to prevent Node.js 22 unhandled rejection crashes when a race-loser promise is later rejected by resource cleanup.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T22:56:20.288Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJKCF1SNKNBV25JG0VPW9HZ6\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Agent investigation breadth vs accuracy tradeoff — Explore agents are valuable for surveying many files quickly but their conclusions need manual verification before acting. In this session, the agent reported event listener accumulation as CRITICAL (wrong — listeners registered once per spawn) while the actual bottleneck (getEventCount O(n^2)) wasn't in its top findings. Pattern: use agents for breadth, verify claims against actual code, then form your own root cause hypothesis.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T00:23:40.085Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  }\n]\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"[\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF89NXNJVRJQ6RTHJ310SHXC\",\n    \"type\": \"idea\",\n    \"content\": \"Need better error messages\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": \"@session-start\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T10:16:15.283Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:06.781Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": \"@01KF89NY\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93NC0FXND1244CN31ZH22Z\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"ReferenceIndex Result<T> pattern gotcha: resolve() returns Result objects with .ok field, not items directly. Must check result.ok before accessing result.item - TypeScript doesn't enforce this at compile time. Pattern: if (result.ok) { use result.item } else { handle error }. Encountered multiple times across iterations.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:20.175Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:07.260Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93NCXZNXTPWAPCFPNH0STG\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Linter/tooling auto-revert blocker: During ralph loop iterations, file changes were repeatedly auto-reverted by linter/auto-save system. Code written and verified would disappear after edits. Affected shadow.ts, index.ts, test files. Possible causes: aggressive format-on-save, linter deleting code it doesn't understand, file watcher conflicts. Blocks implementation work when it occurs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:21.120Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:07.778Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93NDYAX7CWP4QP7072AHMH\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop session state freshness: Multiple issues with stale state in automation loops. (1) Iteration started on non-main branch from previous session. (2) Session context showed already-completed task as ready because context generated before commits reflected. (3) Picked completed work repeatedly. Solutions: generate context AFTER pulling latest, validate task is actually pending before starting, checkpoint script should update .kspec before next iteration.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:22.155Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:08.181Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93P6NTQJP3C2ZSND2J2MZT\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Subprocess spawning complexity: When promoting observations to tasks, initially tried spawning npm/tsx subprocess which caused temp directory path issues in tests. Switched to direct API calls (createTask/saveTask) which simplified implementation and avoided process overhead. Pattern: prefer direct API over subprocess when both run in same codebase.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:47.483Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:08.526Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93P7W2A063T315RXPC6ZF7\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Commander --json flag conflict: Command-specific --json flags conflict with global --json flag in Commander. Solution: use global flag only, check isJsonMode() instead of options.json. This pattern should be documented or enforced via convention.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:48.706Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:08.975Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93P8XZK7K9V8ERYYH6FE0Z\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Bash tool cd persistence: Commands run in same directory as previous command unless explicit cd. Running 'cd .kspec && git status' left session in .kspec worktree. Need explicit 'cd /path/to/main' to return. Can be confusing when working with shadow branch.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:49.792Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:09.402Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93PA837GGVE8DH3PVZE8WC\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"CLI output pattern: When implementing CLI commands with both human-readable and JSON formats, use success(message, data) instead of calling both success() and output() separately. The success() function already handles JSON mode internally, avoiding duplicate/mixed output.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:51.140Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:09.731Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93PBBYDPRH0WQSKN4Y18SV\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task status accuracy gap: Found task marked as priority 3 ready but implementation was already complete. All code, tests, and functionality existed. System correctly updated spec alignment when task completed, but task remained in ready list longer than it should have. Need earlier alignment checks or better detection of 'code exists but task not marked done' scenarios.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:52.286Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:10.062Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93PCN5NVFEHR801G77EK3X\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Shadow branch auto-commit PR challenges: PR included WIP commits from shadow that were auto-committed. Consider: (1) squash strategy for shadow commits when creating PR, (2) explicit checkpoint command before PR creation, or (3) shadow commit message convention (wip: prefix) to make cleanup easier.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:53.606Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:10.411Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93PDXFBPM2B1WYE6HFYJCX\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review automation friction: Had to manually launch review subagent, wait for output, interpret results, then fix issues. Could streamline with dedicated /review skill that: (1) checks for open PRs, (2) launches review subagent automatically, (3) interprets results + decision tree, (4) applies fixes if trivial, (5) merges if appropriate.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:54.895Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:10.930Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93Q1Y31HP8245N4DF67MCA\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Auto-sync vs interactive prompts anti-pattern: When adding interactive prompts to modify state, always check if automatic sync/calculation logic already exists. AlignmentIndex calculates spec status from all linked tasks - interactive prompt would allow single-task override, creating drift. Pattern: if system has 'calculated truth', don't add manual override without considering multi-entity consistency.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:51:15.396Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:11.342Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93Q2W8DC2RNGG1NA4ABQE0\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Test fixtures spec_ref conflicts: Test fixtures should avoid spec_ref assignments that conflict with derive tests. When adding spec_ref to test tasks, check if they're used in derive --dry-run tests which expect tasks not to exist yet.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:51:16.360Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:11.921Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93Q4JZ571ZGRTHZ3QXCYJQ\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Parser vs CLI layer disconnect: Meta includes were fully implemented in parser but CLI used wrong accessor (metaCtx.manifest.* vs metaCtx.*). This kind of bug suggests value in integration tests that exercise full stack, not just parser logic. Consider smoke tests for all CLI commands with complex scenarios.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:51:18.112Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:12.429Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93Q6BCQXGTJ7X4FAK13KVT\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Spec gap discovery during implementation: AC mentioned 'origin: observation_promotion' but origin field didn't exist in schema. Good example of spec-code drift. Consider: pre-implementation spec validation against schema, or schema-first approach where AC references must match existing schema fields.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:51:19.917Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:13.031Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93Q83M6RJ0YXH1H2H4F3TK\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"kspec-meta shadow branch divergence: Shadow branch has diverged significantly from remote (99 local vs 2 remote commits). Merge conflicts in sessions/ and modules/. May need manual reconciliation or a fresh sync strategy. Task changes are committed locally and functional.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:51:21.717Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:13.557Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93Q9S85XSBT1JVV1S1F9F3\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Type guards for union types: When narrowing AnyLoadedItem | LoadedMetaItem to LoadedTask, check for required properties that exist on Task but not on meta items. Use 'status' in item && 'depends_on' in item - NOT optional properties like closed_reason which won't exist on incomplete tasks.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:51:23.432Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:14.020Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94EZQT8WP107P6QV9ZC4JD\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review workflow pattern: Review subagents proved critical for catching issues before merge. Established pattern: (1) check for open PRs, (2) launch review subagent, (3) fix trivial issues directly, (4) re-review confirms fixes, (5) merge when checks pass. Works smoothly when changes are minor - automated review + fix + merge flow is efficient. Multi-step workflow (review→fix→merge→continue) provides good session continuity. Review caught real issues: reference matching bugs, TypeScript errors, duplicate PRs, missing tests. Self-review via subagent is valid for automation loops despite GitHub not allowing self-approval.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:04:19.579Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:14.432Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94F0W0BPTB5RP6FDWH63SM\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Incremental refactoring pattern: Large multi-iteration refactors work well when pattern is established early. Key lessons: (1) Create module first with comprehensive coverage, (2) Start with smallest files to establish pattern, (3) Commit incremental progress with clear 'what done/remains' tracking, (4) Use TodoWrite for sub-phases. String/error centralization phases showed this: early PRs for small wins, direct commits for established patterns. Tests catch issues early, smaller files build confidence. Having checkpoints and running totals (e.g., '179 of 201 = 89%') made continuation easy. This phased approach balances review overhead with execution speed.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:04:20.737Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:14.851Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94F20W3MKFPBA1XN0ABQ7P\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Implementation pattern (schema→parser→CLI→tests): New features follow clean path. Reuse agent command structure (formatTable, formatVerbose, JSON output via output()). Reference validation integration is clean - add to REF_FIELDS. Meta reference implementation was straightforward thanks to existing ReferenceIndex infrastructure. Pattern of implementing formatters first, then command registration works well. Testing is fast and reliable. Module add followed same pattern: validate inputs, create data, write file, update manifest, shadow commit. Could extract into reusable helper.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:04:21.916Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:15.326Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94FHX7C98EFRCSGAXAKBBR\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Reference implementation value: Checking prior work (../kspec-acp-test, ../kspec-ralph-test) before implementing saves significant design time. Found identical spec and working implementation providing clear blueprint. Prior work avoids edge cases and provides consistency. Explore subagents are valuable for understanding prior implementations - provided comprehensive details: file paths, schema patterns, CLI structure, test isolation challenges. Having parallel agent repos with prior work is highly valuable. Pattern: exploration as standard first step for implementation tasks.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:04:38.184Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:15.816Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94FK4G7W86NXDVTAZ77SK8\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task verification workflow: Some ready tasks are already implemented from prior sessions. Pattern: when starting task, verify current state by reading code, running tests, checking existing functionality before implementing. Saves time and avoids duplicate work. Meta commands (resolve, observe, promote, conventions) were already implemented but tasks remained pending. Need better sync between implementation status and task status - perhaps command to scan for already-implemented specs and auto-complete tasks. Consider 'verify implementation status' step especially for CLI commands.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:04:39.441Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:16.168Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94FMF9Y5VCS7EQXP4G2FRJ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Session/workflow patterns: Spike tasks with no code output don't need commits - value is in task notes documenting research. Shadow-only changes (task state updates) don't need main-branch PRs since shadow branch is source of truth. PR skill correctly detects no changes and exits cleanly for metadata-only tasks. PR workflow smooth with auto-generated branch names and /pr skill. Shadow CLI verification iteration showed pattern: pick task, verify implementation exists, complete task, no code changes needed.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:04:40.810Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:16.582Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94G1HYX2DCY796SKB9XB7P\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task guardrails and completion checks: Feature dogfooded successfully - tested on itself during completion. Interactive prompt provides immediate feedback about AC coverage ensuring implementations match specs. Implementation preserves spec status.maturity when updating implementation status (important pattern to avoid losing maturity context). Default to 'draft' if status doesn't exist yet.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:04:54.208Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:17.054Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94G2RY8JAX71K9BC8HJSF7\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Context and session integration: Meta focus command implementation straightforward thanks to well-structured SessionContext schema and existing loadSessionContext/saveSessionContext functions. Pattern of supporting show/set/clear modes in single command is clean and user-friendly. Auto-prepending @ to references maintains UX consistency. Context integration showed context BEFORE active work for immediate agent orientation - context is 'what thinking about' while active tasks are 'what doing'.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:04:55.454Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:17.500Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94G3YV75DYWZENYG19N9NX\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Review subagent catches real issues: Found validation strictness issue with RefSchema (too strict for manual files), TypeScript compilation errors, import path issues. Demonstrates value of code review even for simple changes. Pattern: when review finds flag conflicts or behavioral issues, fix includes both code AND spec updates. Renamed --verbose to --debug-shadow based on review finding conflict.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:04:56.668Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:17.832Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94GR1RQ0JXWNHD6RQGZ4SE\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Schema strictness value: ULID validation strictness caught real bugs - test fixtures had 24-char ULIDs passing because MetaUlidSchema was too lenient. Fixing schema to use UlidSchema forced proper fixture ULIDs. Important pattern: schema strictness prevents silent data corruption.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:05:17.241Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:18.266Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94GSM8KQP9QSQK47KT3J7X\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"JSON output helper pattern: output() provides clean separation between JSON and human-readable modes. Used successfully: return observation object in JSON mode, success message for human mode. Pattern: output(dataObject, () => humanFormatter()). Avoids duplicate/mixed output that happens with separate success() + output() calls.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:05:18.857Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:18.669Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94GV0DY58HXPVZJRQWBBAP\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"findChildItems path-based hierarchy: Implementation based on _path nesting worked well - path structure makes parent-child relationships explicit and easy to query. Similar pattern could be useful for other hierarchical queries: siblings, ancestors, tree depth.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:05:20.270Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:19.089Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94GWFGAHGPNM9HNCCESTSC\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Commander introspection for help: Commander's structure is stable and well-defined, making it reliable source of truth for help output. Consider applying to other CLI frameworks (Oclif, yargs). Separation of auto-generated syntax vs curated concepts is clean and maintainable.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:05:21.777Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:19.568Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94GXWR0CDRDG5GJ898XR24\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Command suggestion with Levenshtein: Feature implemented cleanly using Levenshtein distance. Threshold of 3 works well for catching typos without false positives. Commander.js already handles subcommand suggestions, so only needed top-level command handling.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:05:23.225Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:19.960Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94HCFSAD6WJ4PJG1T0SSY1\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Validation architecture scales: Adding warnings alongside errors required minimal changes - new type, updated return structure, simple CLI formatting. Separation of concerns (refs.ts for logic, validate.ts for orchestration, validate CLI for display) made enhancement straightforward. Pattern worth replicating: warnings as first-class citizens alongside errors.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:05:38.169Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:20.309Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94HDYHTGCMZCC6MMFYJGNJ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Spike workflow refinement: When completing spike, capture recommendation in closed_reason (brief) + final note (detailed). Spike task notes form mini research doc. Pattern: findings → analysis → recommendation. Example: task-archive spike documented current system, reviewed references, recommended MVP approach all in notes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:05:39.666Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:20.795Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94HFCXHSBAYMYXVTKRV3T8\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Convention validation foundation: Implementation validates convention schema. To be fully functional needs integration with actual content sources (git log for commits, task notes for note validation, etc.). Foundation is complete, content gathering is future enhancement.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:05:41.150Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:21.247Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94HGRMD0BF4524V3KQ8V2Q\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task origin field tracking: Added origin enum to track task creation source (manual, derived, observation_promotion). Could be extended for other sources like 'agent_suggestion', 'test_failure', 'lint_error'. Useful for metrics and understanding task flow.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:05:42.548Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:21.698Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF96T3VVQ8CTXQYQ4XNMTQ1W\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"Shadow branch PR workflow clarification: When work only updates shadow branch (.kspec/) metadata - task state, inbox items, notes - should PRs still be created? Ralph instructions say 'create PR after commit' but this seems intended for code changes on feature branches. Shadow changes track the work; code changes are the work output. Current behavior: skip PR when working tree is clean. Need clarification on whether meta manifest changes should follow different review process than code changes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:45:21.404Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:22.131Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF96T6E67ZB7FVJ8JEDBKTYS\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Iteration workflow patterns: (1) Verification-only iterations produce no commits - efficient, avoids code churn, skipping PR is correct when working tree clean. (2) Implementation vs verification task distinction - verification tasks are quick wins for automation loops, implementation tasks need focused sessions. (3) Iteration findings show shadow branch is source of truth for task state (git status on main shows clean after adding inbox items), session context can be stale. Pattern: prioritize verification in loops, save implementation for context-rich sessions.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:45:24.039Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:22.610Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF96TKTHJ8DNBGCTR8ACQ7DN\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review momentum: When reviewing own PRs from previous iterations, fix trivial issues directly (like invalid ULIDs) rather than leaving comments. Merge when checks pass unless changes are substantial. This keeps momentum going in automation loops.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:45:37.746Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:23.094Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF96TN2JQ4PPH7MW0G42MXBT\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"CLI label centralization: item.ts and inbox.ts had drifted from established src/strings/labels.ts pattern. Quick grep audit found inconsistencies. Fix was straightforward: import centralized labels and replace hardcoded strings. Pattern prevents drift: new commands should import from strings/ from the start.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:45:39.027Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:23.455Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF96TPK7BTRZ1XZ9BK5YD6G8\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Reference directory exploration: For spikes, launching dedicated Explore subagent for reference dirs (kspec-acp-test, kspec-ralph-test) prevents context bloat while getting comprehensive findings. Subagent found identical spec content across both test dirs. Pattern worked well - consider for other research tasks.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:45:40.584Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:23.878Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF96TQV69YX5RQKAJQDQ1S25\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Shadow CLI verification: Picked task from ready list, found all three commands (status, log, repair) already implemented with 43 passing tests. Verified functionality, completed task, updated spec alignment. No code changes needed. Key learning: spec items marked 'implemented' were accurate.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:45:41.863Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:24.454Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF96V5J1QJR44K8M7MMGFS0M\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Meta schema verification batch: Completed 8 meta-related tasks in single iteration by verifying existing schema implementations in src/schema/meta.ts. Pattern: start task, read schema file, verify fields match spec, document in notes, complete. Efficient for verification tasks when implementation already exists.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:45:55.906Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:24.860Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF96V6MZKAJC86KJD949CW8P\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Display-first implementation strategy: Many derived tasks for meta-spec features were already implemented. Schema layer and CLI display commands (meta show, meta agents, etc.) are complete. Gap is in interactive/mutation commands and validation integration. Pattern: display-first is pragmatic - read operations complete, write operations deferred. Allows early testing of schema design.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:45:57.023Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:25.443Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF96V82FAJANHX3P5GWEH8HQ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Convention schema test gap: Schema was already implemented but lacked test coverage. When picking up implementation tasks, check if code exists first - may just need tests or documentation rather than new code. Tests added brought coverage up to spec.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:45:58.480Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:25.758Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF96V9DF3FX5XH224TM996TE\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Session checkpoint hook value: Hook caught uncommitted .gitignore change. Important to follow never-commit-to-main rule - all changes should go through PRs. Hook successfully prevented incomplete session state.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:45:59.857Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:26.087Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF9WR7HTSHYCHSFKYFG31JSJ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel exploration agents gave comprehensive context quickly for documentation audit\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T01:08:48.314Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:26.540Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF9ZFAGH35RQG6J9BA20TM6E\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop iteration 1 completed successfully: merged PR #58 (meta thread), implemented and shipped meta question command as PR #63. Pattern replication from existing code (meta thread) worked perfectly - implementation and tests completed in single iteration with all tests passing.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T01:56:22.161Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:27.048Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA0DVCMDFM7QFDJQ2ZCY21G\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task descriptions with clear problem statements enable fast resolution - the ralph newline issue had a detailed description that made the fix obvious: just move console.log() before success() call. Spent <5 min from task start to fix complete.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T02:13:02.485Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:27.570Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA0S3X005NWJY3D8931BGP5\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Hook debugging methodology: For hook errors, test with synthetic inputs (valid JSON, invalid JSON, edge cases) to isolate root cause before fixing. The '2>&1' pattern in test commands reveals stderr leakage that wouldn't be visible in normal hook execution.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T02:19:11.648Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:28.048Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA0WGSE81VFMN080ARJEQHG\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task verification pattern successful: Check git history for related commits before implementing. Task @01KF9B4W was already completed in ff935fd - verification took <2 minutes, saved duplicate work.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T02:21:03.150Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:28.565Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA17QWT1KQJGG4J8E6ZT6AZ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Clear task scope led to clean implementation - 'ralph loop session save' was well-defined with obvious file naming (context-iter-N.json) and storage location (.kspec/sessions/{id}/). No ambiguity about what to build or where to put it. Good example of actionable task with minimal design decisions needed.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T02:27:10.874Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:28.966Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA1T2TD09TXAD8KHNAB0JFJ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Comprehensive design work captured entirely in task notes - created detailed analysis of agent-first CLI improvements with 5 key areas, phased implementation plan, and 5 follow-up inbox items. This design-in-notes pattern works well for planning tasks that inform future spec creation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T02:37:11.885Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:29.515Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA1T7F256DV5H7W73GG1V3C\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Shadow branch worktree was missing at iteration start - required manual 'git worktree add .kspec kspec-meta' then 'kspec shadow repair' to restore. This may be an environment issue (worktree cleanup?) or session isolation problem. Worth investigating why .kspec worktree disappeared between iterations.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T02:37:16.642Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:30.005Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA2BWD2KC305W3SBDYQR2DH\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Minimal viable implementation pattern works well: Started with complex task (subagent review workflow), scoped down to core value (review context command), shipped working feature in single iteration. Command provides immediate value for manual use while leaving door open for automation later. Design-first approach (notes documenting decisions) helped keep scope manageable.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T02:46:55.139Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:30.439Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA32BJBH3D2HY6ACYNJBNWA\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review subagent workflow worked effectively - launched dedicated review agent, identified missing test coverage and type safety issues, implemented fixes, verified all tests pass (555/556), merged with proper trailers. Review-fix-merge cycle completed in single iteration.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T02:59:11.564Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:30.782Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA380DVCVJT84GA2XNBRWY0\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Documentation-focused task worked well with todo tracking - broke down 5 documentation updates into clear steps, executed systematically, verified commands against CLI, completed all updates in single iteration with comprehensive commit message\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T03:02:16.764Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:31.185Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA3SBMD2507GB1TYZTN8G8R\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Smooth workflow on implementing kspec meta context - spec was clear, implementation straightforward, comprehensive test coverage added, all tests pass. The meta command family now has a unified context view that complements the individual management commands (focus, thread, question).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T03:11:45.294Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:31.619Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA4RFT8D2T2SW95A8ZK1JZE\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Shadow branch auto-commit workflow is seamless - created 5 spec items with ACs, all automatically committed without manual intervention. Task completion tracked properly across worktrees.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T03:28:45.385Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:32.212Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA4Y20RN7W6ZMG7ZNE1VE3E\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"ACs discovery pattern: Reading implementation code + corresponding tests provides complete picture of behaviors that need acceptance criteria. For @status-cascade, found 5 distinct behaviors (prompt shown, cascade accepted, cascade rejected, JSON mode, no children) by examining handleStatusCascade function and integration tests.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T03:31:47.864Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:32.655Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA599DH7QAR73HRWZMMWR5Z\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Efficient workflow iteration: picked task, analyzed code (Read tool), identified root cause (syncSpecImplementationStatus saves but doesn't commit), implemented minimal fix (2 identical changes in start/complete), verified with tests (561/561 pass), committed and created PR. Single-focus iteration completed in ~10 minutes of work.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T03:37:55.889Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:33.151Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA63VXRCMDNFNEVSNNHQ71M\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Tree view implementation was straightforward - used existing findChildItems pattern and _path property to build hierarchy. The box-drawing character approach (├──, └──, │) provides clear visual structure without complex dependencies. Integration with existing filters worked seamlessly because tree formatting happens at display layer, not query layer.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T03:52:26.808Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:33.546Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA6WBT1A8WRNQ4F7NM2KAFX\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR workflow smooth - auto-generated branch name from task slug (feat/add-priority-flag-to-derive), created branch from main with unpushed commit, reset main, pushed branch, created PR. The pattern of: checkout -b new-branch && git checkout main && git reset --hard origin/main && git checkout new-branch works cleanly for moving commits from main to a new branch.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T04:05:49.505Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:34.020Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA8C874AX1X3SDB2BZWC6AE\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task start spec context feature - clean DX improvement that follows existing patterns. Pattern: show context at point of action (when starting work), suppress in JSON mode, add test coverage with real fixtures. The alignment guidance string pattern in src/strings/guidance.ts is effective for maintaining consistent agent messaging.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T04:31:58.693Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:34.442Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA9KJ13NES8R3R26QESDS02\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test coverage tracking implementation demonstrates good separation of concerns - validation logic in parser/validate.ts, display logic in CLI commands. The AC annotation pattern (// AC: @spec-ref ac-N) provides simple traceability without complex tooling. Duplicating scanTestCoverage in task.ts is acceptable given the focused use case, though could be extracted to utils if pattern grows.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T04:53:26.691Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:34.910Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFA9N9FMZCAJAQNE97K479RF\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task state management across sessions: found task @01KF9G2X left in_progress from previous iteration. No built-in command to reset task to pending - only cancel (which marks it cancelled) or complete. Added note documenting state, but task remains in_progress. Consider adding 'kspec task reset' or 'kspec task stop' command to move tasks back to pending when abandoned mid-work.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T04:54:23.476Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:35.387Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAA0XW7PHR9EWXEP3HR1HR7\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Iteration 16 handled two tasks effectively: completed test coverage tracking (my primary work) and discovered/completed abandoned WIP for spec item notes (3 WIP commits from previous session). The spec item notes feature was nearly complete - just needed commits. This demonstrates good cross-session continuity when WIP is properly committed with clear messages.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T05:00:44.808Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:35.760Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAAC1AYM45CE8B8MDWGJ4GW\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Reusing NoteSchema across both tasks and spec items worked perfectly - no code duplication, consistent behavior, and symmetric CLI commands. The pattern of import { NoteSchema } from './task.js' into spec.ts demonstrates good schema reuse.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T05:06:48.798Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:36.184Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFABRSMHWD0Q33800AX7TYSS\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review workflow worked well: subagent found TypeScript compilation errors (missing imports), implemented fix directly on feature branch, verified with tests, then merged. Clean separation between review agent and implementation agent.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T05:31:15.473Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:36.709Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFABRY971XP4KD8D3198R2KT\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Spec-first workflow for schema changes: Updated @maturity-states spec with new 'deferred' status and added ACs before implementing in schema. This ensures spec remains source of truth and provides clear acceptance criteria for implementation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T05:31:20.231Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:37.258Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFADNW4SYG78Y13M8KHXAR92\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Auto-generating implementation notes from specs during derive significantly streamlines the spec-first workflow. Rather than requiring manual 'kspec task note' after derive, the context is automatically captured. This reduces cognitive load and ensures implementation context isn't lost. The pattern of using spec description + AC summary provides exactly the right level of detail for implementation reference.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T06:04:36.889Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:37.742Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFADRNQN3SG8FMZF3EMWHF6N\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"INSTALL.md creation went smoothly - clear task description made it easy to know what to write. Agent-focused documentation should always have: concise commands, copy-pasteable snippets, clear success criteria after each section, troubleshooting for common gotchas.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T06:06:08.629Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:38.272Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAEFD4XYVVXH61FNA9HWHGT\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review workflow with subagent worked smoothly. The review subagent provided detailed analysis covering code quality, test coverage, task/spec alignment, and commit conventions. Decision tree in RALPH_LOOP_INSTRUCTIONS.md made merge decision clear. Merged PR #75, then picked next task and completed docs work. Clean iteration from review → merge → new work → PR.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T06:18:33.501Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:38.692Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAF48W58CCFZBC0DBGCCK21\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Git worktrees use hooks from main .git/hooks (via commondir), not from .git/worktrees/-kspec/hooks. This is a key architectural detail that wasn't obvious from git documentation. Testing revealed the issue when hooks weren't being called. The commondir file points to '../..' which makes git look for hooks in the main repo.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T06:29:57.253Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:39.120Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAFEAADJPTN5ZRHK0PDYGJY\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Small DX improvements (like setup:dev script) have high impact for low effort. Pattern: when you find yourself documenting a multi-step setup process, consider if it can be a single script instead.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T06:35:26.413Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:39.559Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAGYE5VYH1YSNS7ZD4R20BX\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Shadow branch worktree repair workflow issues: (1) Nested .kspec/.kspec directories created by repeated git worktree add commands, (2) Commands that navigate into .kspec (cd .kspec && ...) fail when already in subdirectory, causing directory confusion, (3) Git worktree metadata (/.git/worktrees) can become desynchronized from actual directory state, (4) kspec shadow repair command failed with 'spawn /bin/sh ENOENT' error. Resolution required: manual git worktree prune, removal of nested directories, and manual git operations in worktree with KSPEC_SHADOW_COMMIT=1 to bypass hook. Consider: (a) More robust worktree repair that handles nested directories, (b) Better error messages showing current directory context, (c) Idempotent repair commands that check current state before operations.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T07:01:43.227Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:40.049Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAH2B2H0P3ZZRXMKY7F35BV\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Completed full task cycle in iteration 25: merged open PR, resolved shadow branch sync issues, picked and completed task @01KFAB9B, committed work, created PR #80. The worktree friction observation captured detailed troubleshooting context for future improvements. Task completion workflow worked smoothly once shadow branch was synchronized.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T07:03:51.122Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:40.632Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAHKB1REKZMA6EP9HM7J1FZ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Integration test strategy: Using command JSON output directly from promote command instead of querying tasks list afterward provides more accurate, focused tests and avoids format parsing issues. The promote command returns the created task in its JSON output, which is exactly what we need to verify.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T07:13:08.152Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:41.043Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAJSS392ZV47Z373HK29HAM\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Batch operation pattern scales well - created reusable executeBatchOperation() utility that handles all common concerns (mutual exclusion, partial failures, output formatting). Applied to 3 commands (complete, cancel, delete) with minimal duplication. Pattern: extract single-item logic into executeOperation callback, utility handles iteration/error collection. Makes adding batch support to new commands straightforward.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T07:34:07.722Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:41.409Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAM6VF2MY7QKC526SZX8PY8\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test-first debugging pattern worked excellently for batch operations\\n\\nThe PR review subagent identified a critical bug: resolveTaskRef() called process.exit() \\ninstead of returning errors, breaking partial failure handling.\\n\\nThe fix process was clean:\\n1. Review identified the bug with clear evidence\\n2. Created batch-compatible resolver that returns {task, error}\\n3. Updated batch.ts to expect new format\\n4. All existing tests passed (no regression)\\n5. Added 9 new tests covering all 8 ACs\\n6. Tests caught edge cases (ambiguous ULID prefixes)\\n\\nKey insight: When refactoring error handling, create new functions instead of modifying\\nexisting ones. The original resolveTaskRef() serves single-ref commands that should exit\\non error. The new resolveTaskRefForBatch() serves batch commands that should continue.\\n\\nThis separation of concerns made the fix safe and testable.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T07:58:44.706Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:41.783Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFANADZJA4VAFBSH0F8FAWXP\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Test observation from Ralph Loop\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T08:18:10.546Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:42.284Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAND9RY95MCTPE02QB9103E\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Iteration 29 workflow was efficient and clean: picked highest priority task, implemented feature with comprehensive tests (5 tests covering all AC), manual testing verified functionality, PR created. The --from-inbox flag for meta observe enables bucket correction during triage - items captured in wrong bucket can be easily converted.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T08:19:44.542Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:42.833Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAPKVHCJGKTVM1690P8P8CF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Passthrough args implementation pattern - When adding passthrough args to CLI commands that normally parse output, create separate raw output path. Trying to parse structured output with custom format flags breaks. Used searchCommitsRaw() for raw git output when passthroughArgs.length > 0, avoiding format conflicts.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T08:40:47.917Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:43.177Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAPWQVB7K0DV4ZK6TDRJMM2\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review and merge workflow worked smoothly. Dedicated review subagent provided comprehensive analysis covering code quality, test coverage, and spec alignment. Clear APPROVE recommendation made merge decision straightforward. This validates the review-before-merge pattern in RALPH_LOOP_INSTRUCTIONS.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T08:45:39.051Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:43.493Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAQN66S95434T70FPXES77X\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Implemented kspec setup worktree detection cleanly by leveraging existing shadow module utilities. The repairShadow() function already handled the complex worktree creation logic, so implementation was primarily about adding the detection and prompting layer. This demonstrates the value of the shadow module's well-factored utilities for worktree management.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T08:59:00.185Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:43.850Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFARJ6TDYJFKS5EP5XAJB89W\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Bulk refactoring pattern: Created automated script to replace magic numbers with constants across 18+ files. This approach was much faster than manual edits and ensured consistency. The script handled the mechanical replacements, then manual fixes addressed edge cases (import paths). This pattern is reusable for similar bulk refactoring tasks (e.g., error message standardization, import path updates).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T09:14:51.085Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:44.386Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFATCXG9439H99JN0KK8SV71\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Multi-round PR review with dedicated subagents worked extremely well. Pattern: (1) Launch review subagent after PR created (2) Review finds issues (3) Fix issues (4) Launch new review subagent (5) Repeat until clean (6) Merge. This approach caught all CONFLICT exit code inconsistencies through 3 fix iterations before merge. The independent review prevented merging incomplete work. Key: each review cycle provides fresh perspective and catches missed cases.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T09:46:54.857Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:44.886Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFATQ46A835BQ657YX7AC853\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Implementing features with clear acceptance criteria is much faster than without. The @stale-status-detection spec had 5 well-defined ACs that mapped directly to implementation steps. AC format (Given/When/Then) made it easy to verify each scenario. Spent more time fixing type issues than implementing logic. Key learning: read schema thoroughly first to understand data structures before writing validation logic.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T09:52:29.386Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:45.251Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFATS86AMESWQJA9E1T2JCVM\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Staleness detection implementation completed successfully. The feature detects status inconsistencies between specs and tasks, with 3 key checks: task dependencies completed but task pending, spec implemented without tasks, and task completed but spec not started. All tests pass.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T09:53:39.018Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:45.817Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFATSF5A7KEEY4CHSKTCFG4G\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Found task in progress but work already committed. This may happen when: (1) previous iteration completed but didn't mark task complete, (2) concurrent work from another process, or (3) git operations completed before kspec state sync. Consider adding 'kspec shadow sync' at session start to ensure state is current.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T09:53:46.155Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:46.180Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFATSKF22KHRZYCQ0TJP1P1E\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Complete iteration workflow: (1) Check open PRs and review/merge, (2) Pick highest priority ready task, (3) Implement with clear ACs, (4) Manual test verification, (5) Commit with task/spec trailers, (6) Create PR. This pattern ensures no work is left in limbo - PRs are either merged or created by end of iteration. The /pr skill makes PR creation seamless.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T09:53:50.562Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:46.720Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFATTDS4G9VHDXXF4DDHS1C2\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Iteration 34 outcome: Merged 1 PR (semantic exit codes with 4 commits), implemented and shipped stale status detection (3 commits, PR #88 created). Multi-round review pattern prevented incomplete merges. Every iteration should end with either merged PRs or new PRs created - no work left uncommitted or unpushed. This keeps the project moving forward consistently.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T09:54:17.508Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:47.283Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAVMTHF0KRC1YKH8QMF1W9W\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Global --json mode interactions complicate command-specific JSON output. Commands that want to output simple JSON (like {path, branch}) end up wrapped in {success, ...} objects or interfere with git stderr. Consider: (1) per-command JSON output control, (2) dedicated JSON output stream, or (3) convention that commands bypass global mode for simple output.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T10:08:42.543Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:47.870Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAVYRDBQYJEAK4Z8E5QMQXA\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task was cancelled prematurely by automation (01KEZ9DSD3). The automation cancelled the task after initial investigation notes, but actual implementation work was completed successfully. The code changes were made and tested, but the task was marked as cancelled before completion could be recorded. This suggests the automation may be too aggressive in cancelling tasks that appear to be in research/investigation phase.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T10:14:08.043Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:48.302Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAVYYD7GKN0VXBP67B4CR8G\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Successfully improved YAML formatting consistency by switching from js-yaml to modern 'yaml' library. The new implementation provides deterministic formatting that won't randomly change between saves, addressing the core DX issue. While not preserving exact original formatting/comments, this is a pragmatic solution that significantly improves the developer experience without requiring complex CST manipulation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T10:14:14.183Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:48.734Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAY1AB5CT6KEJ2J9NY37WQX\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Complete YAML library migration completed successfully. Initial implementation had critical bug (timestamps round-tripping as Date objects), but review subagent caught it before merge. Fixed by migrating both read and write operations to yaml library. PR reviewed, fixed, and merged in same iteration. This demonstrates the value of: (1) Launching review subagents for own PRs, (2) Acting on review feedback immediately, (3) Complete testing before declaring done.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T10:50:29.093Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:49.163Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAY1FS7QHBMV350A899878F\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task automation cancelled 01KEZ9DSD3 prematurely during investigation phase, but work was actually completed. The automation should be more lenient with tasks in early research/investigation phases, or have a way to detect when implementation is actually progressing even if lots of notes are being added.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T10:50:34.663Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:49.658Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAY281BQT8BGFP3YRF6SYXF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Full iteration workflow executed successfully: Task pickup → Implementation → PR creation → Review subagent finds bug → Fix implementation → Re-review → Merge. The review-before-merge workflow prevented a production bug. Total time: ~40 minutes for complete feature delivery including bug fix.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T10:50:59.500Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:50.042Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAY7NM46JVAJ0JAKEDHAH0C\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Research spikes captured in task notes provide durable artifacts. Task 01KF9G22 demonstrates pattern: comprehensive research findings documented directly in notes, preserving context even when temporary files (scratchpad) don't persist. Notes become the source of truth for future spec/task creation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T10:53:57.252Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:50.446Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFAY7ZXQ0P119X3S9N42KZVW\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task 01KF9G22 was cancelled in previous iteration but appeared in ready_tasks list. When attempted to complete after adding research notes, got error 'Cannot complete task with status: cancelled'. The ready_tasks filter should exclude cancelled tasks, or there should be a way to reopen/uncancell tasks that get picked up again.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T10:54:07.799Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:50.887Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFC3BCB8B8F2GXW0GGNCNRT4\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"Bulk import design question: What makes it 'work well'? The cancelled @task-bulk-import had a design for simplified YAML input. Challenges identified: format flexibility vs strictness, error handling mid-import, preview accuracy, integration with existing workflows. What's the core use case - rapid spec capture during design? Plan-to-spec translation? Importing from external sources?\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T21:42:36.136Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Resolved via batch JSON approach: Generic kspec batch command accepts JSON array of CLI args. Skills handle translation from flexible input to batch JSON. See inbox 01KFC3SV.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T21:50:38.514Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFC3BM2YJSZ56MFSS8MA8WM6\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Plan mode required multiple back-and-forth cycles. Missing upfront: output type (spec vs code), standalone requirements check, display/UX needs. Review subagent ran AFTER trying to exit plan mode instead of as a step before finalizing. Suggests plan mode needs structured phases or checklist.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T21:42:44.062Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFC3BVA0WNT6FV2B74DY270A\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Subagent review of spec caught 3 blocking issues (AC collision, undefined JSON structure, display contradiction) that would have caused implementation problems. Pattern: review specs with critical eye before finalizing, not just for completeness but for internal consistency and edge cases.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T21:42:51.457Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFC3C23Q4DX7APJEXFEKY1FN\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task notes template for standalone implementation context worked well: Scope (what this task covers), Prerequisites (dependencies), Files (to modify/create), Patterns (code examples), Tests (where to add). Prevents 'see parent for context' band-aids.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-19T21:42:58.423Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCPF1T45VEVDP6PHNY9D6SC\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Exit code fixes completed efficiently using TodoWrite to track all 6 individual changes. The todo list helped ensure no fixes were missed and provided clear progress visibility through the task.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T03:16:39.364Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCQ0SQ1RJ3HTD5FBE2N90RA\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR workflow (#96 → #97) demonstrates smooth iteration loop: review existing PR → merge → pick next task → implement → submit → create PR. The pending_review state effectively gates work and ensures each PR gets proper review before merge. Task @01KFC1GKG scope was well-defined (foundation only) which made it easy to complete in one iteration.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T03:26:20.898Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCQZKW4NF7Z3BA49P9NGQHF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review workflow with dedicated subagent worked well - caught missing test coverage before merge. Strict review guidelines (AC coverage required, no fluff tests, E2E preferred) ensure quality standards are maintained across iterations.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T03:43:10.724Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCR87QM94J4S6CKYCV9Z1B3\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"YAML migration task was straightforward - clear scope, no dependencies, simple find-replace pattern. This type of refactoring task is ideal for automation: well-defined changes, easy to verify with tests, low risk.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T03:47:53.205Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCS35ZYSCC5209668HWBZDA\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test-first debugging workflow effective: Added debug output to failing tests to identify root cause (invalid ULID format), then fixed and removed debug code. Faster than guessing.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T04:02:36.159Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCSQFV6TA8SM8ZPKNVHK09T\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Traits field validation implementation followed clean pattern from existing ref validation. Adding to REF_FIELDS array and extending validateRefs() was straightforward. The test pattern from parser.test.ts made writing comprehensive tests easy. All 5 ACs covered in 6 tests.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T04:13:41.606Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCTE16XZGRDSEGMFFZFWTJ3\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop PR review workflow proved effective: dedicated review subagent correctly identified missing E2E tests as BLOCKING issue, prompted fix, re-review confirmed resolution, and merge completed successfully. The strict review criteria (AC coverage, E2E priority, test isolation) caught important gaps before merge.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T04:26:00.285Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCTR3VVRA9ECADDRDYEGPMR\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Following established code patterns (ReferenceIndex, AlignmentIndex) made TraitIndex implementation straightforward. The bidirectional mapping pattern and constructor-based indexing approach worked well for trait-spec relationships. Test structure with AC annotations provides clear traceability.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T04:31:30.684Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCVFM07FH8DHYPV3AA3TTJ8\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Trait display implementation completed efficiently by reusing TraitIndex foundation. Integrating into buildIndexes() made trait data available throughout CLI. Text and JSON output handled cleanly with separate formatting logic. Test fixtures required valid ULIDs - good validation caught this early.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T04:44:20.872Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCW3TDDPB6G1G8DFS10NAEE\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"ULID validation in tests requires Crockford base32 alphabet (excludes I, L, O, U). Common test ULID patterns like 01TRAIT10... or 01TASK10... are invalid because they contain 'I'. Should document this in test helpers or provide a utility function that generates valid test ULIDs with readable prefixes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T04:55:22.797Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Added testUlid() helper function to tests/helpers/cli.ts that generates valid Crockford base32 ULIDs. Also added documentation at top of file explaining ULID character restrictions (no I, L, O, U). Example: testUlid('TASK') produces valid '01TASK00000000000000000000' - invalid chars are auto-replaced.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-22T19:37:28.386Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCWZ8SEY6Z49V14D2X73ZGE\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"loadSpecFile() only parsed first YAML document when multiple documents present (--- separators). Root cause: YAML.parse() vs YAML.parseAllDocuments(). This broke tests that appended traits to files using document separators. Fix was straightforward once identified, but debugging took time because manual tests worked (single document) while multi-document tests failed silently.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T05:10:22.255Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"This was a code bug that was fixed. loadSpecFile() now correctly uses YAML.parseAllDocuments() for multi-document files.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-22T19:37:51.390Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCX5DYS83R2SYQ1SNCNY03P\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Systematic debugging approach: When implementation code looks correct but tests fail, investigate test infrastructure first. Created isolated debug scripts to replicate exact test scenario, which revealed YAML parser only reading first document. This pattern of creating minimal reproduction scripts in scratchpad is valuable for debugging test failures.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T05:13:44.153Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCXGBQSPN7XYPRTV625E1TZ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Trait AC coverage validation implementation went smoothly by building on existing infrastructure. The TraitIndex and checkCompleteness() architecture made it straightforward to add inherited AC checking - just scan trait ACs the same way we scan direct ACs. The existing test coverage scanning and ref validation already handled most of the heavy lifting. Clean separation of concerns paid off.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T05:19:42.330Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCXQH9GZ4330JWEHD9QVXVT\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review workflow caught test quality issues before merge - the automated subagent review identified fluff tests and missing documentation that would have degraded test quality patterns in the codebase. The strict review criteria (MUST-FIX vs suggestions) worked well.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T05:23:37.393Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCXY2PK61MY006C48874R44\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Full PR review → fix → merge cycle completed successfully in one iteration. The Ralph Loop workflow of dedicating review subagent, fixing issues, waiting for CI, and merging is working smoothly. Key: strict review criteria and blocking on CI checks before merge.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T05:27:11.828Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCXYZYP9E8CJMRS7TJMW29G\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"CI checks can take 3-4 minutes to complete, which can consume a significant portion of an iteration when waiting for merge approval. Consider: (1) Starting CI early if possible, (2) Using wait time productively for reflection/documentation, (3) Maybe implementing a timeout strategy in Ralph Loop for when CI takes too long.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T05:27:41.782Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCYH1P91QYPT0Q1WKW9JJZE\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Trait CLI implementation followed clean separation: parser infrastructure (TYPE_TO_CHILD_FIELD, NESTED_ITEM_FIELDS) before CLI commands. This pattern worked well - infrastructure changes enabled CLI to use existing patterns (addChildItem, buildIndexes) without special cases. E2E tests caught integration issues early (traits not loading from manifest).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T05:37:33.385Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCZ3SHZSW2RDA6CCNTAPE5W\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"trait-cli tests fail in vitest despite implementation working correctly in manual testing. All 12 failing tests involve trait list/get/item commands. Manual replication of exact test scenarios works perfectly. Tests use same CLI dist files. Issue is test infrastructure related, not implementation. Need to investigate vitest test execution environment differences.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T05:47:47.647Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"This was a test infrastructure issue that was resolved. Trait CLI tests now pass.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-22T19:37:56.472Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFCZ4SK76NHJM1N4YT2RHS4Y\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Used dedicated review subagent to identify critical schema bug in PR #104. The subagent's strict review caught that ManifestSchema was missing the traits field, causing Zod to strip traits during parsing. This was a blocking bug that made all functionality fail. Fixed the issue and verified through extensive manual testing. Pattern: Always use review subagents before merge, they catch bugs that aren't obvious from code inspection alone.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T05:48:20.455Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFD0A2TX3WZFG6RQMN45Y8CR\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Test fixture anti-patterns found: (1) Naive YAML string manipulation breaks structure - use CLI commands or proper YAML parsers instead. (2) Tests creating invalid kspec structures - spec items must be nested under module items in type-specific fields. (3) Slug collisions with existing fixtures - tests need unique identifiers. (4) Missing test dependencies - tests assuming entities exist without creating them. These issues compound and hide real implementation bugs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T06:08:42.334Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Added documentation to tests/helpers/cli.ts header explaining: (1) Don't use JSON.stringify for YAML fixtures (2) Use setupTempFixtures() with pre-built fixtures (preferred) (3) Write YAML strings directly with template literals (4) Use yaml library stringify for programmatic creation. Also added testUlid() helper to avoid invalid ULID issues.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-22T19:37:35.380Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFD0A8HPBCD40WAZSF3GMZRX\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Systematic test debugging approach worked well: (1) Run tests to see failures, (2) Isolate root cause through manual reproduction, (3) Fix fixtures to match actual kspec requirements, (4) Verify all tests pass. Using manual CLI invocations in temp dirs helped identify structural issues that weren't obvious from test code alone.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T06:08:48.182Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFD0DWVHZJSMHVAQY11HFPEF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review feedback loop worked well: (1) Subagent identified test quality issues with clear MUST-FIX verdict, (2) Systematic debugging traced root causes (YAML structure, slug conflicts, missing deps), (3) Fixed all 12 test failures, (4) All 695 tests pass locally, (5) PR updated and CI re-running. The strict review criteria (E2E tests, temp dirs, AC coverage, no fluff) ensured high quality implementation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T06:10:47.281Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFD0VXY441EVBG6HA85HNYBT\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Merged PR #104 (trait CLI commands) successfully. Review subagent found 0 blocking issues, 100% AC coverage (8/8), all tests passing. Production-quality implementation with proper isolation and AC annotations.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T06:18:27.140Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFD15XE0W20ZA8M475J43TKY\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Test-driven development revealed implementation bugs in trait edge case handling. AC-2 (cycle detection) and AC-3 (broken ref detection) both show validation passing when should fail. This pattern (write tests → discover implementation incomplete) is good but slows progress when implementation gaps are large. Consider: (1) Review implementation completeness before writing E2E tests (2) Add unit tests for validation logic first (3) Use TDD for new features but integration-test existing features differently\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T06:23:54.304Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"This is expected TDD behavior - discovering implementation gaps through tests is part of the process. Not a problem to fix but a useful pattern to be aware of.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-22T19:38:07.580Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFD1TCR2MSTXEQE6TJD3ETG7\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Bug investigation pattern: When validation passes unexpectedly, check item counts in output. 'Items checked: 3' vs expected 5 revealed traits weren't being loaded. Count mismatches are powerful debugging signals for data loading issues.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T06:35:05.346Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFD2G0RJ53P1Z0YQWBTF7WEM\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Testing git operations in isolated test environments - git clone --mirror fails in vitest with 'repository does not exist' despite source repo being properly initialized with commits. Same commands work when run manually. May be related to how vitest sandboxes processes or handles child_process spawn. Need to investigate if this is a PATH issue, git config issue, or test isolation problem. This pattern will affect any future commands that need to test git cloning or repository manipulation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T06:46:53.970Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Known vitest environment issue. initGitRepo() helper handles basic git setup. Complex git cloning scenarios may need simpler approaches in tests.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-22T19:38:01.946Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFD2YKYFJ9WB1EX5R8D38WD1\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test helper pattern clarity - integration.test.ts showed the correct pattern of importing kspecOutput as kspec for string output. When tests fail due to type mismatches (expecting string, getting object), check imports against working test files.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T06:54:52.367Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFD2YSFK15FSYZC7X4J9GPX3\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Optional positional parameter order in CLI commands can create usability issues. [source] [dest] signature made it impossible to provide dest and default source. Changed to [dest] [source] which better matches common usage patterns. Consider: use named options (--source, --dest) for commands where both parameters are truly optional and order-independent.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T06:54:58.035Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFD2YYTAEEPDQ6CA3P6WSJ9H\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Systematic debugging approach worked well: (1) Verified git clone works standalone, (2) Added debug output to trace actual parameters, (3) Discovered output was empty not error, (4) Checked test helper return types, (5) Found pattern in working tests. Each step narrowed the problem space until root cause was clear.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T06:55:03.498Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFDPKZC956WTYA4BA7Q7SDQB\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Shadow branch worktree gets removed when checking out branches. After merging PR and checking out main, .kspec/ worktree was removed. Attempting to recreate with 'git worktree add .kspec kspec-meta' created nested .kspec/.kspec/ worktree breaking kspec. Fix required absolute paths and manual cleanup. Root cause: git worktree add interprets paths relative to CWD which may be inside .kspec. Consider: (1) kspec commands that detect missing worktree and auto-repair (2) fix spawn error in 'kspec shadow repair' (3) prevent nested worktree creation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T12:38:35.146Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFDPM7VF7ZGE02MCP3JB7131\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph Loop iteration completed successfully: (1) Checked for open PRs per instructions (2) Found PR #106 with failing tests (7/8) (3) Launched review subagent to identify issues (4) Fixed all 3 blocking issues (worktree metadata cleanup, test setup, helper usage) (5) Verified locally (8/8 tests + full suite 707 passing) (6) Pushed and waited for CI (all green) (7) Merged PR and completed task @01KFBBTT (8) Captured 4 observations. Full workflow from PR review to merge completion in single iteration.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T12:38:43.824Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFDZBXCJQWP1CHC0277JAA0V\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Completed first task in spec review sequence (@01KFDYAW). Simple cleanup task (removing non-existent file reference) was straightforward. Shadow branch auto-commit worked correctly - no manual commit needed for .kspec/ changes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:11:28.146Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFDZC1RFZFR8FEHBFCEQ9S7G\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Easy to accidentally stay in .kspec/ directory after checking git log and then run kspec commands, which fail. The error message is clear ('Cannot run kspec from inside .kspec/ directory'), but would be better to avoid this by being more careful about pwd or using absolute paths.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:11:32.624Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Documented in AGENTS.md 'Important: Always Run from Project Root' section with troubleshooting guidance\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T05:13:29.247Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFDZGT05N02FNX2HXM4CRT8H\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"E2E validation workflow effective for confirming system readiness. Created test data, verified behavior, cleaned up - all within single iteration. Trait system confirmed production-ready without needing to create permanent test fixtures.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:14:08.518Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFDZVK4MA028H031BR26YZCE\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Manually editing .kspec/kynetic.yaml to add traits requires:\\n1. Understanding ULID format constraints (no I, L, O, U chars)\\n2. Manually generating valid ULIDs\\n3. Working around shadow branch auto-commit restrictions\\n\\nThe kspec trait add command would have handled all this, but for bulk creation of 8 traits with detailed AC, manual YAML editing was more practical. Future improvement: support adding AC during trait creation, or bulk trait import from YAML file.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:20:01.941Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFDZVT1Z2HBAY7D8T3M1JEE2\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Debugging approach for YAML loading issues:\\n1. Used node scripts to test individual components (initContext, extractItemsFromRaw, SpecItemSchema)\\n2. Isolated the failure point (ULID validation regex)\\n3. This incremental debugging approach was much faster than adding console.logs to source code\\n\\nPattern to remember: when kspec commands don't work as expected, test the parser/schema layers directly with minimal scripts.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:20:09.024Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFE03DTPTD76XA5J8DH6H5KM\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Systematic AC addition workflow worked efficiently: grouped items by category (schema types, task types, relationships, YAML), added 2 AC per item following given/when/then format. Pattern: each AC should test a specific aspect of the item's behavior. For type definitions, one AC validates structure and one validates usage/purpose.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:24:18.647Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFE0E736KWBTZDRA1M01W1W8\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Shadow branch auto-commit pattern works seamlessly for spec changes. Modified cli.yaml (spec file) and all changes were automatically committed to shadow branch via kspec commands (task note, task complete). No manual git operations needed. This confirms the design - spec changes live in shadow branch, auto-committed by CLI.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:30:12.199Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFE0EM48X85MQSJDCJJMDWPR\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Trait application pattern for CLI commands: (1) All commands get json-output, semantic-exit-codes, error-guidance. (2) Batch operations add multi-ref-batch. (3) Destructive operations add confirmation-prompt. Applied consistently to 7 task lifecycle commands. Pattern is clear and repeatable for remaining commands.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:30:25.545Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFE0RJTKJG04MGEVZ5NFJZ6G\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Shadow branch auto-commit workflow: File changes made via Edit tool are automatically committed when kspec commands (like task note) run. No manual git add/commit needed for shadow-tracked files. This is the expected behavior and works well.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:35:51.892Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFE0RS0XE3AYATECAMNNPN2X\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Directory context confusion: When running git/bash commands that cd into .kspec, subsequent kspec commands fail with 'Cannot run from .kspec directory'. Need to be explicit about returning to project root or use absolute paths. Mitigated by using 'cd /absolute/path && command' pattern.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:35:58.237Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Documented in AGENTS.md - use absolute paths or check pwd before kspec commands\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T05:13:31.492Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFE13K905B3263M48Y7Z4M19\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Spec review task series completed efficiently. Breaking down large spec updates into 7 focused tasks (trait creation, AC addition, trait application by command category) enabled systematic progress tracking and validation at each step. TodoWrite tool helped track progress within each task.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:41:52.801Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFE13RKXKERPMTNPY7PJHGJN\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Working directory confusion: Agent tools (Read, Edit, etc.) can change working directory during exploration, but this isn't always obvious. When pwd shows .kspec/, kspec commands fail. Need to be more aware of current directory before running kspec commands. Pattern: always use absolute paths or check pwd before kspec commands.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:41:58.270Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Documented in AGENTS.md 'Important: Always Run from Project Root' section\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T05:13:34.013Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFE1BE12S5W2TCJAC1K6DN1E\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Fixed spec-implementation mismatch by updating the spec to match working implementation. Key insight: When spec and implementation diverge, evaluate which is more useful before blindly 'fixing' code to match spec. In this case, task dependency checking was more actionable than spec hierarchy checking, so updating the spec was the right choice. The tests validated that the implementation was correct for what it does.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:46:09.570Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFE1BKDZXAFHWFZE855VF9HR\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Working directory kept changing to .kspec/ during the session, requiring multiple 'cd ..' commands. This happens when reading files in .kspec/ or checking git status. Should be more mindful of pwd before running kspec commands, or establish a pattern of always returning to project root after .kspec/ operations.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-20T15:46:15.104Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Documented in AGENTS.md - always return to project root after .kspec/ operations\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T05:13:36.432Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFEYT39MFQGBH9YY7K8GSH8K\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Subagent review of specs before implementation caught 4 missing ACs and 2 missing flag behaviors. Worth doing for non-trivial specs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T00:20:58.804Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFEYT8CH48P6B4WGKTCM7627\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Breaking monolithic feature into requirements before deriving tasks produces self-contained tasks with proper dependencies. One feature with 14 ACs became 4 requirements with 4-6 ACs each.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T00:21:04.018Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFEZ86NHX1SYXX38DJBN44A8\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Spec-plan session validated guided workflow design - the manual process of creating the guided-workflow-execution spec followed exactly the pattern the feature would automate: requirements → exploration → design → review → spec creation → derive. Dogfooding opportunity once implemented.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T00:28:41.009Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFM7NAN2GW0BEXX6JZR5MV5\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task reset implementation went smoothly. Following existing patterns from task.ts (cancel, complete, block) made implementation straightforward. Comprehensive test coverage (15 tests for 6 ACs) caught no issues. Shadow commit verification simplified by trusting commitIfShadow success rather than parsing git internals. All 783 tests pass on first try.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T06:35:23.349Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFMRZ746PMVGB00TDS532GR\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task scoping from retrospective notes works well - the task notes from the ralph loop retrospective provided clear, actionable improvements that translated directly into implementation steps.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T06:44:50.533Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFMS3G3EZ6PGSN7DV8WGJ76\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR CI waiting pattern - when CI is pending on a PR, better to move to next task rather than blocking iteration. The PR will be picked up in a future iteration once CI completes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T06:44:54.915Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFN7TYV4VEBM6J47RWDRQYV\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review workflow validated: spawned subagent for strict review before merge, identified blocking issues (spec field name mismatch, fluff test), fixed them, then merged. Review agent correctly flagged AC-5 test as not validating its criterion.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T06:52:57.691Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFN7ZAX6FD7G6EC21N9M15X\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Merged PR #114 before pushing fix commit (66010b6) that addressed review feedback. Had to create new PR #115 with the fixes. Should push all commits before merging PR.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T06:53:02.174Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Historical incident - lesson learned: always verify fix commits are pushed before merging PR\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T05:13:41.217Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFN83NCYJACXVPC2A0EA0RZ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test improvement strategy: AC-5 test was fluff (admitted in comments it didn't test the scenario). Rewrote to actually set up dependency scenario and validate via tasks ready command. Understanding how dependency checking works (at query time, not start time) was key to writing correct test.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T06:53:06.604Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFP5DB5QDZT8HR91XN8C7SQ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"CI workflow implementation pattern: GitHub Actions with github-script action provides clean GraphQL API integration without custom tooling. For review thread resolution checks, the isResolved and isOutdated fields are exactly what's needed - filtering for \\\\!isResolved && \\\\!isOutdated gives accurate results. Excluding outdated threads prevents false positives from force-pushed commits.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T07:09:06.789Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFPWAAGAH865DKPYBR5W63E\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"CI workflow implementation was already partially complete from previous session - checking git status and existing files before starting work prevented duplicate effort. The workflow uses GitHub GraphQL API to query review thread resolution status, which is more robust than REST API approach for checking unresolved comments.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T07:21:37.360Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFPWFJXA1Y2ZFA3FG4BJAN1\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop PR workflow is working well: started iteration by checking for open PRs, reviewed and merged PR #115 (fixing spec trailers), then picked next priority task. PR review → merge → task selection creates natural workflow cadence.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T07:21:42.749Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFPY13M7AWHEQSM6Z3HKB0C\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review workflow working well: Claude review posted actionable feedback (null check for comment.author), fix was straightforward (optional chaining), all checks passed after fix, and merge proceeded smoothly. The automated review catch prevented a potential production bug.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T07:22:33.460Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFPY60ZHYYCHBA3PB3E7HD6\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Skipped test was actually ready to run - validation infrastructure improvements had resolved the original issue. Worth periodically reviewing skipped tests to see if they can be unskipped. Test passed immediately when .skip was removed.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T07:22:38.495Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFQQAFR8FZY9EBESFK1MFBZ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test fixture management pattern: Using setupTempFixtures() + removing .git + git init creates clean test environment with kspec structure but no commits. More reliable than manually constructing YAML. Pattern used successfully in AC-2 and AC-5 tests.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T07:36:22.264Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFQSB85FCJJK5MBENJ2GW7M\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR creation workflow smooth - auto-generated branch name from task slug, moved commit from main to feature branch, created comprehensive PR body from task/spec context. Task notes provided all context needed for PR summary.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T07:37:28.581Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFR8HXWQ2TS9R6TGDCY90R0\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Iteration 8: Successfully implemented @01KFC3AR (--description flag for task add) from start to PR creation. Pattern that worked well:\\n1. Read spec to understand all ACs\\n2. Check existing schema (description field already existed)\\n3. Add CLI option and wire to TaskInput\\n4. Write comprehensive tests FIRST with AC annotations\\n5. Fix shell escaping issues in tests (not implementation bugs)\\n6. All 792 tests pass on first implementation try\\n7. Created PR with full context\\n\\nTotal time: ~15 minutes for feature + tests + PR. Clean handoff to next iteration.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T07:45:46.941Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFRD1Q9A8Q1M2YE5VK8R8CD\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"CI test failures can occur when tests don't configure git user.name/email before running git commit in temp dirs. Pattern to follow: Always add 'git config user.email/user.name' commands after 'git init' in tests that create fresh repos and commit. Found in PR #118 - test passed locally but failed in CI.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T07:48:14.185Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFRDEN1V6A68Y2RSDFPX84V\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Iteration 8 complete - accomplished multiple tasks:\\n\\n1. Reviewed PR #118 (log empty repo fix) - comprehensive review passed\\n2. Implemented @01KFC3AR (--description flag) with full AC coverage\\n3. Created PR #119 for --description implementation\\n4. Fixed failing CI test in PR #118 (missing git config)\\n5. Captured observations (success + friction patterns)\\n\\nKey patterns:\\n- PR review workflow with subagent worked well\\n- Implementation -> tests -> PR flow is smooth\\n- CI failures often reveal env config issues (git user.name/email)\\n- Test patterns: always configure git after init in temp dirs\\n\\nBoth PRs now ready for merge once CI completes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T07:48:27.426Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFS1A3YTHSJ31GK245P75VC\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review subagents worked excellently in parallel. Spawned two review agents simultaneously - both produced comprehensive, strict reviews identifying issues (PR #119 had failing test, PR #118 was clean). The parallel approach saved time and both reviews were thorough with proper AC coverage validation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T07:59:18.142Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFS1G84GSYKT6AFWVA8R0GM\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Shell escaping in tests is tricky across environments. The $'...' syntax worked locally but failed in CI. Using printf with double-escaped newlines ($(printf 'Line 1\\\\\\\\nLine 2\\\\\\\\nLine 3')) is more portable and explicit. Tests should prefer printf over $'...' for multiline string handling in bash commands.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T07:59:24.421Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFS1PAWEHVW5E4JA8FXJ2BD\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"RALPH_LOOP_INSTRUCTIONS.md PR review workflow is well-designed: check for PRs first, spawn review subagents, use decision tree (pass→merge, fail→fix). Following this process caught issues before merge and ensured quality. The --merge flag (not --squash) preserves kspec trailers which is critical for kspec log @ref functionality.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T07:59:30.652Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFS6VWQ8CAA2Z4S238YWXRR\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Successfully completed full PR review cycle in single iteration: reviewed 2 PRs in parallel, merged 1 immediately (PR #118), fixed failing test in other (PR #119), waited for CI to confirm fix, then merged. Both tasks (@01KFBPQA, @01KFC3AR) completed. The --watch flag on gh pr checks was useful for waiting on CI completion.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T08:02:20.183Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFSGAE5R6B49N4G4P52NQDD\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Spec status audit revealed that implementation often outpaces spec updates. ULID shortening, cascade updates, and YAML conventions were all implemented but marked not_started. The cascade feature in item set updated 18 child items automatically, demonstrating the value of hierarchical status propagation. Shadow branch separation meant no main branch PR was needed for metadata updates.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T08:07:29.989Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFT1E7G0FE9P83PPAJAQ0WJ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"State enforcement implementation went smoothly - clear spec with detailed ACs made implementation straightforward. Breaking existing tests was expected and fixing them reinforced the new workflow.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T08:16:50.929Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFT1JE45D0FKYAESH496GWV\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test helper pattern (kspecWithStatus vs kspecError) worked well once I found the right function. The cli.ts helper exports are well-structured for different test needs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T08:16:55.236Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFT481GRXPVSQJ0T63D2S1R\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR creation workflow smooth: auto-generated branch name from task slug, created branch, reset main, pushed, created PR with comprehensive summary including AC coverage checklist. The /pr skill handled the complexity well.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T08:18:22.896Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFTRJSKQ48241MWX3GR7VFJ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"JSON output audit revealed mostly good patterns - only one inconsistency found (clone-for-testing had its own --json flag). The systematic approach of searching for JSON.stringify, checking stderr handling, and documenting envelope format conventions was effective. Key insight: envelope format variation is intentional and serves different use cases (raw data vs success confirmations vs errors vs hook-specific formats).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T08:29:29.267Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFTSZW5903HK4XPN6J5Q6C6\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop iteration 13 completed successfully: Reviewed and merged PR #120, then completed task @01KFBDM8 (JSON output consistency audit). The PR review workflow worked smoothly with automated CI checks. The audit task was well-scoped with clear notes about what to investigate. Created PR #121 for the fix. Key efficiency: Using TodoWrite to track sub-tasks within the larger audit task helped maintain focus.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T08:30:15.430Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFVC7840GWEQVAE422SRD8H\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task @01KFBDQE 'Add spec-schema drift detection' needs clearer scoping. The original note mentions three issues but #2 appears to be a misunderstanding (already handled by --staleness check), and #3 (fixture conflicts) lacks concrete examples. Tasks derived from retrospective observations should include specific examples or reproduction steps, not just abstract descriptions of problems.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T08:40:12.805Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFVEK1FMH6M89DZJRGQYSSP\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop iteration 14: Successfully merged PR #121 (JSON output consistency), researched drift detection task (found it under-specified), and started well-defined task-set-batch task. Pattern: When a ready task lacks concrete examples or clear scope, checkpoint it with observations and move to a better-defined task rather than spinning on requirements gathering.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T08:41:30.415Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFVG0YMGCGHMCBRPPE67CGT\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Stop hook successfully caught incomplete session cleanup. Ralph loop should always checkpoint in-progress tasks before ending iteration, even if not completing them. The hook reminder ensures continuity for next session.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T08:42:17.428Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFW9Q828XCGG5B6HH1KWHEB\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Batch operation pattern in batch.ts worked well for task set implementation. executeBatchOperation() handled all the complexity of partial failures, ref deduplication, and output formatting. Helper function extraction (setTaskFields) allowed clean code reuse between single and batch modes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T08:56:19.459Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFWAJYXXY0SY7M12YAA4CT9\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test-first implementation worked well for task set batch. Writing all 15 tests first (based on spec ACs) provided clear targets and caught issues early. The 'write tests → implement → fix → repeat' cycle was faster than trying to implement and test simultaneously.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T08:56:47.837Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFWR2MPFXFF5BJ0VE5MNCCB\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop PR review workflow successful: spawned review subagent for pending_review task, agent performed comprehensive AC coverage check (13 ACs validated), test quality assessment (E2E strategy, isolation), and edge case verification. Review found no issues. Waited for CI, then merged with --merge flag to preserve trailers. Pattern: pending_review task -> spawn review agent -> wait for CI green -> merge -> complete task. This workflow ensures systematic quality checks without human intervention.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T09:04:09.879Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFWV250GFXWADZX4VW2ARSW\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task @01KFBDR7 'Improve Result type enforcement' has unclear scope. Initial investigation shows current Result pattern (discriminated unions with 'ok' field) is well-implemented and consistently used. Most code properly checks .ok before accessing success fields. Task note suggests multiple improvements (branded types, lint rules, never throw library) but unclear which is actually needed or would provide value. Without concrete examples of bugs or near-misses from this pattern, hard to prioritize improvements. Recommendation: Block task pending concrete evidence of problems, or pivot to documentation task.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T09:05:47.681Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFX1B8F3QJB5HCX8TKY0V7C\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Iteration 16: Successfully completed full PR workflow - reviewed and merged PR #122 (task set batch), blocked unclear task @01KFBDR7 (Result types), completed and shipped @01KFBJFE (dedupe formatRelativeTime) via PR #123. Pattern: PR review -> merge -> pick new task -> implement -> commit -> PR. Task selection improved: skipped manual_only task, blocked ambiguous task, picked clear tech-debt task. Total: 2 PRs processed (1 merged, 1 created).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T09:09:13.615Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFXTYEDSFF82Q1JXGX8CGME\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"KSPEC_TEST_TTY pattern works well for testing interactive prompts. By adding an env var check alongside process.stdin.isTTY, we can simulate TTY in tests while preserving real TTY detection in production. This pattern can be reused for other interactive commands.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T09:23:12.461Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFXV389J8EPW2ZJXQF6CEYR\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test error message checking pattern: When commands fail, error messages can be in either stdout or stderr. Using 'const output = result.stdout + result.stderr' and checking that combined output is more robust than checking just stdout. This worked for all 4 initially failing tests.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T09:23:17.386Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFYBZ4Z6V0DQQBYTJ4XCJYA\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Test helper API mismatch: kspec() expects string args but wrote tests using array syntax. Need to convert ['item', 'delete', '@ref'] to 'item delete @ref'. Should have checked helper signature before writing all tests.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T09:32:30.239Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Test helper API is documented - kspec() takes string args. Check helper signature before writing tests.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-22T19:38:17.603Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFYC3N6H7K8XPZ26MKMAAQV\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"findChildItems already existed in items.ts with correct implementation - avoided duplicate code by discovering existing helper. Good pattern: search for existing helpers before implementing new ones.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T09:32:34.854Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFZ0F443X3JG15DVT86TQS9\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test helper API documentation was critical for fixing tests. The kspec() helper signature (string args, not array) wasn't obvious from test file alone. Reading tests/helpers/cli.ts revealed correct usage pattern. Future: consider adding JSDoc examples in helper file showing common patterns.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T09:43:41.957Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFZF7C18HAJ6GR2RP69V6W6\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Git handling of files with newlines in filenames is extremely difficult. Standard commands like 'git rm' with shell quoting don't work. Even null-terminated operations struggle with escaping. Solution: Python script with subprocess.run() successfully handled the special characters where shell commands failed. This type of git corruption should be prevented at commit time if possible.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T09:51:45.537Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFZFCVXFDTXRZJMNVNTC5GP\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review subagent workflow is effective. Spawning a dedicated subagent with strict review criteria caught the critical file corruption issue before merge. The subagent provided detailed analysis including: blocking issues prioritized, test coverage gaps identified, code quality assessment, and specific fix commands. This caught a problem that would have been difficult to spot in manual review.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T09:51:51.165Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFZFHSEJXS6CW39BN7CMF7Z\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Interactive rebase with automated editor worked well for fixing historical commits. Using GIT_EDITOR with sed to automatically mark commits for editing eliminated manual intervention. Pattern: GIT_EDITOR='sed -i \\\"s/^pick <hash>/edit <hash>/\\\"' git rebase -i <base>. This allowed scripted fixes to commit history while maintaining full control.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T09:51:56.206Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFZG3YZZGRCGKG93MM087C1\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop PR review workflow successfully prevented corrupted code from being merged. The iteration followed RALPH_LOOP_INSTRUCTIONS.md: (1) Checked for open PRs, (2) Spawned review subagent, (3) Fixed blocking issues found, (4) Re-verified tests locally, (5) Merged with --merge to preserve trailers, (6) Completed task with proper documentation. This systematic approach caught and fixed a critical issue that manual review might have missed.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T09:52:14.815Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFFZSMSZMRKN2SQKZS42QC6F\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Tech debt cleanup pattern: When finding duplicate logic, check if the duplication serves a purpose (e.g., specialized behavior) or is truly redundant. In this case, inbox.ts had a local shortUlid() helper that was functionally identical to .slice(0,8) used elsewhere. The 'smart' ReferenceIndex.shortUlid() method wasn't needed for ephemeral inbox items without slugs. Solution: remove helper, use direct string slicing consistently. This makes code more maintainable and easier to understand.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T09:57:26.975Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFG0GWZC73H2GXDA2E5DDEJG\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Vitest v1 to v4 major version upgrade required only minimal changes: single async/await fix in test file. Breaking changes were well-contained. The vitest v4 warning message ('Promise returned by expect(actual).rejects.toThrow(expected) was not awaited') was clear and pointed directly to the issue, making the fix trivial. Major version upgrades don't always require extensive refactoring if the codebase follows best practices.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T10:10:09.005Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFG13F217CN26AT45BAW7VBR\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review and merge workflow is efficient - spawned parallel review subagents for both PRs, got clear recommendations, merged both immediately, completed tasks, pulled changes, and started new work. The review agents provided comprehensive analysis including local test verification and CI status context.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T10:20:17.345Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFG1CXNHG6X3V5B5W2KAHZ6Q\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task reset command workflow: Reset cancelled task to pending, then start/submit/complete with proper documentation. Fixed @task-yaml-formatting status efficiently using task reset flow.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T10:25:27.218Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFG1JNM235TJ78BTXQZJYKN2\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task @extract-test-helpers was already completed before being picked up. The workflow correctly handled this by verifying implementation (tests/helpers/cli.ts exists with all helpers, no duplicates in test files, 841 tests pass) and documenting findings in task notes before marking complete. This demonstrates good verification practices when tasks may have been completed out of band.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T10:28:35.586Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFGRVJPBP5HS9S19ENFGS448\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Spec-first with traits: Creating spec, adding traits, then deriving task immediately surfaced what tests were needed (trait ACs). Applied to --clear-deps feature.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T17:15:24.748Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFHJP6MKVAJ7653KC87J8C6Q\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR automated review catching AC test coverage gaps - the Claude reviewer on PR #141 identified two missing test assertions (--clear-deps and --automation author validation) that I'd missed. The strict AC coverage requirement in CLAUDE.md combined with automated review provides good safety net.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T00:46:51.539Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFHYJ9DH26CRPRFWZJYXKPJP\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"When debugging opaque CI/auth errors, search GitHub issues early. A quick search for 'npm trusted publishers OIDC' would have found the npm version bug immediately, saving significant iteration time.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T04:14:26.225Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJ636YGAN4ACZ8D1HVT10HQ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Workflow run foundation implementation demonstrates good schema-first development pattern. Defined all Zod schemas first, then storage operations, then CLI commands, then tests. This ordering prevented type errors and made the implementation flow smoothly. The type safety from Zod schemas caught issues early in compilation rather than at runtime.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T06:26:00.785Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJ63DA38WC8GVKEQ4W0G2Q0\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"E2E test fixture setup requires understanding of proper YAML formatting. Using JSON.stringify() to create YAML files doesn't work - produces invalid YAML syntax. Tests need either: (1) setupTempFixtures() with pre-built fixtures, (2) manual YAML strings, or (3) yaml library stringify. This pattern repeats across test files - consider documenting test fixture patterns in testing guide.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T06:26:07.300Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Documented in tests/helpers/cli.ts header: Don't use JSON.stringify() for YAML - use template literals, yaml library stringify, or pre-built fixtures.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-22T19:37:40.972Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJ6YNZMPF5YKAJWVDRFP1K1\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Test fixtures with invalid ULIDs (e.g., 01TEST000...) silently fail schema validation. Error only visible when parsing logic is instrumented with debug output. Should add test helper that validates fixture data before use, or use ulid() to generate proper test IDs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T06:41:00.916Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Added testUlid() helper that generates valid Crockford base32 ULIDs and auto-replaces invalid characters (I->J, L->K, O->0, U->V). Also documented common invalid patterns in tests/helpers/cli.ts header.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-22T19:37:45.999Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJ7AGSPNACKH2TCY9SZT5E8\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test fixture ULID validation issue was quickly identified through systematic debugging. The root cause (invalid ULID format in test fixtures) was found by examining validation failures and understanding that ULIDs must match proper regex format. Fix was straightforward: import ulid() and generate valid ULIDs. This pattern of using valid test data that matches production validation rules is important for reliable tests.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T06:47:28.823Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJ7APXVT6TXJH0CCEVY64XB\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Tests should use non-shadow mode setup (files in project root) unless specifically testing shadow functionality. The .kspec/ directory is ONLY used when shadow branch is properly configured. This keeps test setup simple and matches how kspec actually discovers files in non-shadow environments. Pattern: create kynetic.yaml, kynetic.meta.yaml, project.tasks.yaml directly in temp root directory.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T06:47:35.099Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJ7SAGTW27KKHS2RSXV019H\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"When fixing bugs with AC coverage: First read the code to understand the implementation, then identify the exact function/logic that needs updating, then add tests that validate the AC before implementing. This workflow ensures the fix is correct and properly validated. For AC-15, updating getParentTaskRef() to filter cancelled tasks was straightforward once the problem was identified.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T06:55:33.914Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJ8J51FZP9DQY25PYYS3Y3Y\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Systematic approach to code cleanup - created comprehensive mapping document before making changes, built automated sed script to handle bulk replacements, then manually verified and fixed edge cases. This pattern of 'map-script-verify-fix' worked well for 72 annotations across 9 files with zero regressions (all 874 tests pass). Script-first approach with manual verification is effective for large-scale mechanical refactoring.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T07:09:07.503Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJ8JBSB7WR6M3VD2HAW3B32\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review-merge flow worked smoothly: spawned subagent for comprehensive review, verified CI checks passed, checked for review comments, merged with --merge to preserve trailers, then completed task. The strict review requirements (AC coverage, test quality, isolation) caught in advance prevent merge issues. Subagent review before PR creation + automated CI review + manual merge checks = robust quality gate.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T07:09:14.411Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJ97VFR4WDPKNCVQJ9QMKAE\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review workflow is effective: spawned review subagent found 3 incorrect spec references that would have been missed. The strict review caught that annotations referenced @shadow-init instead of @shadow-init-remote for remote detection code. Fixed before merge, maintaining proper traceability.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T07:20:58.616Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJ9NFZ64QGSJZ61VSZ5ATRH\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Workflow step navigation implementation went smoothly. The existing workflow foundation (AC tests, error patterns, helper functions) made adding the next command straightforward. Test-first approach caught edge cases early (e.g., inferring run when exactly one active). Pattern of checking spec ACs against test coverage helped ensure nothing was missed.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T07:28:25.575Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJ9YR00XGX63F4Z2KYZA5KE\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review and merge workflow executed successfully. Used Task agent for comprehensive review (AC coverage, test quality, E2E strategy, test isolation all verified). All CI checks passed, automated reviews found no issues. Task completed cleanly with proper trailers and spec sync. Total time from PR creation to merge: ~4 minutes. The structured review process caught no issues because implementation quality was excellent from the start - comprehensive E2E test coverage, proper AC annotations, perfect test isolation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T07:33:28.704Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJ9YY8VPR4G1VVQK20H092C\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Workflow step navigation implementation demonstrates excellent code-to-spec traceability. AC annotations used throughout both implementation and tests. Run reference inference (auto-detect single active run) provides great UX. Error messages include actionable guidance with exact commands. Summary output on completion (duration, step counts) matches spec requirements exactly. This is a model implementation for future workflow features.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T07:33:35.131Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJA21CHKVD52598EQ9994FS\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Added comprehensive E2E tests for shadow hook functionality. Tests verify: 1) Hook installation during init copies from hooks/pre-commit to .git/hooks/pre-commit with executable permissions, 2) Hook blocks unauthorized commits (verifies commit count stays at 1), 3) Hook allows commits with KSPEC_SHADOW_COMMIT=1 env var (verifies commit count increases and message is correct). Used real hook file for tests 2 and 3 to ensure accurate behavior. All tests run in isolated temp directories. Task notes captured implementation approach before coding.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T07:35:16.626Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJA3PTYEPFHK8XHNEQGCRJV\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Iteration 8 completed: Merged PR #157 (workflow step navigation), then completed task @01KFJ4VT (shadow hook tests). Created PR #158. Workflow: reviewed and merged open PR first (per RALPH_LOOP_INSTRUCTIONS), then picked highest priority ready task. Task had clear 3-case scope from notes. Added tests to existing shadow.test.ts file, all 61 tests pass. PR created with /pr skill - auto-generated branch name test/shadow-hook-tests from commit message and task context.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T07:36:11.358Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJAVEGVBTYJ38PFTP30V5C2\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test-driven workflow implementation pattern worked well: wrote comprehensive E2E tests covering all ACs before refining implementation. The tests caught a subtle ordering issue (exit criteria must be checked before entry criteria) and a logical issue (skipping should bypass entry criteria for next step). Having 15 tests covering edge cases (strict/advisory modes, skip/confirm/force combinations) gave confidence that the implementation was correct. All 915 tests passing confirms no regressions.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T07:49:09.276Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJBNXX3C7PDGBTJ3PH4S070\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Automated PR review (Greptile) caught critical bug where entry_confirmed was never recorded - only exit_confirmed was working. The review identified that entry_confirmed remained undefined in all cases. This demonstrates the value of automated code review in catching semantic bugs that pass tests. The fix involved creating stub step results when advancing to the next step to capture entry_confirmed, then updating those stubs when the step completes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:03:36.995Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJBP2QJF9JV14331T8YGTF8\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Test failures from architectural changes can be misleading - when implementing stub step results, tests failed because they expected specific array lengths. The failures looked like bugs but were actually correct behavior - the architecture changed. Need to carefully evaluate whether test failures indicate bugs or just outdated expectations when making architectural changes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:03:41.938Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Expected behavior during architectural changes. Test failures from changed expectations (not bugs) are part of refactoring.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-22T19:38:12.290Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJBZJXM7ETYK1NKSY5S7CKW\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Workflow advanced features implementation completed smoothly. Key success factors: (1) Read existing workflow implementation first to understand patterns, (2) Extended schema before implementing CLI commands, (3) Followed existing test patterns for comprehensive coverage, (4) All 13 new tests passed on first run without fixes needed. The incremental approach (schema → commands → tests) worked well for this feature.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:08:53.429Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJC23TKBA6EQKETRSY3BP91\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"The /pr skill workflow (auto-generate branch name from context, move commits from main to feature branch, create PR) worked seamlessly for shipping completed work. The skill correctly derived 'feat/workflow-advanced-features' from the task reference, handled the branch creation and main reset cleanly, and created a comprehensive PR. This pattern is efficient for the ralph loop where work completes on main and needs to be shipped via PR.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:10:16.275Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJC2AA94N276JWH542F5RYD\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task state transition worked well: pending_review status held the completed work until PR was created, then completing the task after PR creation provides clean separation. This matches the RALPH_LOOP_INSTRUCTIONS.md pattern: task submit → PR creation → task complete after merge. However, I completed the task immediately after PR creation rather than after merge - should verify if this is the intended workflow or if completion should wait for merge.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:10:22.921Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJC2TSMBR0T2VDH5Y4CPNBH\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Completed task @task-workflow-advanced-features immediately after PR creation, but RALPH_LOOP_INSTRUCTIONS.md line 20 specifies task completion should happen AFTER merge. The correct workflow is: task submit → /pr → review → merge → task complete. Need to follow this sequence in future iterations to maintain proper task state. There's no way to 'uncomplete' a task once marked completed.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:10:39.796Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Lesson learned - workflow documented in AGENTS.md: submit → PR → review → merge → complete\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T05:18:17.949Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJCFDD4RMTAP9TSVRK20KYQ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Complete iteration 12 workflow executed successfully: Found pending_review task → Created PR #160 with /pr skill → Spawned review subagent → Review approved with 100% AC coverage → Merged PR with --merge strategy → Pulled merged changes to local main. The automated review subagent provided excellent quality checks (AC coverage, test quality, code patterns). Total time from pending_review to merged: ~8 minutes. Key learning: Task should stay in pending_review until AFTER merge (I completed it prematurely after PR creation).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:17:32.069Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJCFN0Q9KV5C0YFHYKP4KWX\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Review subagent pattern from RALPH_LOOP_INSTRUCTIONS.md worked exceptionally well. Single Task tool invocation with focused prompt ('check code quality, test coverage, alignment with spec, be strict about AC coverage') produced comprehensive review in table format covering: AC coverage (100%), code quality (excellent), test quality (E2E, no fluff), CI status (passing), files changed summary, and clear merge decision. The strict AC coverage requirement caught that all 4 direct ACs + 6 inherited trait ACs were properly tested. This automated review quality rivals human PR reviews.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:17:39.864Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJCZ4TFV7MBRTD896F4GR30\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Using spawnSync instead of execSync for test helpers provides better control over stdio streams. Key insight: execSync only returns stdout on success - stderr is lost. spawnSync captures both stdout/stderr in separate properties regardless of exit code. This pattern is more predictable for testing CLI tools that write warnings to stderr.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:26:07.567Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJCZB7A5PA8KMX4WMPJP840\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test-first verification for infrastructure changes: after making the helper change, ran full test suite to verify no regressions. The failing tests revealed a subtle stdin handling bug (empty string vs undefined) that would have been hard to catch otherwise. Full test coverage paid off immediately.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:26:14.122Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJDBDPNEMGRRJVXJZ830ADQ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Biome initialization process worked smoothly - the auto-init command detected the repo structure and configured appropriate excludes (dist/) and VCS integration automatically. Only manual change needed was adjusting indentation style from tabs to spaces to match existing code.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:32:49.877Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJDE8NKD0G9BGR94RDYJYND\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop PR workflow is now well-established: create PR for pending_review tasks, wait for CI, review comments, merge if clean, then complete task. This iteration demonstrated the full cycle twice (PR #161 merged, PR #162 created).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:34:23.027Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJE2DD8ZNRFCAS86J3QVEBB\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task @01KFJ52W completed smoothly using proper workflow: read real implementation first (src/cli/commands/ralph.ts), understood the protocol format, implemented matching behavior in mock. Reading the production code before implementing the test mock ensured format compatibility.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:45:23.240Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJENJNKYQABQ67HVNHQ7MTP\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review workflow caught missing test coverage - the automated review correctly identified that new mock functionality had zero tests, blocking merge until tests were added. Added 6 comprehensive tests by spawning the mock subprocess and using ACPClient to validate the full JSON-RPC protocol flow. The review requirement to test through the actual mock process (not just unit testing the logic) ensured we validated the complete integration.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:55:51.219Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJENS73FRJ811YBX4TGAD7K\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Successfully executed ralph loop PR review workflow: spawned review subagent → identified MUST-FIX issue (missing tests) → added test coverage → pushed to PR branch → waited for CI → verified all checks pass → merged with --merge flag to preserve trailers. Review agent correctly identified the gap between stated goal (catch format bugs) and reality (no tests exercising the code).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T08:55:57.924Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJF6NH0EF6DWG9EYGSGQ607\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Implementing validation warnings follows a clear pattern: 1) Add warning type to interface, 2) Add check logic in validation function, 3) Add formatting in display function, 4) Add E2E test. The existing staleness checks provided a good template to follow.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T09:05:11.201Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJF6V40XSX7CDANPJWWY5GA\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR workflow from main branch with unpushed commits: create feature branch, reset main to origin/main, push feature branch. This cleanly separates completed work from main without losing commits.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T09:05:16.928Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJFVX5KC3R69Z10BAJ0FSAX\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Type safety improvements catch bugs at compile-time: Adding typed response methods (respondReadTextFile, respondWriteTextFile) to ACPClient prevents runtime bugs by enforcing correct response structures. The pattern of replacing 'unknown' with SDK types (ReadTextFileRequest, etc.) provides IDE autocomplete and catches errors early. This approach worked well - build caught all type mismatches immediately.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T09:16:47.155Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJFZ1AQ5YT0NRGR3SDPAE8T\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop iteration completed two tasks efficiently: First reviewed and merged PR #164 (validation warning), then picked up next ready task (@01KFJ571 ACP type safety) and completed it with PR #165. The loop workflow (check PRs → merge if ready → pick next task) worked smoothly. Key pattern: Complete one task fully (including PR creation) before loop ends.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T09:18:29.720Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJGQE47HFDMZZEZATGWM73E\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"E2E test pattern for multi-entity search worked well: tested each entity type individually first (inbox, observation, agent, workflow, convention), then attempted combined test. When combined test had issues, individual passing tests proved core functionality works. This approach provides both comprehensive coverage and clear failure isolation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T09:31:49.255Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFJHA3H4EEANVVSC0HY4GHQY\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Pattern for adding new validation types: Created separate validation module (validate-skills.ts), integrated into validate command with dedicated flag (--skills), added comprehensive tests in matching test file. This modular approach makes validation extensible without bloating the main validate.ts file.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T09:42:00.996Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFKR87J5A4R0M5JYH1D7GXWH\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Session context commands work smoothly\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T21:02:34.053Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Tested during workflow evaluation session\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-22T21:04:15.970Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFKRBGPJ2C29V6ZD0YH4SBM2\",\n    \"type\": \"idea\",\n    \"content\": \"Add step editing to workflow add command\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T21:04:21.714Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": \"@01KFKRBN\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFKSGWR6SK7A59EVY54X7V34\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Hybrid skill-workflow model works well: skill as entrypoint providing context, workflow for structure and tracking. Reduced reflect skill from 215 to 152 lines while adding progress tracking.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T21:24:46.470Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFKA4RTKVTQ54AQF7Z2NTKDQ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop analysis: 5 parallel subagents (iterations, PR compliance, reflections, commits, review feedback) provided comprehensive audit coverage efficiently. Pattern: split analysis by concern, run in parallel, synthesize results.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T16:56:00.595Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFKA4S7HXXSY0PNQY1ZCKJB9\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Branch deletion without content verification: compared commit messages but didn't diff actual file contents. Should always run git diff <branch>:<file> <main>:<file> before concluding content is merged.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T16:56:01.009Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFM8HP1XACBQW6BK85EBXRNW\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Plan mode + subagent review workflow - Having a Plan agent review the plan before presenting to user caught several issues (exit code semantics, missing AC coverage, CLI signature mismatch) that would have caused rework. Worth replicating for complex specs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T01:47:21.022Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFMFTX4BNF58A29ZC7ZT0ESP\",\n    \"type\": \"idea\",\n    \"content\": \"Test shadow commit fix\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T03:54:43.211Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Test resolution for shadow commit\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-23T03:55:08.924Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFMH5SZGA6WF6TB75825DV6V\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Trait-based approach for cross-cutting concerns - creating @trait-shadow-commit made implicit shadow commit behavior explicit, testable, and documented. Subagent exploration before planning caught 6 additional missing commits beyond initial 4. Spec-first implementation ensures AC annotations in code reference back to spec.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T04:18:09.008Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFMP6TAMDM2Q9CRV1ZSD0PEE\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Plan mode with subagent exploration before spec creation. Using Explore agent to gather context from related projects (kynetic) and Plan agent to review/refine plans caught gaps early.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T05:46:05.012Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFMP73J7CY0QJYHN34BT1J15\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Detailed task notes with code snippets, file paths, and AC mappings. Makes tasks self-contained for automation and future sessions without needing original context.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T05:46:14.472Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFN35C6AHD2DW8N31ZN1F1T7\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"PR merge blocked by unresolved review threads requiring manual UI action. GitHub API doesn't support programmatic resolution of review conversations - they must be clicked 'Resolve conversation' in the UI. The check-unresolved-comments CI workflow blocks merge even when all issues are fixed and acknowledged by the bot.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T09:32:29.258Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Accepted limitation - GitHub requires manual 'Resolve conversation' clicks in UI, documented in AGENTS.md\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T05:18:21.704Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFNAT4N61CEP3GHFQZ328T28\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR merge workflow with review resolution: Successfully merged PR #189 using @pr-review-merge workflow. All CI checks passed (tests, claude-review). Greptile feedback was addressed in code but threads weren't programmatically resolvable - documented in PR comments instead. Workflow enforced systematic review before merge.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T11:46:09.702Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFNKFR78AJY6J1MMY42J1H2M\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Interactive CLI tools block automation loops. Encountered with 'sv add tailwindcss' and 'shadcn-svelte init' - both require user input even with --yes flag. This forces either: (1) finding alternative non-interactive installation methods, (2) manual configuration, or (3) pre-scripted answers via expect/stdin. For automation-friendly workflows, prefer tools with true --yes/--no-interaction flags or configuration files over interactive prompts.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T14:17:46.472Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFP01QSX0DB7EQBWW7S7ZFR0\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Daemon serve tests failing in both main and feature branches with 'Daemon failed to start within 5 seconds'. Manual daemon start works fine, suggesting test environment issue. Path resolution fix committed (7dd2106) but underlying timeout issue remains. May need to increase timeout or add stdio logging for test debugging.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T17:57:18.782Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Obsolete - daemon-serve.test.ts was refactored into multiple smaller test files (daemon-server.test.ts, daemon-api-*.test.ts, etc.)\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T05:18:24.199Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFP9AJAJKHTZ005GYT1E017V\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel subagent research for planning - Launching multiple explore agents simultaneously (one for best practices research, one for existing codebase patterns) provided comprehensive context quickly. Combined with Plan agent review, caught issues early before implementation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T20:39:25.266Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFP9ANG7QFQNWC7WNPEDGRES\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"AC-driven test design - Reading spec file directly and mapping tests to acceptance criteria ensured 100% coverage. Table format (AC | Test) made gaps immediately visible.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T20:39:28.519Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFPH3X3Z8YK2GVVKATAEKVHF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Investigation-first approach for bug fixes - reading task context, exploring code to understand root cause before proposing solutions. Found test failures were separate bug from the actual task issue.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T22:55:35.551Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFPH3ZV73P7FA5V1A4EX5N89\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Documenting findings in task notes before implementing - created clear audit trail of decisions (daemon bundling approach) that future sessions can reference.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T22:55:38.343Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFQ38Z76KSABGCHE44P4662G\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Test fixture ULID creation was error-prone - manually crafted ULIDs had wrong length or invalid Crockford chars. testUlid() helper exists but isn't mentioned in fixture documentation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T04:12:55.911Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Documented testUlid() helper in AGENTS.md Test Fixture Patterns section\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T05:13:26.859Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFQ3ADC1GRARE3BAZZWDS9CF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Detailed task implementation notes made E2E infrastructure setup straightforward - step-by-step guidance with verification checklist reduced ambiguity\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T04:13:43.170Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFQ59D0DBN8A654QA0Q2MG6Y\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"E2E debugging: Playwright error-context.md files with page snapshots are invaluable for understanding what browser actually sees vs what code expects\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T04:48:07.181Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFQ59KETY6PT8FA6YKZT332Q\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Same-origin architecture: daemon serving both web UI and API on single port simplifies CORS, WebSocket setup, and eliminates cross-origin complexity\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T04:48:13.787Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFQ8VZQC8J2VNDVXXWGZAG5N\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Subagent research pattern: Delegating architecture research to a subagent produced comprehensive findings with code examples, references, and concrete recommendations - more efficient than inline research\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T05:50:41.900Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFQ8W7Q3TWT541VNMTYNQ38M\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Capturing scope expansion immediately: When debugging revealed architectural issues beyond task scope, captured to inbox then promoted to proper task with full research context. Prevented context loss.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T05:50:50.083Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFR0M0HQEPB9ZJ80HSF1H4R9\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Iterative question-based design with AskUserQuestion tool - asking one design question at a time during spec work (X-Kspec-Dir header choice, PID location, etc.) kept decisions focused and got clear answers. Better than presenting all options at once.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T12:45:46.424Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFR0MBH2Z9GKP96DPTW9J5HN\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Subagent plan review before spec finalization - having a Plan subagent review the spec plan caught gaps (missing error cases, race conditions, path validation) that would have been harder to fix after writing the spec. Worth making standard practice for architecture specs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T12:45:57.667Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFR0MNJTDJ7SGWN2PWCPY5BA\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Didn't know about existing CLI features - wrote 36 ACs inline in YAML instead of using 'kspec item ac add', ran 29 individual 'task set --automation' instead of using --refs batch mode. Need better CLI feature discovery or habit of checking --help first.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T12:46:07.963Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Learning experience - established pattern of checking --help and using batch operations\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T05:18:26.718Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFRAKC9HG1YD6192H0XJNFBW\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Plan-Review-Revise cycle with subagents: Having a Plan agent design specs, then a second Plan agent review for gaps with full user constraint context, then fixing issues before presenting to user. Caught critical issues like ambiguous subagent spawn trigger.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T15:40:11.442Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFRAKVW1Q6E5FY9PTRFHXGA6\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Incremental question-based requirements via AskUserQuestion: Asking one focused question at a time (task selection order, subagent model, skill invocation, error tracking) kept decisions clear and avoided ambiguity in spec design.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T15:40:27.393Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFRCQHCS2Z9Y0XCKFYKT1K8Z\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Using testUlid() helper for test fixtures prevents silent failures from invalid Crockford base32 chars (L, I, O, U). The helper auto-replaces these with valid chars. PR #210 adds documentation for this pattern.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T16:17:24.889Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFS6AX4BHF071F63S4PTPGMS\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"E2E test creation workflow worked smoothly. Pattern established in project-selector.spec.ts provided clear template for documentary tests. Using test.skip() for pending implementation is effective for capturing expected behavior before UI exists. All 17 tests passed structure validation on first run.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T23:44:53.899Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFS6P9Q1GDVYAXF1E3ZGJTPZ\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Workflow runs accumulate without lifecycle management. 34+ active runs exist with no clear way to complete/cancel old runs. Need: kspec workflow complete/cancel/cleanup commands to manage run lifecycle and prevent stale run accumulation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T23:51:07.233Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFST4YEZ7C3FYCFXAFTGKP09\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Subagent audit pattern: Spawn agent to analyze multiple tasks → get structured findings → act on findings. Effective for task/test audits where parallel exploration needed.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T05:31:10.176Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFST50NYXR9Q7TB9A3JC92F8\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task reframing pattern: Change 'Write tests for X' to 'Implement X (AC-N to AC-M)' with implementation steps, required testIds, and 'No test.skip()' in Definition of Done. Prevents documentary test anti-pattern.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T05:31:12.447Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFST52N598B4EQ4P2F2G2K2M\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Documentary test anti-pattern: Agents write test.skip() tests that pass CI but don't verify anything. Task framing as 'write tests' enables this. Root cause: tests treated as goal rather than validation mechanism.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T05:31:14.469Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFT1Q5Y5RNBFXXCB7DA8RGDF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Subagent delegation for git history recovery: Pattern of spawn agent → search git log -p -S → extract lost content → report structured findings worked well for recovering 12+ lost notes from merge. Effective when content exists in history but was overwritten.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T07:43:27.686Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFT1QE8X64CFNDSJ9ATEEB1Y\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Shadow branch divergence lacks guided resolution. When local and remote kspec-meta diverge significantly (61 vs 362 commits), kspec shadow sync just fails with no guidance. Manual git merge-tree diagnosis and conflict-by-conflict resolution required. @yaml-merge-driver would help but was cancelled.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T07:43:36.221Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTESK40ED91F97SCD76JP6W\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test-first development pattern: Writing comprehensive tests before integration implementation catches edge cases early and provides clear specification. Pattern used in loop-mode-error-handling task: (1) Created test file with 23 tests covering all 9 ACs, (2) Implemented utilities to make tests pass, (3) Integrated into ralph.ts. Benefits: TypeScript compilation errors caught immediately, edge cases identified before integration, tests serve as executable documentation. This approach is especially valuable for complex logic with multiple edge cases (failure tracking, progress detection, escalation thresholds).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T11:31:58.208Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTFWFZ6370BPQ1GMZRVMTN3\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Automation-eligible tasks lack time/scope estimates. All eligible tasks in iteration 4 were large-scope (10+ ACs, 30-60+ min work). Automation loops work best with 10-15 min tasks but selection mechanism doesn't filter by estimated effort. Existing eligibility system addresses complexity/clarity but not time dimension. Result: loops start work that can't complete in single iteration. Suggest: add estimated_effort field (small/medium/large) to tasks, --max-effort flag for automation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T11:51:01.863Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTFWS69M8GSAXS7TJZBKMEA\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task Definition of Done (DoD) not visible during task selection. Task @01KFP84N had DoD requirement 'All E2E tests pass - no skips' in notes but wasn't surfaced during ready task selection. Workflow enforced DoD strictly at completion but constraint wasn't visible upfront. Created situation where task appeared eligible but became non-completable mid-work. DoD criteria are critical constraints that should influence task selection, not just exit validation. Suggest: extract DoD to structured field, show in task list, filter tasks by DoD compatibility.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T11:51:11.305Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTFX1MSXCMTBTYC05WD8NSY\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Partial progress commits valuable in automation loops. Iteration 4 on @01KFP84N: added test IDs to components (fd70b86d) even though DoD required fully enabled tests. Committing partial work provided value: (1) next iteration can continue from checkpoint, (2) incremental progress visible in git history, (3) work not lost if task abandoned. Better than all-or-nothing approach. Pattern: commit meaningful increments even if task incomplete, document remaining work clearly in notes and commit message.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T11:51:19.962Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTFX9SDQQ7ZP5BC7E8SB821\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Comprehensive session-end notes enable clean task handoffs. Final note on @01KFP84N documented: what's done, what remains, estimated effort, specific next steps, blockers, recommendations. This level of detail makes continuing work in next iteration frictionless - no context rebuilding needed. Pattern: when leaving task in_progress, include (1) completed work summary, (2) remaining work list, (3) effort estimate, (4) next concrete steps, (5) blockers/considerations. Especially valuable in automation loops where next iteration may be hours/days later.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T11:51:28.301Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTGC48BJC0A13Q7NW8SVJKX\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"E2E test verification blocked by daemon requirement in automation loops. Pattern encountered in @01KFP84N and @01KFP84S: (1) Adding data-testid attributes to components is automatable, (2) Removing test.skip() is automatable, (3) Verifying tests actually pass requires daemon running + test execution + debugging failures which exceeds single loop iteration scope (est 30-60+ min). This creates a 3-phase workflow where phase 3 blocks automation. Tasks remain in_progress at ~70% completion awaiting human verification. Solutions: daemon auto-start infrastructure, task splitting (separate test ID addition from verification), or DoD adjustment for automation eligibility.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T11:59:34.155Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Addressed by task @01KG5VSF\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-29T21:51:19.232Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTGKVRXEEV5MBV1XH1XQ39T\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Loop iteration 6 encountered systematic blockers: All eligible P2 tasks are web UI E2E tests requiring daemon startup + test verification, exceeding single iteration capacity. Both in-progress tasks (@01KFP84N, @01KFP84S) hit same blocker (daemon requirement) and now at failure count 2. Attempted @01KFMMXF (export command) but ~300-500 line implementation scope also exceeds capacity. Pattern suggests: (1) Web UI E2E tasks incorrectly marked automation:eligible - should be automation:needs_review until daemon automation exists, OR (2) Tasks should be split: 'Add test IDs' (automatable) + 'Verify E2E tests pass' (manual), OR (3) DoD should be relaxed to 'Tests enabled, pending verification'.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T12:03:47.613Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTGRPJXF2K3EW6RRR2WY3WD\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Loop mode failure tracking not queryable: [LOOP-FAIL:N] notes exist but no CLI command to check task failure count. Had to manually grep task notes to determine if @01KFP84N and @01KFP84S hit 3-failure threshold (both at count 2). Needed for automation decision: should loop retry task or escalate to automation:needs_review? Suggest: kspec task get @ref --loop-failures or similar to return failure count.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T12:06:26.141Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTH5GC9955K0HDD6V0MXSGT\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Loop error handling protocol (PR #243) executed correctly in iteration 7: [LOOP-FAIL:N] notes tracked failures per task, failure count visible across iterations, auto-escalation to automation:needs_review triggered at threshold 3. Pattern enables clear visibility into which tasks are struggling in automation and systematic escalation when human intervention needed. Tasks @01KFP84N and @01KFP84S hit 3rd failure (daemon requirement blocker) and were properly escalated.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T12:13:25.769Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTHK60JWKZKH928E6QVZ6TF\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"E2E test tasks hit systematic blocker in automation loops: Cannot run daemon (npm run serve) + E2E tests (npm run test:e2e) within loop constraints. Pattern affects all web UI E2E test tasks. Results in [LOOP-FAIL] notes and automation:needs_review escalation. Encountered on tasks 01KFP84N, 01KFP84S, 01KFP84X in iteration 8. Implementation completes successfully (test IDs + test files), but verification step requires human-driven session with long-running daemon.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T12:20:53.906Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTHKCY5R1K8N136P1HH3Y3J\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Session checkpoint hook blocks exit when in_progress tasks have automation:needs_review status. Hook expects all in_progress tasks to either complete or have handoff notes. However, tasks marked automation:needs_review are intentionally paused for human review. Workaround: manually add comprehensive handoff notes before exit. Pattern suggests automation:needs_review should either auto-add handoff notes or be recognized as valid exit state.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T12:21:00.997Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTHKM3WR00TD31129KQEMAF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task-work-loop workflow provided effective structure for automation. Clear steps (filter eligible → select → verify → start → work → commit → submit → PR → exit) prevented skipped steps. Workflow state tracking enabled clean handoffs. Successfully completed inbox view implementation (01KFP84X) following all steps systematically.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T12:21:08.348Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTJNAK1HV8NJKQCSB767QS5\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Automation loop cannot verify E2E tests that require daemon running. Pattern: Tasks add data-testid attributes and create E2E tests, but verification requires manual session to start daemon (npm run serve -w packages/web-ui) and run tests. Repeated across @01KFP84N (tasks view), @01KFP84S (items view), @01KFP84X (inbox view) in session 01KFTDBQB3Z0PA5Y0GQD8T1RW3. Tasks marked automation:needs_review and stall at ~70-80% complete. Potential solutions: headless daemon fixture for E2E tests, mock API layer, or split tasks (implementation + verification).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T12:39:32.705Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTJNJYX2PHTGXCAG3KA0M7Y\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task-work workflow (@task-work-loop) successfully enforced complete task lifecycle in automation loop: task selection from eligible list, verification before start, implementation with notes during work, DoD validation, commit with trailers, submit to pending_review, PR creation. Session 01KFTDBQB3Z0PA5Y0GQD8T1RW3 iteration 9 completed @01KFP850 (command palette E2E tests) from start to PR without friction. Workflow prevented common mistakes: starting without verification, skipping notes, missing DoD checks.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T12:39:41.277Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTKCK1P5GTM073CM64X5WTM\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task verification pattern: Before starting test-only task (01KFP854 - E2E tests), verified WebSocketManager implementation existed. Read manager.ts to confirm AC coverage (ac-28 to ac-32) before committing to E2E test creation. This prevented wasting iteration on tests for non-existent features. Pattern: For tasks scoped as 'write tests for X', verify X implementation exists first. Especially valuable in automation loops with limited iteration budget.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T12:52:15.031Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTMKWW95BXAHA9TF79XT9MR\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Batching related E2E test tasks into a single PR branch: Completed 3 tasks (@01KFP85D observations panel, @01KFP85G error handling, @01KFP85M navigation) on feature branch feat/observations-panel-e2e-tests. All tasks involved E2E tests and data-testid attributes for web UI. Benefits: (1) Avoided multiple PR context switches and branch overhead, (2) Shared commits across tasks (e.g., error-message testid used by all 3), (3) Coherent scope for review. Pattern works when tasks are tightly related, share common files, and can be reviewed together. Session completed 4 tasks total efficiently using this approach.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T13:13:43.049Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTP0GJKNPDMH60GSPXD95P0\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Automation loop cannot handle daemon-dependent E2E test verification. Pattern: Tasks get to ~80-85% complete (implementation done, test IDs added, tests enabled) but then block on daemon startup + iterative test debugging. Three tasks hit this in session 01KFTDBQB3Z0PA5Y0GQD8T1RW3 (iteration 14): @01KFP84N, @01KFP84S, @01KFQAGY. Root cause: Daemon requires manual 'npm run serve', E2E failures unpredictable, debugging cycle exceeds single-iteration capacity. Workaround: Mark automation:needs_review and exit loop. Impact: Web UI E2E testing tasks systematically blocked from automation completion. Potential solutions: (1) Automate daemon lifecycle in loop, (2) Split tasks into 'implementation' + 'E2E verification' phases, (3) Add automation:daemon-required tag for better categorization.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T13:38:05.012Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTPN91A5V1A3NBC088WA5QE\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task-work-loop workflow lacks exit condition for 'eligible but unsuitable' scenario. When eligible tasks exist but all exceed single-iteration capacity (e.g., 5 P3 tasks requiring 300-500 lines each), workflow continues to step 4 (start task) with no clean exit path. Had to manually cancel workflow in iteration 16. Exit conditions defined (no eligible tasks, already done, work complete) but not 'all eligible tasks too complex'. Affects ralph when only complex work remains in eligible pool.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T13:49:25.418Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTPNH9WXC0G77CB9JDSM5C8\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task automation eligibility assessment happens too late in workflow. Tasks get marked automation:eligible without scope assessment. Automation loops then waste iterations doing [LOOP-FAIL:1], [LOOP-FAIL:2], [LOOP-FAIL:3] assessments before marking automation:needs_review. Example: task @01KFMMXF assessed in iterations 6, 7, 14 as too complex (~300-500 lines) but stayed in eligible pool causing repeated evaluation. Assessment should occur BEFORE tasks marked eligible, not after automation attempts them. Related to @task-automation-eligibility but focuses on pre-eligibility workflow gap.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T13:49:33.884Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTPYK46Y190SQJC6RTA7HAA\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Automation loop graceful exit: When tasks require daemon/multi-file coordination exceeding loop capacity, system correctly escalated 3 tasks to automation:needs_review with comprehensive handoff notes. Clean exit without attempting incomplete implementations. Session 01KFTDBQB3Z0PA5Y0GQD8T1RW3 iteration 17.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T13:54:30.663Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTPYVEK0ZQTH006HH1H5F1M\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Zero-completion automation sessions: Loop iteration 17 completed with 0 tasks finished, all 3 in_progress tasks escalated to automation:needs_review. Distinct from prior successful Ralph loops. Root cause: Tasks marked automation:eligible but require daemon E2E testing (2 tasks) or multi-file coordinated implementation (1 task). Gap between 'eligible' tag and actual automation feasibility in single iteration. Affects task selection heuristics.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T13:54:39.187Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTQJ62852K34N95AFCKX5SC\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Loop iteration 19 assessment: Correctly identified that all 4 eligible GitHub Pages export tasks (@01KFMMJ4, @01KFMMXK, @01KFMMXR, @01KFMMXW) exceed automation loop capacity. Marked all as automation:needs_review with clear reasoning. Tasks form a coordinated feature set requiring multi-hour focused implementation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T14:05:12.649Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTR8FDCNMBT7P0VNN8SDBSW\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Repetitive checkpoint notes across automation loops: Tasks stuck in automation:needs_review state get identical checkpoint notes added every iteration. Example: @01KFP84N received 36 notes, with notes 27-36 being nearly identical 'Loop Iteration N - Session End Checkpoint' messages. Creates noise without adding value. Possible solutions: (1) Skip checkpoint notes if last note is recent and task state unchanged, (2) Update most recent checkpoint note instead of appending, (3) Add checkpoint command that manages session-end state separately from progress notes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T14:17:23.116Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTR8ZK3WJV841Y8F7C3KN9P\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Loop iteration 21 efficiently completed pending_review task @01KFP85M in first action by checking task status, validating work was already merged, and immediately completing it. Demonstrates value of prioritizing pending_review tasks over in_progress tasks - they're usually closest to done and just need verification/completion. Pattern: pending_review > in_progress > ready.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T14:17:39.684Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTRRAAF4852S6F5H249P78G\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Automation loop iterations consumed even when zero eligible tasks exist. Pattern observed in iteration 23: loop checked 3 in_progress tasks (all automation:needs_review), found 0 eligible ready tasks, added checkpoint notes, then exited. No actual work possible but iteration budget still used for status quo documentation. Systemic issue - will recur whenever queue is fully blocked on manual work. Potential improvement: early exit detection before iteration starts, or iteration budget exemption for no-op sessions.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T14:26:02.191Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Resolved by @01KFV6CZ (PR #247). Ralph loop now filters both ready AND in_progress tasks by automation:eligible. Session 28 demonstrates clean exit when no eligible tasks remain - zero redundant iterations.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-26T01:13:03.331Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTRY6ASB4AHM7D0ZTP2HX68\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Loop mode runs redundant iterations when no progress possible. Iterations 22-24 added identical checkpoint notes with no state changes. All 3 in_progress tasks marked automation:needs_review, no eligible tasks available, but loop continued for 3 iterations adding duplicate 'no progress possible' notes. Suggest: early exit condition 'if no state change in last N iterations AND no eligible tasks, exit immediately' to avoid redundant work.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T14:29:14.713Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Resolved by @01KFV6CZ (PR #247). Exit condition now checks automation eligibility for both ready and in_progress tasks. Session 28 exited immediately when finding no eligible work.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-26T01:13:09.905Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTSQQSAEJ0HXNEQJ209YCRZ\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Workflow system lacks early exit mechanism. When workflow determines no work is possible (e.g., no eligible tasks), must still step through all remaining workflow steps providing skip reasons. Attempted 'kspec workflow complete @ref' which does not exist. Would benefit from 'workflow exit' or 'workflow skip-remaining' command to cleanly terminate when continuation is impossible.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T14:43:11.786Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTSR2MBYJQ6GAS3Y8Z4DBV4\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Automation loop adds repetitive status notes to stalled tasks. After 27 iterations of ralph automation, same 3 in-progress tasks (@01KFP84N, @01KFP84S, @01KFQAGY) accumulated 27+ nearly-identical notes documenting 'Loop Iteration N - No Eligible Tasks'. While notes provide audit trail, they create significant noise obscuring substantive progress notes. Consider: batch note update mechanism, dedicated status/stall-reason field, or suppress iteration notes when status unchanged.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T14:43:22.891Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTSWYG75X3E38BWWRK8HBWQ\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop ran 28 iterations with identical outcome (no eligible tasks, same 3 tasks documented each time). After 2-3 consecutive iterations returning no eligible tasks, the loop should recognize the pattern and exit early. Current behavior wastes API calls and adds redundant notes. Need early termination logic: if last N iterations (N=2 or 3) all exited with 'no eligible tasks' and same task set, stop the loop.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T14:46:02.504Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFTTA3TFQ6MBC3CZ2Z1V740J\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Structured loop iteration note template pattern: Used consistently across 30 automation iterations to document why progress wasn't possible. Template format: '## Loop Iteration N - [Status]' followed by Exit Reason, Task Status (with ✅/❌ checkboxes for completed/incomplete work), specific blockers, and clear next actions. Creates audit trail showing automation decision-making and prevents false 'why is nothing happening' concerns. Makes it obvious when automation is correctly identifying blockers vs stuck in broken logic.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T14:53:13.935Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVPXSZXJE3FNK50A1M0MYN8\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"E2E tests in packages/web-ui timeout after 2+ minutes with no progress indication or diagnostic output. Makes debugging test failures extremely difficult - cannot iterate rapidly. Tests may be waiting on daemon startup that never completes, or Playwright fixtures have configuration issues. Blocked work on @01KFP84N and @01KFP84S in loop iteration 2.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T23:13:19.358Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Addressed by task @01KG5VSF\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-29T21:51:17.744Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVPY36ARRRWYKQZTRXC8CAX\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Loop mode task verification gap: Multiple iterations accepted task notes claiming 'already implemented' or 'tests exist' without independent verification (running tests, checking code). Iteration 1 concluded UI was incomplete based on test failures; iteration 2 found UI components actually exist with proper test IDs. Real issue was E2E infrastructure, not missing implementation. Task notes are context, not proof of completion.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T23:13:28.778Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVPYB4RSBEGW5GF5Z7W1WY8\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Reading actual source code to verify task claims proved more reliable than trusting notes. When @01KFP84N notes said 'UI incomplete', reading TaskList.svelte revealed all required test IDs were present. Verification approach: Read components -> check test IDs -> run tests (if possible) -> only then accept completion claims. This prevented false conclusions about missing implementation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T23:13:36.921Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVQKD22NWCRJFJWRBKPNDR0\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"E2E tests via Playwright for daemon API endpoints: Using packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/*.spec.ts for real HTTP integration tests (not vitest mocks) aligns with project architecture documented in AGENTS.md. This session: created api-projects.spec.ts with 5 passing tests making real fetch() calls to running daemon. Pattern: Start daemon via test fixture, make HTTP requests, verify responses. More reliable than mocking and tests actual behavior.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T23:25:07.010Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVQKFHX5SX08ZQZDX25MKJS\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task DoD conflict with project conventions: Task @01KFQAF9 DoD said 'write real HTTP tests' and 'no documentary/stub tests remain' but AGENTS.md documents that daemon API routes use documentary tests (static analysis). Had to resolve conflict by checking existing patterns in daemon-api-*.test.ts files. Resolution: Created E2E tests in packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/ and updated documentary test to reference them. Friction point: When DoD contradicts documented patterns, unclear which is authoritative.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T23:25:09.566Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVQYR778DPEYXP93M0JKW0V\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Loop mode error handling AC-5 not working: Tasks @01KFP84N, @01KFP84S, @01KFQAGY all have [LOOP-FAIL:3] notes but remain automation:eligible instead of being auto-escalated to automation:needs_review as specified in @loop-mode-error-handling AC-5. Implementation in PR #243 claims to handle this but actual behavior shows automation status not being updated after 3 failures. Verified in session 01KFVN3DDTKEQF1DAF8V3KV48V iteration 4.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T23:31:18.887Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVRK63DF261C4ZNK9NWQJJX\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Loop iteration 5: Accountability in action - instead of immediately marking tasks as needs_review, actually debugged E2E infrastructure issues. Fixed real problems (Vite proxy configuration, API client URL handling) that were blocking all E2E tests. Committed working code (c24fd694) that moves the project forward. Loop failures should document genuine investigation and progress, not just 'this is hard, skipping.'\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T23:42:28.461Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVSBZ9AKZY33E0SAYB9KJEK\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"E2E test infrastructure debugging pattern: When E2E tests fail, work backward through the stack systematically. Session 01KFVN3D example: test timeout → Vite proxy missing → API client hardcoded URLs → daemon fixture loading issue. At each layer, verify the fix (tests connect successfully) before moving to next layer. This methodical approach identified root cause (daemon ContextManager path handling) after fixing intermediate issues (Vite proxy + relative URLs in commit c24fd694).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-25T23:56:00.682Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVSKKCZVQ2K2BRJMT0A86WP\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Loop mode automation tag disconnect: Across 8 consecutive loop iterations, task notes documented 'marked automation:needs_review' but the actual command 'kspec task set @ref --automation needs_review' was never executed. This suggests a pattern in autonomous loops where intent is documented in notes but the corresponding state change command is not run. Root cause: loop documenting WHAT should happen without executing HOW to make it happen.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T00:00:10.655Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVTBAYZ7S0403M97E2XG31T\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop iteration without progress: Loop ran 12 consecutive iterations with zero code changes or git commits. All iterations exited with 'no automation-eligible tasks' message. Tasks remained in_progress state throughout despite being marked automation:needs_review. Each iteration added near-identical checkpoint notes documenting 'no work attempted'. Pattern indicates need for circuit breaker that detects repeated no-progress iterations and either auto-escalates tasks or stops the loop. Related to @01KF554T circuit breaker concept but captures actual observed behavior rather than theoretical design.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T00:13:08.448Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVTBKBKDNJ0HJ6VMJ9AXQMH\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Session checkpoint hook enforcement prevented task abandonment: Stop hook detected 3 in_progress tasks without recent meaningful progress and blocked session exit until checkpoint notes were added. All tasks received documentation of current state, blockers, and next steps. This pattern ensures tasks don't silently stall - they either get documented or completed. Hook runs automatically on session end with no manual intervention needed. Particularly valuable for automation loops where task state must be explicit for next iteration.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T00:13:17.043Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVTYSJECRND016ZATZ25N3A\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop continues iterating when all active tasks are automation:needs_review. Observed across 15 consecutive iterations: each iteration runs 'kspec tasks ready --eligible', finds 0 tasks, then adds repetitive status notes to all escalated tasks. Exit condition correctly identifies no eligible work but doesn't trigger early exit before status documentation. Result: unnecessary API calls, note bloat (45+ notes across 3 tasks), slower session completion. Ideal: exit immediately when no eligible tasks remain without adding iteration notes to needs_review tasks.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T00:23:45.998Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Resolved by @01KFV6CZ (PR #247). Ralph loop now correctly exits when all in_progress tasks are automation:needs_review. Verified in session 28.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-26T01:13:16.392Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVTYW9TT5NNV7JNR0PHRM0R\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task escalation with comprehensive rationale prevents false automation work. Pattern observed: when tasks blocked or require human decisions, automation loop adds multi-paragraph notes documenting: (1) WHAT blocks the work, (2) WHY it's not automatable, (3) WHAT human needs to do next. Tags task automation:needs_review. Result: zero false work attempts across 15 iterations, clear handoff context for human sessions. Quality over speed: better to escalate with context than attempt inappropriate work.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T00:23:48.795Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVVATF0YA11E7EB88TAHP3X\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph automation loop ran 10+ iterations (7-17) with zero implementation work after all tasks marked needs_review. Loop exit logic only checks task existence, not progress stagnation. Should detect: N consecutive iterations with no file changes, commits, or task status transitions → early exit with diagnostic.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T00:30:20.128Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVVB2KHS3P06SR1X42DFW7Q\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Session checkpoint notes (iterations 7-17) consistently documented: task state, what's complete, what's blocked, required resolution steps, investigation files, automation status. This pattern provides excellent continuity for next session and clear audit trail of escalation reasoning.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T00:30:28.466Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVVBBE6ED70C0ZKXW32Q97Z\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Daemon fixture loading blocker affected 2/3 tasks across 10 iterations with no alternative approach attempted. Pattern: E2E test harness starts daemon with --kspec-dir pointing to temp fixtures, daemon returns empty data instead of YAML content. Should have tried: run daemon manually with debug output, inspect ContextManager code paths, create minimal reproduction case, or escalate infrastructure debugging to separate focused task.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T00:30:37.511Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Promoted to task @01KG5VSF\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-29T21:51:11.063Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": \"@01KG5VSF\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVVHGHH2Q71ECC19CF59E4E\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Loop mode escalation discipline working as designed: Session 01KFVN3D ran 18 iterations with 3 in_progress tasks. All tasks marked automation:needs_review in iterations 7-8 after assessment. Loop correctly exited when kspec tasks ready --eligible returned empty array. No thrashing, no shortcuts attempted, no improper completion claims. Tasks stayed in_progress with comprehensive checkpoint notes providing human handoff context. This validates the automation system recognizing its limits and delegating complex/blocked work appropriately.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T00:33:59.346Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFVXSQF1YH0J7X5HPQHJDR8D\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop exit condition working correctly: Session 28 demonstrated clean exit behavior after @01KFV6CZ fix. Loop checked 'kspec tasks ready --eligible', found empty array (all 3 in_progress tasks were automation:needs_review), and exited immediately with zero redundant iterations. This resolves the overnight session issue where loops ran 30+ iterations with no progress. Exit condition now filters both ready AND in_progress tasks by automation:eligible status.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T01:13:25.730Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFXTADHRF0ZBX4E0HR7H11AS\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Tasks created via 'kspec derive' have auto-generated notes that just copy spec content. For standalone tasks, needed to manually add structured sections: Background (why this matters), Reproduction steps, Concrete examples, Open design questions. This structure makes tasks actionable without conversation context.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T18:51:07.192Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFXTAKKXZ27TMK4SA7TQMAFG\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Subagent plan review caught CLI command syntax issues (missing --as and --id flags) before execution. Using a reviewer subagent after writing a plan prevents wasted iterations.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T18:51:13.405Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFXVK5QBFCN3A3BTXME0G86C\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"dist/daemon/ can become stale without warning - packages/daemon/src changes aren't reflected until root 'npm run build' is run. E2E tests can pass web-ui build but fail because daemon code is outdated. Wasted debugging time on what appeared to be runtime error but was actually stale build.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T19:13:22.667Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Fixed in PR #276 - added daemon staleness detection that warns when dist/daemon is older than source\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T02:03:06.384Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFXVKJJE3JWG67VFYNM64ZC8\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Comparing dist/ vs source when debugging daemon issues - immediately revealed the stale build problem when runtime debugging was going in circles\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T19:13:35.823Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFYAH1CQ6FP9V5MJ4MMB33AW\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Debug element technique for Svelte reactivity: Adding conditional debug elements like `{#if state}<div data-testid=\\\"debug-...\\\">{state}</div>{/if}` quickly verifies whether state is actually true at runtime vs expected. Useful for diagnosing reactivity issues where console logs show updates but UI doesn't reflect them.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T23:34:21.335Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFYAH9ABXKZNRAWVN8G751YF\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"bits-ui Sheet/Dialog Portal reactivity broken in Svelte 5: Props passed to child components through bits-ui Portal don't update reactively. PresenceManager.shouldRender returns false even when open=true. Workaround: use native elements or custom components instead of bits-ui Dialog for Svelte 5 projects. See task @01KFP84N notes for full investigation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T23:34:29.452Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Resolved by using $state object pattern + flushSync. See @01KFZ708 and /svelte-5 skill for documentation.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-27T07:52:07.714Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFZ3YG03R29D6MYRHFT5WV5S\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task notes from loop mode sessions can become noisy/unreliable, requiring manual cleanup or user warning to ignore recent notes. Example: @01KFP84N had 26 noise notes removed and user warned remaining notes might be incorrect.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-27T06:58:36.675Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFZ3YNHQWZFZ6MMWBR81H6Y6\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Using Explore subagent for deep analysis before making changes provided comprehensive understanding (file locations, line numbers, root cause, impact analysis) that enabled confident parallel fixes via multiple subagents.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-27T06:58:42.360Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KFZ708S00S4EA95C1A57HHD2\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Svelte 5 reactivity solution: Use $state object pattern + flushSync() for reactive conditional rendering. Separate $state variables may not trigger {#if} block re-renders; wrapping state in object (panel = $state({ open: false, task: null })) and using flushSync(() => { panel.open = true }) ensures synchronous DOM updates. Also documented in /svelte-5 skill. Resolves friction @01KFYAH9.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-27T07:52:00.544Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG031N6WQM6BM3S0J2YFEF0H\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"bits-ui Select onValueChange in Svelte 5 returns array of characters plus new value (e.g., ['a','l','l','in_progress'] instead of 'in_progress'). Workaround: extract last element from array when Array.isArray(value).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-27T16:02:06.172Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Incorrect diagnosis - bits-ui Select works correctly; issue was likely misuse of spread operator or other code error\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T05:14:58.910Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG031Y246EC054DSQ2CEX9SF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Console log capture in E2E tests revealed exact bits-ui callback values, making the array quirk immediately visible. Adding console.log to component handlers during debugging is highly effective for understanding Svelte 5 reactivity issues.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-27T16:02:15.236Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG0J4H7FFW05RZP39YDBM2YF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Reading reference tests (tasks.spec.ts) before writing new tests - understanding existing patterns informed structure and avoided reinventing conventions\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-27T20:25:49.040Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG0J4XRDKQ7Z6Y7FBP2TX1K8\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Documenting blocking issues with specific symptoms, likely causes ranked by probability, and debug commands - makes next session pickup much faster\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-27T20:26:01.869Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG0N4V90NDXX0MVSYXWWTN2M\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Schema validation (safeParse) failures in extractItemsFromRaw are silent - items just don't appear in results with no error or warning. This caused significant debugging time when trait had invalid enum values and module had nested items in traits field. Consider adding validation error logging or a strict mode that throws on parse failures.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-27T21:18:25.056Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG0ZHY1QR402HYBSWCMZJ9Z5\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Dedicated E2E fixtures pattern - creating packages/web-ui/tests/fixtures/ separate from shared tests/fixtures/ cleanly isolates E2E test data from unit tests, preventing cross-contamination\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-28T00:20:19.639Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG17R6Y5MEF5DPZ1Z73YFJEW\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Using /e2e skill patterns immediately caught ULID validation issue (Crockford base32 excludes I, L, O, U). Invalid ULIDs in fixtures fail silently - the skill's warning helped debug quickly.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-28T02:43:33.957Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG17RDSGDZB9X9XTRXN4458K\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Session context is loaded from .kspec-session file (not kynetic.meta.yaml). This caused debugging time when E2E tests couldn't find session focus. The API (fetchSessionContext) and file location should be documented in /e2e skill or AGENTS.md.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-28T02:43:40.977Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG17RKW385KB2RXRV8KCAVWV\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"TaskSummary interface was missing depends_on field, needed for dashboard to compute blocked task count. Had to add to shared types + daemon routes. API contracts should include all fields needed for common UI computations.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-28T02:43:47.203Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Fixed - depends_on field added to TaskSummary interface and daemon routes\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T05:13:39.126Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG1GNQJZRR2F3TH526VHVA3A\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"E2E skill has incorrect selector guidance for bits-ui Select: recommends getByRole('option') but bits-ui uses data-slot attributes. Correct pattern: await dropdownContent.locator('[data-slot=\\\"select-content\\\"]'); then dropdownContent.locator('[data-slot=\\\"select-item\\\"]').filter({ hasText: 'value' }).click(). Update e2e/SKILL.md line 15 and lines 162-164.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-28T05:19:29.888Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Fixed in PR #256 - updated E2E skill with correct bits-ui Select selector pattern\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-28T05:24:34.861Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG2FM29NVPRY5BF8DW52FQ00\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"isStaticMode() guard pattern worked well for conditionally disabling features without major refactoring - single check at API layer propagates through entire app\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-28T14:20:21.173Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG4M2HRF76XZRXKVAMDZFDP2\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Investigation-first debugging: When tests pass but docs say they shouldn't, investigate WHY before closing. In this session, discovered skill documentation was outdated rather than tests being wrong - prevented false task closure and led to fixing actual issue (stale docs).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-29T10:16:38.927Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG4M2R8569QYJMCB8GJ6XR9C\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Throwaway inspection tests: Writing quick, disposable tests to inspect actual DOM/state is effective debugging. DOM inspection test revealed bits-ui elements have both role='option' AND data-slot attributes - concrete evidence in minutes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-29T10:16:45.573Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG4M2YJ6TSAQ52TWWK1F2337\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Skill documentation can become stale without detection: /e2e skill claimed getByRole('option') doesn't work with bits-ui when it actually does (bits-ui added proper ARIA roles). No mechanism flags skill docs as potentially outdated when dependencies change. Task @01KG1H91 was created based on incorrect assumption from stale docs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-29T10:16:52.039Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG5SGK089902EVXG1FPKPX0S\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Explore+Plan parallel subagent pattern for implementation tasks: Before implementing a task with existing spec/notes, launch two subagents in parallel - (1) Explore agent to gather codebase context (file locations, interfaces, test patterns) and (2) Plan agent to design the implementation approach. Both complete before coding begins, providing thorough context AND a concrete plan. Used successfully for ref normalization task - all tests passed first try.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-29T21:10:56.264Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG64RZ0E5YPAMRYH81851MJA\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"CLI --force flag pattern works well for agent/script use. inbox delete --force skips confirmation. Same pattern could apply to other commands needing non-interactive mode.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-30T00:27:45.039Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG6WJZFBGPPPMSNQ2H5C8Q8E\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Observation triage session efficiently resolved 12 friction observations by: (1) batch retrieving all observations, (2) cross-referencing AGENTS.md documentation, (3) categorizing into resolvable/keep-open/historical before acting, (4) verifying obsolete items (like deleted test files) before resolution\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-30T07:23:54.731Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG7A7ZSDZCK6RD639Q7Q02AS\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Test1\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:22:34.669Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Batch test\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:22:46.874Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG7A84F9WX9KXDKSQKJ6X3MX\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Test2\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:22:39.465Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Batch test\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:22:46.980Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG7A867AR8FGM6WE8EXM64QT\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Test3\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:22:41.259Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Batch test\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:22:47.048Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG7A8T9GCNWNEF22DX5P6Z15\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Debug1\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:23:01.808Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Test\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:23:08.702Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG7A8W996JYVJ9BGNHBRAZC3\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Debug2\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:23:03.849Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Test\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:23:08.817Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG7ACHTW9P6R0G5GD49WP4DY\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Batch1\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:25:04.220Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Test\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:25:12.344Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG7ACKM3GYQPQ6RHY81BXW72\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Batch2\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:25:06.051Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Test\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:25:12.456Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG7AD09XV1EJFAN1DSW4XS4F\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"ShellA\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:25:19.037Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"ShellTest\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:25:26.717Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG7AD2AXC4ZZBNMZW62K516P\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"ShellB\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:25:21.117Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"ShellTest\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:25:26.831Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG7ARFWPEDQZE6FH3A9RYZ1A\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test pattern: when creating multiple items in quick succession for batch operation tests, use JSON mode to capture full ULIDs instead of parsing 8-char prefixes from human output. ULID prefixes can collide when items are created within the same millisecond, causing test deduplication to produce unexpected results. Full ULIDs are always unique.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-30T11:31:35.447Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG8PFDENWCZK15W036ZB8CX9\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Following existing patterns (task-limit marker) made implementing new feature (end-iteration) straightforward. Same file paths, detection mechanism, and cleanup lifecycle.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-31T00:15:35.381Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG8RAYQJPYB4KBVHQMMGKXPV\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Review feedback loop (Greptile + Claude) caught real bugs: async race condition in signal handler and no-op test. Worth keeping mandatory.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-31T00:48:06.387Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG8RB42RY7YS3283JZJ40EGS\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"User edge-case questions ('what about Ctrl+C?', 'does it work on Windows?') led to better implementation. Don't rush to close - invite scrutiny.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-31T00:48:11.864Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KG95K29ERJ12XFDWW44P0MPF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"kspec search command exists and works well - found it during reflection when checking coverage. Searched 'multi-ref' and got comprehensive results across specs, tasks, inbox. Should use this more proactively during work.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-31T04:39:43.662Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGG9KZQ5XXJ44RMQ0MW52RBF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Multi-codebase exploration via parallel subagents: Spawning 4-6 explore/research agents simultaneously to analyze kspec and kynetic-bot for gap analysis, architecture comparison, and Rust migration planning was highly effective. Each agent focused on one domain (CLI stack, bot ecosystem, ACP, context mgmt, migration strategy) and the results synthesized into comprehensive documentation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-02T23:04:49.125Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGG9M76B5N03Z660P2B7NVH3\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"kspec bootstraps greenfield projects well: Initialized kynamo (Rust rewrite project) with kspec to track its own development. Shadow branch, spec items for 6 implementation phases, and inbox items all created smoothly. Demonstrates kspec's value beyond self-hosting - can bootstrap any new project with structured planning.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-02T23:04:56.779Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGK93JZGTRSRBEB2NHW6ERBF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task notes with root cause analysis and specific file list made implementation straightforward - this pattern should be replicated when creating reflection-based tasks\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-04T02:53:35.088Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGKVNV4ZXHE1AYD8ZWA11HRF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Spawning a Plan agent to review completed spec/task work against the original plan catches gaps (like missing traits) that the primary agent overlooked. Useful pattern for quality assurance on spec creation work.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-04T08:18:07.647Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGKYG2XXQ4GG2X6S87CP4HJM\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Bulk AC add missing: Adding 33 ACs required 33 individual kspec item ac add commands. Would benefit from kspec item ac add-batch @ref --file acs.yaml or stdin JSON support.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-04T09:07:24.733Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Batch command system exists (PRs #321/#322). Friction is documentation, not capability.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-02-06T10:34:37.210Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGKYGDYSYSF0WC2KEJN5P66S\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Parent relationship not persisted: item add with under flag creates items but parent field is null. Also spec says parent flag but CLI requires under flag.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-04T09:07:36.025Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGKYGFQX8G25Q2ZACE340CHD\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Spec split for automation eligibility: Splitting a large spec into focused child specs made task-to-AC mapping clear and enabled granular automation eligibility assessment.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-04T09:07:37.854Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGM07N5F047VJTWK2R3QJZW4\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Test reference ambiguity with @01 prefix - When writing integration tests that create plans/tasks, using generic references like @01 fails when test fixtures already contain items with ULIDs starting with 01. Must use explicit slugs (--slug test-plan-1) for test isolation. Affected cli-plan.test.ts and task-plan-ref.test.ts - all references needed slugs added.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-04T09:37:45.647Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGM07QTQKAAQTMWERMMZHJ65\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Schema-first implementation pattern - Defining schemas (Plan, PlansFile) first, then parser functions (loadPlans, findPlanByRef), then CLI commands (plan add/get/set) created clean separation. Each layer had focused tests. Pattern worked well for both plan CLI (23 tests) and plan_ref field (8 tests).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-04T09:37:48.375Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGM07T7QV2VV9Z6PY0TJEBHX\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Validation ordering for better errors - When validating references, check type mismatch (isTask/isSpecItem) before checking existence. Gives 'Reference X is not a plan' instead of 'Plan reference not found' when user passes wrong type. Applied in task add and task set --plan-ref validation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-04T09:37:50.839Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGM1RX4NR7ADX19G2FTPF0S2\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Pattern-following implementation: When implementing new CLI commands, examining similar existing commands (e.g., derive.ts for task creation patterns, plan.ts for command structure) and reusing their patterns leads to consistent, correct implementations. This approach worked well for plan derive - imports, error handling, slug generation, and bidirectional updates all followed established patterns, resulting in clean first implementation with no structural issues.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-04T10:04:39.445Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGMX3K0D0104A8JD0NWRP526\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test-driven regex debugging proved effective: wrote comprehensive tests for plan document parser's markdown section extraction (## Specs, ## Tasks, ## Implementation Notes), which immediately caught regex pattern bugs (^## anchors failed to match). Fixed patterns before integration, avoiding late-stage debugging. Pattern: write tests first for parsing/extraction logic, especially when dealing with complex patterns or unfamiliar APIs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-04T18:02:21.069Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGP14AGQRQ3QZFEHGY66T89J\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Test fixtures use @test-core module but many example commands in docs/tests assume @cli exists. Caused global find/replace in tests when module reference didn't match. Consider: (1) standardizing fixture module names to match common examples, (2) documenting fixture module structure in test helpers, or (3) adding @cli as an alias/additional module in fixtures.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T04:31:53.879Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGP14D6DF0APPMFXGEZ8EJS6\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Using createdSpecsMap to track specs during import solved parent reference resolution elegantly. Specs created in topological order could reference earlier-created specs by slug lookup in the map, working in both dry-run and real modes. Pattern: track created entities in a map keyed by slug for multi-step operations with interdependencies.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T04:31:56.621Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGP14G3BD89YS91J02VH3M01\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Acceptance criteria schema requires 'id' field but this isn't obvious when writing test plans or spec YAML. Parser validation fails silently - spec just doesn't appear in parsed output. Better error would be: 'AC missing required field: id' at parse time. Or make id optional and auto-generate if missing.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T04:31:59.595Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGP16HK67C30T8A8KMYGDFCR\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"kspec validate output is noisy with pre-existing reference errors and alignment warnings (22 ref errors, 152 alignment warnings). Makes it hard to verify whether a specific change introduced new issues. A --diff or --new-only flag that shows only issues not present in the previous commit would help.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T04:33:06.662Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGP16KZRYRE4Z921QG9WE8MC\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Plan with exact file paths, line numbers, and 'nature of change' descriptions translates directly to precise edits. The plan for ralph loop fixes had a table mapping files to changes — each row became one Edit tool call with no ambiguity.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T04:33:09.112Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGP40S7D4KXBDQ38542G9ZH7\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Vitest replaces console.log with its own implementation that doesn't flow through process.stdout.write. Tests that capture stdout.write won't see console.log output. When testing code that wraps both console.log and stdout.write, spy on console.log directly (vi.spyOn) and test stdout.write capture separately.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T05:22:23.597Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGP40YN2T598YCSXZWJWWG5T\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Tracing output flow (console.log → stdout.write chain) quickly revealed the doubled prefix bug. When debugging output duplication, mapping the full write path through all wrappers/interceptors identifies where multiple layers add the same content.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T05:22:29.154Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGP3JBQP3XWSQSW83VS8YZB4\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Commander.js optional argument pattern: When a command has an optional argument like .command('help [topic]'), the action handler signature must use (topic: string | undefined, options) NOT (topic?: string, options?). The optional TypeScript syntax breaks Commander's argument passing - options becomes an empty object. Pattern seen in task.ts commands works correctly.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T05:14:31.030Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGP3JJEWMA65YMH03YMY9XKP\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test-first implementation with AC annotations: Writing tests with AC annotations (// AC: @spec-ref ac-N) before implementation ensures complete coverage and creates clear traceability. Pattern used in help.test.ts covered all 5 ACs systematically and caught the --json flag issue early.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T05:14:37.916Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGPHG6D6WFE5AYE4V49AKBE8\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Review agent (opus subagent) caught a real validation bug - missing required 'id' field in plan document AC example. The schema check against actual parser code was the key insight. Always verify examples against actual schema definitions.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T09:18:00.102Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGPHG81NE1BNP4RX9Y7Z6YM8\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Committed directly to main forgetting branch protection requires PRs. Had to create branch after the fact and reset. Should always create feature branch first in this repo.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T09:18:01.781Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGQVA9RFHA4J4BEN5EAAMRJJ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Subagent delegation pattern: using Explore agent for codebase survey + general-purpose agent for PR review kept main context clean and session efficient during daemon strict-mode fix\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T21:28:47.119Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGQY6YCTSAKEY4FKBJTVHXEZ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Workflow run mining before prune: /reflect captured 99.4% of run content into durable artifacts. Out of 181 runs with ~100 meaningful notes, only 1 contained unique info not already tracked. Validates reflection-based knowledge capture approach.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T22:19:22.907Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGQY7097397E46Q8T1WZADDF\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"task-work-loop has 69% abort rate (11/16 runs) — almost entirely because no eligible tasks existed when started. Workflow works fine when work exists (5/5 completed all 9 steps). Root cause: ralph orchestrator starts workflow without pre-checking kspec tasks ready --eligible.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T22:19:24.839Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGQY72Q4C5V3GNRWKCJGY2MZ\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"session-reflect-loop runs too aggressively in ralph loops — 72 runs (40% of all runs), chains of up to 31 consecutive executions, vast majority capture zero new items. 113 min spent (19% of total workflow time) with questionable marginal value in consecutive chains. Should be conditional on whether preceding task-work-loop actually completed work.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T22:19:27.333Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGQY75ANKENZMWPXRNYWJYYP\",\n    \"type\": \"idea\",\n    \"content\": \"Workflow run telemetry: Before pruning old runs, mine them for aggregate stats (abort rates, durations, sequencing patterns). Consider keeping aggregate statistics even when pruning individual records to enable trend analysis. First mining found: 9.9 hrs total, PR review 36%, reflect 46%, task-work-loop 6.5%.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T22:19:30.006Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGQY77CSM15MQWKTJS05N14P\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"pr-review-merge consumes 36% of all workflow time (215 of 594 min). Step 1 (CI check) bimodal: 30 runs under 30s but 9 over 5 min. No fast-path for trivial PRs that pass all gates immediately. Consecutive chains of up to 14 suggest batch PR processing needs a dedicated workflow.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T22:19:32.121Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGQYECS40M7NHKZKJPKKEK9Y\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel subagent mining pattern: spawning 3 specialized agents (notes, patterns, gaps) to analyze the same dataset from different angles. Each found complementary insights the others missed. Effective for pre-prune data extraction.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T22:23:27.012Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGR0NMTJDKB72NAP0YEENDF3\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Subagent-driven holistic review for spec-plan design: Launching a general-purpose subagent with structured review criteria (completeness, consistency, spec coverage, edge cases) caught 2 blockers and 7 should-fix items before plan import. Pattern: write plan doc, then have subagent review against existing codebase patterns before committing.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T23:02:21.778Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGR0NPZC3QHBRCAQBQX7KV92\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Plan import drops ACs and writes malformed trait refs: Two bugs in kspec plan import discovered during batch-exec plan import. (1) ACs from Specs YAML block not written to created items. (2) Trait refs written without @ prefix causing schema errors. Both required manual workarounds. Tasks created: @01KGR0K2, @01KGR0K5.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T23:02:23.980Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Both bugs fixed in PR #319: createSpecItem() now preserves acceptance_criteria, and trait refs are normalized with @ prefix during import.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-02-06T00:25:02.261Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGR5CVAAHCBBX27FD0ZN3SVQ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Precise plan with exact file paths, line numbers, and code diffs made the plan-import bug fix session trivially fast. Plan → implement → test → PR → merge in one smooth pass with zero rework.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T00:24:56.394Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGRP6D35N9WE3EKT2KBEBC5W\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Plan-import scoped notes fix: well-scoped plan with specific line numbers and code changes led to zero-iteration implementation (all tests passed first try). Good pattern for future fix plans.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T05:18:31.013Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGS4Y7YZCP10F4FR6V38DYW5\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"WeakMap<Command, T> annotation pattern works cleanly for adding metadata to Commander commands. Avoids monkey-patching internals, is type-safe and GC-friendly, chains naturally with .command() calls (markMutating(cmd.command(...))), and integrates with extractCommandTree() by reading annotations during traversal. Reusable for future annotation types (e.g. requires-auth, idempotent). See src/cli/command-annotations.ts for reference implementation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T09:36:12.255Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGS89MKMBN56RX8RRGZBB50K\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Subagent-reviewed AC drafts: Pattern of drafting ACs → subagent review → revise → apply caught 5+ real issues (--count+--json interaction, partial success gap, missing optional flag ACs, scope creep in AC-10, missing multi-trait remove symmetry). Prevented rework during implementation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T10:34:51.380Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGTF4QA30P761909YYA8KHVK\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex CLI as external PR reviewer: running 'codex exec -m gpt-5.3-codex --sandbox danger-full-access --full-auto' with a code review prompt caught a real positional-arg-ordering bug that the implementing agent missed. Two independent reviewers (Codex + Claude CI) found complementary issues — Codex caught the arg order bug and temp dir naming, Claude CI caught the validation count mismatch and finally-block safety. Worth making this a standard part of the PR review workflow.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T21:53:44.771Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"01KGTF4Y\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-02-06T22:30:50.992Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGTF4YT5Y2233BHBFZ3S8N75\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex sandbox can't reach api.github.com: when running codex exec with --sandbox danger-full-access, network access to GitHub API was blocked, so the review comment had to be posted manually. This required reading codex output, extracting the review text, and posting via gh ourselves. A wrapper script or skill that handles the 'codex review then post' pattern would eliminate this manual step.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T21:53:52.453Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Addressed by /codex skill (PR #325). Using danger-full-access sandbox gives Codex full network access including GitHub API.\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-02-06T22:30:56.697Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGTF57CRAX3CDYVTGBRS5NTV\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Atomic copy-back was a design gap caught by reviewers, not by tests. The plan described 'copy-back' as straightforward fs.cp, but both reviewers independently flagged that delete-then-copy is not safe under I/O failure. Future plans involving filesystem atomicity should explicitly call out failure modes in the design — the happy path isn't enough.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T21:54:01.240Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGTF5E6S42VZ1FWESSMX2QZS\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Plan-driven implementation with spec-first ACs: having 22 acceptance criteria defined before coding made both implementation and testing systematic. Each test was annotated with its AC reference, and the review could verify coverage by checking annotations. The plan→spec→implement→test→review pipeline worked well for this medium-complexity feature.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T21:54:08.217Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGTH928DVA2CEA4FHH93M8MN\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex self-review loop is effective: had Codex review its own skill file, it found 4 MUST-FIX issues (invalid CLI flags, sandbox conflicts, malformed API payloads). Then had Codex review the PR with inline comments — it found 2 more issues (flag ordering, nested fences). Each round of review caught real bugs that would have caused runtime failures.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T22:31:04.206Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGTH995FGYBH7S0Z0FCRJCTC\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex exec review subcommand has different flag parsing than codex exec: -s must go before the review subcommand (codex exec -s danger-full-access review ...) not after (codex exec review -s ... fails). This flag ordering quirk isn't documented in codex --help and caused a runtime failure that required a fix commit.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T22:31:11.280Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGTH9GNRYXV1P230AB1KWJPH\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"GitHub PR review API with --input JSON file works reliably for inline comments. Pattern: write structured JSON to /tmp/codex-pr-review-body.json with {event, body, comments[{path, line, body}]}, then post via gh api repos/{o}/{r}/pulls/{n}/reviews --method POST --input file. Codex figured out the line vs position issue on its own (first attempt used line numbers which mapped to null, then corrected to diff positions).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T22:31:18.968Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGTM42H2M0WPJGE9X7CHS7MX\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex PR review as documentation quality gate: /codex pr caught real arg-name bugs in batch JSON examples that would have caused user failures. The review→fix→push cycle was fast. Worth using on all docs-heavy PRs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T23:20:46.370Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGTNY96A6TMC4J1Y4V786JMM\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex plan review as pre-import quality gate caught trait ref format bug and compound AC issues. Worth making standard practice for plan imports with 3+ specs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T23:52:33.738Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGTNYAQNT0KVK3YTF5E7ZKYD\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel subagent research (two Explore agents) during spec-plan design phase efficiently gathered session infrastructure context in ~60s instead of sequential exploration.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T23:52:35.318Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGVCEFG5NP47A9K33GS192PD\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex PR review on self-authored PRs creates review threads that trigger check-unresolved-comments CI gate. Requires manual GraphQL thread resolution + CI re-run before merging. Codex skill should either skip inline comments on own PRs or auto-resolve threads after posting.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-07T06:25:53.158Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGVCENXDGQ8QVSC7V21SDFQT\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Tracing ACP bugs through the chain (framing.ts → client.ts → spawner.ts → ralph.ts) was efficient because the codebase has clear layering and the override mechanism (methodTimeouts) was already in place. Minimal change (18 lines, 3 files) for the fix.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-07T06:25:59.725Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGVDDPDMPZ9008WHBJHGHZN6\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task @01KGVARW had excellent root cause analysis in its notes (specific file, line numbers, all call sites, exact reproduction). This made the fix trivial — under 10 minutes from start to merged PR. Detailed bug reports with root cause are high-leverage.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-07T06:42:56.052Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGVK9K0AR02A2MJBXWBFE5DH\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Batch triage workflow: categorize inbox by theme first, quick-win deletions, then one-at-a-time promotion with AskUserQuestion showing What/Why/How context. Cross-reference against git log and completed tasks to catch already-done items. This pattern processed 61 items efficiently.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-07T08:25:32.938Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGVK9MH4RRSZT8JZP7E3089F\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Implementation notes at promotion time: adding concrete implementation notes during inbox promote (not after) makes tasks self-contained for future agents. Include: which files to modify, patterns to follow, approximate scope.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-07T08:25:34.500Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGVK9P011GDQGTW9TJRE8FA9\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Automation triage forces context switch to spec creation: when assessing eligibility, discovering a task needs a spec means switching from assessment mode to authoring mode (find module, find parent, create item, add ACs, link task). Consider a guided flow or --create-spec flag on task set --automation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-07T08:25:36.001Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGWG8W1A9ZHHWCKVNVAFQM6B\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex PR review caught silent bug in session log list — tasks_completed metric searched for non-existent event type. Real task completions use session.update tool_call events with rawInput.command containing 'task complete'. Without review, feature would ship reporting 0 tasks for all real sessions.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-07T16:51:58.122Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGWG8YSAFS6GG225AV0AXPHW\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Session event data payloads are untyped — EventTypeSchema defines the type enum but data field is z.unknown(). Had to grep through real JSONL files to discover that Ralph records task completions as session.update events with sessionUpdate: 'tool_call' and rawInput.command. This caused a bug that was only caught by Codex reviewing against real data.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-07T16:52:00.939Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGXHNDY3R4AC24TS1R4Q54CA\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Commander's .option() parse function (e.g. parseInt) silently pre-coerces values before the action handler runs. When replacing inline validation with shared helpers, the helper never sees the raw string. This caused a bug in PR #347 where derive/plan-derive still accepted '3abc' as priority 3. Fix: never use Commander parse functions for options validated by shared helpers.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-08T02:35:32.675Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGXHNR4TWC7Z8V6FB5NR72XF\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Using Codex (/codex pr) as an automated second reviewer caught a real bug (Commander parseInt pre-parse bypass) that manual review missed. The review-fix-re-review cycle completed in one session. Worth using for every non-trivial PR.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-08T02:35:43.130Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGXN2YYMYG5EEFQDM5CA6C2A\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Documentation tasks that update README/AGENTS.md should also check skill files (.claude/skills/) for staleness on the same topics. Easy to miss because skills are a separate concern. A validate --skills --docs check could catch this.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-08T03:35:21.813Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGXN2Z5DF52R8XHKHYFV9XE1\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Running 4 parallel Explore/Bash subagents to research README structure, AGENTS.md structure, full CLI catalog, and recent git features simultaneously saved significant time and produced comprehensive input for the docs update.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-08T03:35:22.029Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGXN2ZATMXN5QJJQSMJVJZWC\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"AGENTS.md task state transitions documented task complete as working from in_progress/pending, but CLI actually requires pending_review (or --skip-review). Pre-existing inaccuracy that propagated to README. Codex caught it via runtime spot-checks that I did not do.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-08T03:35:22.202Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGWZ26Q5N99GVBCSF23HM253\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Stale index mutation pattern: when mutating items in a loop with a pre-built refIndex, track created slugs in a parallel Set since refIndex won't see loop-created items. Pattern: importReservedSlugs Set alongside refIndex.isSlugAvailable(). Applied in plan-import to prevent cross-namespace slug collisions within a single import run.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-07T21:10:28.325Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGWZ26T7QDNKSE0F0GSX0W5T\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex iterative review as convergence loop: codex review → fix → re-review converges on correctness. 4 rounds on PR #346 found progressively deeper cross-namespace slug collision gaps (duplicate_slug handling → plans missing from refIndex → stale index for import-created specs → spec creation not checking importReservedSlugs). Each round caught a real bug.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-07T21:10:28.423Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGWZ26WJB8X4S3SN7GPF881Q\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex review depth insufficient on first pass: 4 review rounds were needed to fully validate plan-import slug safety. Each fix introduced or revealed the next gap. Root cause: Codex reviews surface-level patterns first (wrong API check) before deeper ones (stale index across mutations). Need a way to prime Codex to reason about mutation-staleness and index invalidation upfront, possibly via a review checklist or system prompt addition to the codex skill.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-07T21:10:28.498Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGY73W0M9YD0PKC74CW5NSFR\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Test-first doc editing: building eval scenarios before trimming AGENTS.md prevented info loss. 15 scenarios + 8 stress test recall questions validated the trimmed doc (14/15 PASS, 6/8 PASS). Pattern: build test suite → make changes → validate → fix gaps.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-08T08:50:25.940Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGY73W3NX1Q0AV6KA9TZB2E9\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Stress testing with real codebase exploration is more effective than synthetic padding for finding doc gaps. Agent reads actual code (building 30k+ tokens of context), then answers recall questions. Found 2 real degradation points (PR workflow steps, scope expansion) that were reinforced.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-08T08:50:26.037Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGY73W66K9NASKQBHSKY2ZHG\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex as second reviewer on doc PRs caught a real inconsistency (scenario expected answer vs AGENTS.md rule) and a non-existent file path. Worth running on documentation PRs, not just code PRs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-08T08:50:26.118Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KGY73W872YHXWQ8VNBAQF5DD\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"GitHub PR review thread resolution requires GraphQL mutation (resolveReviewThread). REST reply endpoint posts replies but does not resolve threads. Had to discover thread node IDs via GraphQL query first.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-08T08:50:26.183Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHAAN8DMG4HYPXCQY05R9QT9\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Re-baseline research findings against current code before creating specs. In CLI agent-UX session, 7 of 21 recommendations from telemetry analysis were already implemented. Verifying each against the codebase with parallel explore agents before speccing saved significant overhead (would have created 7 unnecessary specs and 7 unnecessary tasks).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-13T01:43:14.612Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHCYW7KKRGN2MV594S8YZMXH\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Commander.js parent-action option routing: when parent and subcommands define the same options, Commander doesn't cleanly route them. Tried passThroughOptions (requires global enablePositionalOptions, breaks --json global option), ended up using allowUnknownOption + temporary Command re-parse. Pattern works but is non-idiomatic. If more command groups need default actions, consider extracting this into a shared utility.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-14T02:15:03.539Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHFCMD893TQMFJWQY84RR59C\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel subagent research pattern: launching 4+ research agents simultaneously on different aspects of the same question (cross-project audit, usage patterns, external ecosystem, install story) produced comprehensive non-overlapping findings in ~6 minutes. Much more effective than sequential investigation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-15T00:53:56.105Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHFCMDBFRWBZ1P7NFFH8J7RA\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Dual-reviewer pattern for plans: having both an internal holistic reviewer (Claude) and an external reviewer (Codex) independently review the same plan catches complementary issues. Internal finds code-level integration problems, external finds architectural concerns. Both agreed on the same critical issues (compound ACs, inline YAML). Three revision cycles (v1 reviewed v2 reviewed v3) produced significantly stronger output.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-15T00:53:56.207Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHFCMDEATQ0R2Q4WW4979DQA\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Iterative clarifying questions with ask tool: asking one question at a time with 3-4 concrete options (each with descriptions) before synthesizing research into a plan led to well-informed decisions. User could respond quickly because each question had enough context from the research. Better than presenting a full plan and asking for feedback.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-15T00:53:56.298Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHFPVSVMKQTR0DZCVVZ2QS6J\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"CLI commands targeting main project files (like .claude/skills/) must use ctx.rootDir, not ctx.specDir or path.dirname(ctx.specDir). The specDir is the spec content location (.kspec/ in shadow mode), while rootDir is always the project root. Using dirname(specDir) fails in shadow mode because .kspec/ is a worktree at the project root level. Encountered in skill render command where files were written to /tmp/ instead of project root.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-15T03:52:44.148Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHHR77A38WS28NJSMWG2FN0R\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Structured interview (one question at a time with pro/con analysis) before planning leads to well-reasoned architecture decisions. User engagement is higher when they see trade-offs laid out clearly.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-15T22:54:55.811Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHHR77CK3KME4QHCS62H0JFH\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Running both internal Plan agent review AND Codex review-plan on the same plan catches complementary issues. Internal review finds code-level gaps; Codex finds spec quality issues.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-15T22:54:55.891Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHHR77EW34VT6EEW1NZHK6YF\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"kspec batch uses kebab-case args (depends-on) but schema fields use snake_case (depends_on). Inconsistency causes trial-and-error on first batch use.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-15T22:54:55.964Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHKTQNHA07MZXGVJQHQAW7CA\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel subagent review of ralph loop: 5 agents reviewing different PR ranges (371-376, 377-384, 385-393, 394-402, test suite) completed in ~3min wall clock. Independent agents finding the same duplication issues confirms real problems vs noise. Effective pattern for post-loop quality review.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-16T18:17:20.683Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHKTQNN38FSK8SAEJ34G0P6F\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop PR-by-PR review process misses cross-PR duplication accumulation. PR #381 added rendering utils, #383 duplicated them in a new file, #394 consolidated render functions but missed the utilities, #401 added more dead code. Each PR passes review individually but the aggregate drift is significant (24 inbox items from one loop). Consider adding a consolidation/cleanup iteration every N PRs or at loop end.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-16T18:17:20.803Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHQXGWG6BEEQBJ0VZ32NX2T1\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Background PR review agent can act on stale context: agent added 172-line test file for a spec that was deleted during review. When running review agents in background while making spec/task changes in foreground, the agent does not see those changes. Required a follow-up cleanup PR.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-18T08:23:01.894Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHQXGWQJGKKY7H3KKRDXT5HQ\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex PR review skill always demands // AC: @spec-ref ac-N annotations, even for infrastructure/cleanup tasks where ACs describe absence of code. Should skip AC annotation checks when task has no spec_ref or when spec type is not user-facing behavior.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-18T08:23:02.130Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHRP78K7727DMKA224B3ZZ9Y\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Running kspec setup during development creates kspec-agents.md and .claude/skills/ in project root. These are test artifacts for the kspec project itself (which uses AGENTS.md, not kspec-agents.md). They trigger repeated stop hook warnings about uncommitted changes. Need either: (a) test isolation so setup tests dont leak into project root, or (b) cleanup step in bootstrap/dev workflow.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-18T15:34:40.999Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHRP78PDNPQAKZCPHR5XZV86\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Multi-model PR review (Claude + Codex in parallel) caught issues that single-model review missed. Codex found missing debugLog in outer catch and weak test assertions. Worth continuing this pattern for non-trivial PRs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-18T15:34:41.101Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHRYZ569SCKS1HAFJK71Y2Z7\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel dual-reviewer strategy (Claude agent + Codex) is effective: Claude validates correctness, Codex catches spec-alignment gaps. Use both for PRs with spec ACs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-18T18:07:32.554Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHSG0CSF18QF1S4MMMEM3S8Y\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex PR review (gpt-5.3-codex) caught a real correctness bug in drift detection (hash-gating for sidecar changes) that the implementing agent missed. Codex reproduced the issue locally with a concrete script. High value for code review.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-18T23:05:18.896Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHSKZDW60J9YF6XTJ2WZDDE5\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Refactoring tasks without spec_ref have AC traceability gap — task-level ACs in notes aren't discoverable by standard // AC: @spec-ref ac-N annotation pattern. Codex review flagged this on PR #411. Options: (1) allow // AC: @task-ref ac-N, (2) require spec items even for refactoring, (3) teach reviewers to check task notes. Related: @task-skill-module-split had no spec_ref but defined 3 ACs in notes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-19T00:14:41.542Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHT79F7K2QV2HKNRTD0JQTJ1\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Guard script bash code embedded in JS template literal makes quote escaping painful — single quotes inside tr/sed cause parse errors. Consider extracting guard scripts to standalone .sh files loaded at setup time instead of inline template literals.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-19T05:52:13.555Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHT79FAZJZ43QN3BZA28KQYM\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Running codex review in parallel with PR review agent caught a real security bypass (split-quote git \\\"reset\\\" --hard). The dual-reviewer pattern (code-level + quality-gate) provides meaningful coverage overlap.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-19T05:52:13.663Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHVE714TTNEME761Y1783EYC\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Shared test fixture fragility: tests/fixtures/kynetic.meta.yaml is used by multiple test files. Tests that append YAML keys (like meta.test.ts appending conventions:) collide when the fixture gains new top-level keys. Caused real regression in PR #413. Consider per-test fixture isolation or fixture composition helpers.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-19T17:12:28.058Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHVE7189BCM4HWW9PXWAFP37\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel agent reviews (Codex + /pr-review) found complementary issues: Codex caught test annotation gaps, review agent caught shared fixture regression. Multi-reviewer pattern is high-value for quality.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-19T17:12:28.169Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHVYHKAVN1G54X8C2BJYMK3X\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Invoked /spec-plan skill but wrote implementation guide instead of plan-import-format document. User had explicitly said /spec-plan. Lesson: invoking a skill is not enough — must follow its output format from the FIRST write. When /spec-plan is invoked for plan mode, write the plan file in kspec plan import format (# Title, ## Specs with YAML code block, ## Tasks, ## Implementation Notes) from the start.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-19T21:57:51.579Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHVYHKEBF6AHDDXVQZJAZV5H\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Dual review pattern before plan import: running both an internal plan review agent and Codex in parallel caught YAML quoting failures and substantive spec gaps (batch mode, worktree detection, remote type algorithm). Reviews converged on same must-fixes, giving high confidence. Always dual-review complex plan documents before importing.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-19T21:57:51.691Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHVYHKH7J728F29ZS1SGF2PM\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel consumer project exploration: launching 3 agents to explore kynetic-bot, imgen, comfy-ecaj-nodes simultaneously produced convergent findings (same Quick Start pattern, same hooks, same skill drift) that were far more convincing than exploring one project. Use parallel exploration when researching cross-project patterns.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-19T21:57:51.783Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHW3CC8V4PDG1R22S5229TA4\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Dual review pattern (internal Plan agent + Codex review-plan) catches complementary issues. Internal agent finds architectural concerns, Codex finds format/structure issues. Convergent findings give high confidence. Worth standardizing for all plan imports.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-19T23:22:23.387Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHW3CCBSNYH48BKQX2Q2CNAC\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Post-import verification agent catches data integrity issues that dry-run misses (null spec_ref, missing implementation notes). Should be part of standard plan import workflow.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-19T23:22:23.481Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHWVQNZV7NDDTQB5ADP4FPCW\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"GitHub blocks REQUEST_CHANGES on own PR. Ralph review subagents operate under the same GitHub credentials as the PR author, so they cannot post REQUEST_CHANGES reviews — only COMMENT. The pr-review skill instructs posting APPROVE or REQUEST_CHANGES, but REQUEST_CHANGES will always fail in self-authored PRs. Need either: (1) a separate GitHub bot account for review agents, or (2) the skill should use COMMENT event with structured review content instead of REQUEST_CHANGES.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-20T06:27:59.612Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHWVQP3NBA0YYME4FY9K2T0W\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Dual-reviewer pattern (Claude agent + Codex) for PR review. Running both in parallel on PR #424 gave convergent findings on the critical branch-lookup bug (independent discovery by both). Codex also caught input validation gap that Claude missed. Different models find different issues — convergent findings give high confidence, divergent findings expand coverage.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-20T06:27:59.733Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHWVQP6YEJ0241DN6F4QA54J\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel review audit pattern: spawning 4 specialized subagents (worker process adherence, review process adherence, code quality, spec/AC coverage) to evaluate a ralph session. Each agent had a focused lens and found complementary issues. Total wall-clock time ~2 min for what would have been 15+ min of sequential analysis.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-20T06:27:59.838Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHYTNNGG0B44BK1QJMRGNYZA\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Dual review convergence: running both pr-review subagent and /codex review in parallel catches different issues and convergent findings give high confidence. Both flagged dead verifyTaskCompleted code independently.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-21T00:47:53.872Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHZ6H8YSJYW5Z9TDSA3PSRJX\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Convention vs template mental model clarified: Templates carry kspec-generic content (shadow branch, task lifecycle, ralph loop — same for ALL kspec projects). Conventions carry project-specific rules (testing gotchas, dev setup, CI limitations — unique per project). When porting content from AGENTS.md, ask: does this apply to every kspec project? Template. Only this project? Convention.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-21T04:15:12.858Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHZBEEVJXMQ6TYQCP2584JKT\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Spec-before-implement pattern: adding ac-6 to @agent-instruction-gen before coding the noop behavior made test coverage natural and caught the right contract upfront.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-21T05:41:03.474Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KHZHZAQJE6KF7GHBEK2E79PK\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"task get not showing descriptions meant had to grep raw YAML to verify task content after batch creation. Critical gap for agents working on tasks — they cannot read the description via CLI.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-21T07:35:07.762Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ1A32GV14R9ZSDBQYCKFW3V\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Platform behavior assumption: PR #440 added namespace rendering (.claude/skills/kspec/<id>/) without verifying Claude Code actually discovers nested skill directories. It does not. Future platform integration work should verify discovery behavior (e.g. create a test skill, check if Claude Code lists it) before building rendering pipelines around assumed directory structures.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-21T23:55:50.683Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ1RW3898SCWYZN358637199\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Meta vs manifest confusion: skill render reads from meta (shadow branch), not template manifest. Changing manifest ID without updating meta has no effect. Need to delete+re-add skill via CLI.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T04:14:10.697Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ331N2YAJ66MXHK1W9J9HQX\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel subagent research pattern: launching 3+ research agents simultaneously to investigate different aspects (code state, git history, task completions) builds comprehensive evidence in ~3 minutes vs 15+ sequentially. Critical for large triage sessions (95 items). Each agent gets a focused investigation scope and returns structured findings.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T16:31:12.990Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3M13X05B558KQ58AXRM1K1\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Zod superRefine pattern for status-dependent field requirements (e.g., triaged requires reasoning/decided_by, acted_on requires acted_at). Should be the default approach for any schema with status lifecycle — flat .optional() misses state invariants. First used in triage.ts, should apply to plan.ts and similar.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T21:28:01.184Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3T9X36SS737DYRWW9QE9ZV\",\n    \"type\": \"idea\",\n    \"content\": \"Spec gap test\\n\\nReasoning: needs spec\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T23:17:40.582Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ3X7D52RR2R6N3MS45Y7EE6\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"CI timing race: when Codex posts a review comment after CI check-unresolved-comments has already run, the check fails because the new thread is unresolved. Requires manual re-run after resolving. Consider: (1) make check-unresolved-comments a required-last check, (2) have the review workflow auto-re-run the check after resolving threads, or (3) add a gh run rerun step to the codex review skill.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T00:08:44.450Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4SJP2673H5V8NHJPMNNN7X\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"[spec-gap] Include triage records in static snapshot (kspec-snapshot.json). Currently the snapshot format (KspecSnapshot type) doesn't include triage records, so the triage page in static/GitHub Pages mode shows an empty state with a notice instead of displaying existing triage decisions read-only. AC-8 of @interactive-triage-ui expects read-only display. Needs: add triage records to export snapshot, update KspecSnapshot type, add fetchTriageRecordsStatic to read from snapshot.\\n\\nReasoning: There's a spec gap here\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:24:14.150Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4SJP5TREMPX687MHBW8Y2Q\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"[spec-gap] Cross-feature requirement pattern: How to express that core features (search, validate, export) must support all entity types. When new entity type added, should automatically imply tasks for core features. Options: (1) applies_to field on feature specs, (2) trait on entity types like @trait-searchable, (3) validation warning for missing coverage, (4) parent spec that entity types must satisfy. Surfaced when realizing search doesn't cover inbox.\\n\\nReasoning: first item reasoning\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:24:14.266Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4SNE9GHZMFEE49D3P4CKJZ\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"[spec-gap] kspec validate @spec or @task — targeted validation that checks a single spec/task's AC coverage against codebase. Not full approval, just verifies each AC has at least one // AC: annotation in test files. Would make trait AC gaps immediately visible during task-work. Could be used by local-review skill as a concrete check instead of relying on agent diligence.\\n\\nReasoning: Must-have but needs spec design - targeted kspec validate for single item\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:25:44.496Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4SNFHF46MCSST52ZMWXJ1R\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"[spec-gap] Design section configuration for agents generate — allow projects to control which sections appear (skills table, conventions, workflows, static templates). Key questions: where does config live, include vs exclude list, defaults, custom sections, ordering, data vs template distinction, migration path. See plan doc for full requirements.\\n\\nReasoning: Must-have but needs spec design - section configuration for agents generate\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:25:45.775Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ4VDK8ECG1W5T95TPP1KVF6\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Pre-analyzed triage report (HTML artifact) combined with kspec batch made processing 107 inbox items efficient. Record-then-act pattern provided good audit trail. Pattern: analyze offline, port decisions via batch.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T08:56:24.590Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ50B8SFBX6C1E9XRYBXZ22Q\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"settings.json written by 3 independent subsystems during setup (installClaudeCodeHooks, seedPermissions, enablePluginInProject via modifyJsonAtomic). Makes skip-when-unchanged optimization impossible without either a shared coordinator or consolidating all mutations into one function. Each writer reads, modifies, writes independently — interleaving prevents simple content comparison.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T10:22:31.215Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ51NBSJR7R8ZRT4RM8Q26DT\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Post-merge branch state: When inheriting a session where a PR was already merged, the working directory may be on main. Always check branch (git branch --show-current) before committing, and create a feature branch first. Recovering from an accidental main commit requires creating a branch from HEAD and resetting main.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T10:45:30.546Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ5B3SSRXMPW76HE43H15EKS\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex PR review caught a real type drift bug (Convention.validation schema mismatch) during web-ui type deduplication PR. The shared-type approach works well: define in @kynetic-ai/shared, re-export from web-ui, enforce with static analysis test. Dual review (Codex + CI) catches complementary issues.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T13:30:40.824Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ63RW7JFBTJ7FWG6MQR3W71\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel subagent audit pattern: launching 4+ agents in parallel for deep-dive review of ralph loop work (PR quality, functional verification, loop behavior, process adherence) produced comprehensive results in ~90 seconds. Effective for post-loop quality assessment.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T20:41:37.266Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ63RWAKZWYCWNNG68KFBHBX\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Dual review pattern (internal agent + Codex) for plan review catches different issue categories. Internal agent found consistency gaps; Codex found concurrency risks. Convergent findings give high confidence before implementation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T20:41:37.364Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ71CSSQNCH8KAP3YRSQT4GY\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"@trait-semantic-exit-codes ACs hardcode exit code numbers (ac-2: 'exit code 1', ac-3: 'exit code 2', ac-4: 'exit code 3') that don't match kspec's actual EXIT_CODES scheme (ERROR=1, USAGE_ERROR=2, NOT_FOUND=3, VALIDATION_FAILED=4). Every command adding trait AC test coverage needs clarifying comments explaining the mapping. Fix: update trait ACs to use semantic descriptions ('non-zero exit code indicating validation failure') instead of hardcoded numbers, or update to match kspec's actual codes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T05:19:18.839Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ731A1QK5ZZG40DNSERD1MD\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex review caught fail-open bug in getBudget() — corrupt budget.json was silently treated as 'no budget', effectively disabling enforcement. Changed to fail closed (only ENOENT returns null, parse/validation errors propagate). Pattern: for security/enforcement code, always default to the restrictive path. Codex consistently catches error-handling path issues that internal review misses.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T05:47:59.416Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ73MEZ9BFMX73JFB0ZDSJVM\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph task-limit-guard hook blocks gh pr create even when finishing current task work. The guard treats all Bash commands equally — it can't distinguish 'creating a PR for completed work' from 'starting new task work'. Result: branch pushed but PR not created, requiring next iteration to finish. Consider whitelisting gh pr create or detecting PR creation context in the guard.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T05:58:27.050Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ75K21W6FB80AB5567TBKAX\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"task set --depends-on replaces all deps rather than appending. When setting multiple deps in separate batch commands, only the last one survives. Must provide all deps in a single call. Consider adding --add-depends-on for append semantics (similar to --relates-to on item set which appends).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T06:32:38.204Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ75RQEGNKHH82MGZK6Z4NXC\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Dual plan review (internal agent + /codex review-plan) catches complementary issues: internal finds design gaps and terminology problems, codex finds code-level feasibility issues (missing APIs, wrong method names, breaking consumers). Convergent findings indicate high confidence. Used successfully for session-start-redesign plan.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T06:35:43.952Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ77DA9VYBRRT8BCTVGAJC0T\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Budget enforcement in task start integrates cleanly: check before transition, increment after save, resume case handled by existing early return. The library functions (checkBudget/incrementBudget) do the heavy lifting — CLI handler just wires them together. Good separation of concerns between store.ts and task.ts.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T07:04:27.195Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ82GPNAENV2SH3Q8XYJBQA9\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel agent spawning for session log audit: 5 agents analyzing different log files simultaneously gave comprehensive coverage. Pattern worth replicating for any multi-file analysis task.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T14:58:09.706Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ8EE76AQYX301F9A34XXPWK\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"setupTempFixtures() returns a flat dir where tempDir IS the specDir — no .kspec/ wrapper. Agents that assume nested structure (path.join(tempDir, \\\".kspec\\\")) get silent test failures. AGENTS.md test helpers table should note this.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T18:26:31.242Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ8J44C5EXHEAAPHTVC71R0B\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Mock ACP agent pattern (tests/fixtures/mock-acp-agent.mjs) enables fast behavioral testing of ralph subprocess orchestration. Tests real env injection, budget cleanup, and signal handling in ~2s each. Key enabler: --adapter-cmd flag + spawnRalphUntil helper that watches output markers then kills the process.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T19:30:54.981Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ8J44G2VMVX31VYM83FP9TN\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph CLI uses --max-loops but internal variables and log messages say iterations. Minor naming inconsistency that causes confusion when writing tests or debugging. Example: --max-loops 1 but logs Starting ralph loop (max 1 iterations).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T19:30:55.106Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ8NDTX3WCBCC198CJAQQSZN\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex PR review caught exec()+unref() not actually preventing event loop hang (stdio pipes still buffered). Validated that /codex review-pr adds real value beyond rubber-stamping.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T20:28:38.691Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ8QR2WD5BSVEMKJ4R4K0JET\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Pure function pattern for hook/guard commands: exporting the core logic as a testable pure function (e.g. evaluateWorktreeGuard) with stdin/process handling in the CLI layer enables fast unit testing (44 tests, no I/O) while keeping the CLI integration tests minimal (7 tests for protocol compliance). Replicate this pattern for future hook commands.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T21:09:11.693Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ8R05R2GJBCGFQHY966GDD8\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Plan-derived tasks with depends_on sometimes become no-ops because the dependency task already implements all shared spec ACs. Seen in iteration 3: @update-setup-with-migration-cleanup (all 6 ACs done by @implement-native-worktree-guard) and @add-multi-harness-env-injection (all injection ACs done by @implement-session-create-command). Wastes budget starts and discovery time. Potential fix: plan import could warn when multiple tasks share a spec and one depends on the other, or task start could auto-detect 'AC already covered' and offer to close.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T21:13:36.770Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ8X527NACE7S92M7120K6A3\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Session checkpoint hook fires repeatedly on research-only sessions with pre-existing uncommitted changes from a different task. No way to signal this is a read-only investigation session.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T22:43:39.893Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJ8XQFTK1B2Y3CVE6XBQ2WP0\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Cross-cutting skill updates need checklist: When a concept spans multiple skills (e.g., spec context discovery in codex, pr-review, local-review, review template), updating one skill without checking all related ones leads to inconsistency. Codex review on PR #511 found 4 findings where the dig-deeper pattern wasn't applied uniformly. Consider: a way to tag related skills, or a pre-commit check that flags partial updates to skill groups.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T22:53:43.636Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJA6SXWS8W28JRSS5B1D227N\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel audit agents pattern: spawning 4 specialized agents (code quality, test quality, non-test code, process quality) in parallel gives comprehensive coverage in ~2 min wall clock. Each agent needs clear scope boundaries and structured output format.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-25T10:51:35.193Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJA9BTHR62240G32RM5P0VBP\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex skill silently exits with no output when OPENAI_API_KEY is not set. The skill documents gh auth preflight but not API key validation. Agents waste time discovering this. Skill should check for API key and fail fast with clear message.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-25T11:36:18.744Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJAAGK1RK0N21TTF843NZWV6\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Session test helper extraction (task @01KJ9ZDE) went smoothly. The all-fields-optional SessionContext pattern works well for tests that each need a different subset of fields — TypeScript structural typing handles it naturally. Reduced ~315 lines of duplication across 6 files into 2 shared modules. The inbox helpers needed a tempDir parameter change (closure → explicit arg) which was the main mechanical transformation.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-25T11:56:23.481Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJB02BPX9CYWJV8MKWKAG10R\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"testUlid('PREFIX') returns identical values across calls without explicit sequence argument — deterministic with default sequence=0. Caused false-positive test pass in session-checkpoint-scoping tests where mySession and otherSession were identical. Fix options: auto-incrementing counter, require sequence param, or rename to testUlidDeterministic to make behavior obvious. testUlids() works correctly but is easy to overlook.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-25T18:13:05.885Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJBJX00DRJV7AG07Q57HQY2Y\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Self-validating task pattern: created a P1 automation-eligible task whose acceptance criteria IS verifying the fix works. Ralph picks it up, the task checks its own session_id stamp, and the result documents whether the fix works end-to-end. Useful for testing harness-level integration that can't be verified from inside an active session.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-25T23:42:13.006Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJBTMZJE38BW62X2QG6CMYYK\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Elysia body schema validation returns 422 (not 400) before the handler runs. When writing E2E tests for daemon endpoints that have body schema validation (t.Object(...)), missing/invalid body fields return 422. If the handler also has manual validation that returns 400, the schema check fires first. Account for this in test assertions — do not assume 400 for missing body fields on Elysia-validated routes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T01:57:39.023Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJBW3RSM37ERH1SJ37DYHRB3\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"GitHub PR thread resolution requires GraphQL mutation (resolveReviewThread), not REST API. REST API only supports replies. Pattern: get thread node IDs via graphql query on pullRequest.reviewThreads, then loop resolveReviewThread mutations. Reliably resolved all 7 threads in one pass.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T02:23:12.180Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJBW3RXM0JGWW5GP8KBE53C6\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"scanTestCoverage() only scanned rootDir/tests/ — missed packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/ where Playwright E2E specs with AC annotations live. Fixed by extending scan to also cover the E2E directory and .spec.ts/.spec.js file extensions. Risk: any future E2E test directory additions would silently miss coverage until the scan list is updated. Consider making E2E scan paths configurable or convention-documented.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T02:23:12.308Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJC3JSTA7DXYJ8QRZJ341KS8\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Trait N/A annotations placed inside JSDoc block comments are not machine-parseable — the '* // AC:' pattern (where * is the JSDoc line prefix) does not match the scanner's '// AC:' regex. Must use standalone // AC: line comments OUTSIDE any /** ... */ block. Occurred in api-meta.spec.ts E2E tests, caught by Codex review, required fix commit.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T04:33:44.778Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJCVXZYRRDSMSAA2AN5TPVWR\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"AC annotation verification gap: Tests annotated with wrong AC refs (e.g., Elysia 422 tests annotated as ac-23 when ac-23 requires 400+{error,details}; POST body validation annotated as ac-5/6/7 when those are for X-Kspec-Dir header). Fix: always run kspec item get @spec-ref and read AC text before annotating tests.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T11:39:17.337Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJCXMR5S7ZZJ2DYQR7FEHXSA\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex retrospective PR review workflow: /codex pr on merged PRs surfaces real issues. Found stale dist/ bug via retro review of PR #547 that live review missed.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T12:09:11.609Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJD309GMRXFSRKWNJ6KD3MTY\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"JS date validation gotcha in E2E tests: new Date(\\\"invalid\\\") returns Invalid Date but does NOT throw. Tests using expect(() => new Date(x)).not.toThrow() or try/catch will always pass even with malformed timestamps - false positive. Always use isNaN(new Date(x).getTime()) for timestamp format validation. Caught this in api-websocket.spec.ts timestamp assertion (AC-29/@trait-websocket-protocol ac-3).\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T13:42:52.692Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJD309N30QVB8RRSD7A9J3CV\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"CI check-unresolved-comments timing race in review fix cycle: When Codex posts inline review comments on a PR, we push a fix commit which triggers CI immediately. The check-unresolved-comments job runs BEFORE we resolve the Codex threads via GraphQL, causing it to fail on the new commit. Then requires manual workflow re-run. Mitigation: always resolve all review threads BEFORE pushing any fix commits during a review cycle.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T13:42:52.835Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJD309R4M9JR7EDRZPE91AEA\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"window.__testWs pattern for Playwright WebSocket E2E: Store native browser WebSocket in window.__testWs via page.evaluate() and access it across subsequent evaluate() calls. Browser context maintains the global between calls. Enables clean helper functions (connectWebSocket, sendAndWaitForAck, subscribeAndWaitForBroadcast) without needing Playwright WebSocket interception. Used successfully in packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/api-websocket.spec.ts.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T13:42:52.932Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJD6M8MHMH09W8NJ504S0D0R\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"When deleting test files that cover spec ACs, kspec validate does not warn that AC annotations are being removed. This means coverage regressions are only caught during Codex review after the PR is up — requiring an extra fix commit. A pre-delete validate or a local-review gate that checks 'these AC annotations would disappear' would catch this earlier. Observed during task-delete-static-analysis-tests (PR #558): deleted web-ui-triage.test.ts removed all @interactive-triage-ui ac-1..ac-8 coverage; Codex caught it, required creating triage.spec.ts to recover.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T14:46:12.882Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJD933WJ6W0FBY150BET1PZN\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"PR merged by review subagent while worker agent still editing files on same branch — local branch switches to main automatically, all pending Edit tool changes silently lost. Caused significant rework this session (re-applying all triage.spec.ts changes on new branch fix/triage-ac6-session-close-error). The review subagent and worker agent operate concurrently on the same branch in a fix cycle, creating a race condition. Potential mitigations: (1) worker agent checks for branch changes before editing, (2) ralph serializes review subagent after worker fully stops, (3) worker agent uses a local patch/stash before any branch changes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T15:29:16.691Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDFFJGEQ0R6JST5PR2JZVN4\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Dual review pattern (internal plan review + /codex review-plan) catches complementary issues — format vs substance. Worth standardizing for all plan imports.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T17:20:56.334Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDFFJK5FZ5DBANYTJEVH6Q9\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Shadow branch merge driver handles complex YAML conflicts (project.tasks.yaml with 38 divergent commits) automatically during rebase — reliable for ralph parallel sessions.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T17:20:56.421Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDN04RM1EHW2FKD5SRD3Y95\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Dual review pattern (plan agent + Codex) catches complementary issues. Plan agent validates design, Codex validates contracts and test coverage. Worth keeping as standard practice for non-trivial PRs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T18:57:22.197Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ0ZTHNQF93KHS4516B8C6\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"[spec-gap] Merge driver: auto-resolve .kspec-agents-hash file conflicts (deterministic hash, should always take latest)\\n\\nReasoning: Merge driver for hash file — low frequency conflict, manual resolution works\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:47.057Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ0ZZPZZY4TE3CX11Q65BP\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"[spec-gap] Plan import: generate richer task descriptions from Implementation Notes section — include file paths, what to change, verification steps instead of generic 'See plan...' text\\n\\nReasoning: Plan import richer descriptions — improvement, not blocking\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:47.222Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ114YVRSMJQSKZ2P4CQW0\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"[spec-gap] Triage ac-5 says sets result_ref but delete action may not produce one. Verify behavior and update spec or add test assertion.\\n\\nReasoning: Triage ac-5 result_ref for delete — spec may be wrong, needs verification\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:48.414Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ119THNSN93R18BVCPZSN\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"[spec-gap] Triage API spec says ac-4 and ac-5 use PUT method but implementation uses POST /:ref/override and POST /:ref/act. Spec needs updating to match reality.\\n\\nReasoning: Triage API spec PUT vs POST mismatch — spec needs updating to match implementation\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:48.570Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1281SE4DYG57NR127DKN\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"[spec-gap] @cmd-validate spec is stale — missing flags: --completeness, --staleness, --drift, --alignment, --skills, --conventions (all already implemented in code). Pre-existing drift, not introduced by trait AC task.\\n\\nReasoning: @cmd-validate spec is stale — missing 6 flags already in code. Spec drift.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:49.537Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ14VW0MD9YQ077ZM45MVQ\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"[spec-gap] kspec meta set convention: add --update-rule and --remove-rule flags. Currently the only way to fix a rule is to delete the entire convention and recreate it. Surfaced during skill CLI lookups task when codex review caught a wording issue in one rule.\\n\\nReasoning: Convention --update-rule — DX improvement, workaround is delete+recreate\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:52.221Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDR3S3ZJRMAB0M35SQEGXRM\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Triage record-then-act pattern with UI review works well at scale: batch-record 41 decisions, user reviews/overrides in web UI, batch-act on confirmed. Clean separation of agent proposals from user decisions. 12 overrides out of 41 shows useful agent-human collaboration.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:51:47.071Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDV6RXJE25G2B3QRF02MYW3\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex two-pass review pattern effective: implement → codex review → fix bug found → re-review clean. Caught missing previousValue in injectCodexEnv that would have broken Ralph cleanup.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T20:45:50.899Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDXCB7E87A4EYJKK009VQ2K\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Well-decomposed task descriptions with exact files and verification criteria make implementation fast — the per-adapter-auto-approve task took one focused session from start to merged PR.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T21:23:50.639Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDXCBBHHBBKXDKV5Z74BX7B\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"MOCK_ACP_VERIFY_ARGS_FILE pattern extends the existing env var verification pattern cleanly — behavioral test infrastructure for ACP agent spawning is now solid.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T21:23:50.769Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDZV06SJXM9RG4YPXRXHBHQ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex PR review as iterative second reviewer catches real bugs. Two-round pattern (review → fix → re-review) provides high-confidence quality gate for ralph adapter/env code.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T22:06:48.025Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDZV0AJP3K3RNTZ3A9ZXQFC\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Plan-derived task descriptions with exact line numbers and numbered change steps make implementation fast and focused. The plan-to-task pipeline produces high-quality work items.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T22:06:48.146Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJEVM2Y2ZXMSY10GNP2CMBCV\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"When posting content containing $ and angle-bracket placeholders via shell-wrapped commands, interpolation can silently mutate task/PR notes; prefer literal-safe quoting or file-based payloads.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T06:12:21.570Z\",\n    \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJEVMQJJZ127WW5CHM0KQK16\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Portable {skill:<id>} tokens with renderer-side platform resolution reduced template duplication and kept Claude/Codex invocation guidance consistent across SKILL.md and supporting markdown.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T06:12:42.706Z\",\n    \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGAE26H74N8C0ZTZ6HH5V2N\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel plan review (Plan agent + Codex) catches complementary issues: architectural concerns vs format/structural issues. High convergence on edge cases gives confidence. Worth standardizing as a dual-review step.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T19:50:27.281Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGAE2A5KKANQDY4KRZWFM9W\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Plan-derived tasks need manual follow-up (batch set tags + note) to be automation-ready. The derive step should produce standalone tasks.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T19:50:27.397Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGAKM10AY9KFR9JXBWFFCGX\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Core skill update UX gap: kspec skill update is version-gated, so same-version template edits are skipped and require kspec skill install-core. This is non-obvious during local template iteration. Improve guidance (update vs install-core) or adjust command behavior to detect local template changes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": \"@session-reflect\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T19:53:29.377Z\",\n    \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": \"@01KJGQVK\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGFKJ79GAK3QF33QHRMYWJW\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Holistic plan review (plan + derived specs + tasks + traits together) before any code is written caught 6 spec gaps in @plan-auto-close-stale-active-sessions including missing targeting semantics, liveness guard, corrupt events handling, and task dependency ordering. Pattern: evaluate the full derivation tree, not just individual specs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T21:20:50.410Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGQCA1DEK15Y59X5M8N5HR5\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex PR review threads require manual GraphQL resolution + CI re-trigger before merge. Multi-step dance every time codex posts inline comments.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T23:36:41.261Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGQCA7649GZMT2HA0Z5CXQA\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Iterative codex review loop (review → fix → re-review) converges well. Three rounds on PR #582 caught duplicate label, spec alignment drift, and missing test branch.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T23:36:41.446Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGQKPWM32W85246H3VAWDD0\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Targeted dry-run + focused test loop quickly exposed core-skill source-of-truth drift; package-distribution test caught stale plugin artifact path immediately.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": \"@session-reflect\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T23:40:43.797Z\",\n    \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGW8ZB984E1QZHMGGCHSRXR\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"CLI tests that execute dist artifacts can produce misleading failures when dist is stale; this creates avoidable debugging churn before the real code behavior is evaluated.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T01:02:14.889Z\",\n    \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGW8ZFQ697G7Z8T81MTXN35\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Using a focused validate mode matrix (schema/refs/alignment/completeness/staleness + combinations) quickly verified scoped semantics and prevented regressions while keeping turnaround fast.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T01:02:15.031Z\",\n    \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJJHARH9G3CT7R978K6AEBZ4\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Isolated worktree + backup branch pattern for shadow branch recovery. Creating a backup branch before destructive ops, then using /tmp worktree for experimental rebase, then patching the result back as a normal commit avoided force-push entirely. This pattern should be documented for future shadow branch divergence scenarios.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T16:29:27.977Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJJHARMST4YEMPE7PYSVXSCA\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Merge driver silent data loss when --non-interactive flag missing from git config. No error, no warning — just hangs on stdin and leaves files unmerged. 12 task completions lost silently. Root cause: shadow.ts registration code path diverged from actual git config. Fix tracked in @01KJJGJ1.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T16:29:28.089Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJJT519QTQXSJWRM17W06HH6\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex PR review takes 10+ minutes because npm test subagent polling is inefficient. Consider instructing Codex to skip full suite and rely on CI, or use test shards instead of full npm test.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T19:03:37.528Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJJT51HXZZBH71BXK6VXKM15\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex PR review cannot distinguish pre-existing test failures from regressions. Flags false positives (e.g. session-budget-integration flakiness on PR #590). Could pre-seed known-flaky test list or compare failure counts against main baseline.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T19:03:37.790Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJJT51PHNAYJRJFMW7HQHMXH\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex-then-fix cycle on PR #601 was tight: review posted, ac-9 gap caught, fixed in 1 commit, thread resolved, CI passed, merged. Total turnaround ~15 min including CI.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T19:03:37.937Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJK7F4JXEBF205YJ30MK5XS0\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task budget guard blocks needs_work fix cycle transitions. kspec task start @ref fails with budget exhausted even when the task is in needs_work state (an existing fix cycle, not a new task start). needs_work → in_progress should be exempt from the budget guard since it is resuming prior work, not starting new work. Had to skip task state transitions and create PR without proper submit flow.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T22:56:20.063Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJK7F4T0JVSCB40JEAN9PHGP\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Minimal floating-promise fix pattern: storing async function result in a variable and attaching .catch(() => {}) before Promise.race is the clean way to prevent Node.js 22 unhandled rejection crashes when a race-loser promise is later rejected by resource cleanup.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T22:56:20.288Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJKCF1SNKNBV25JG0VPW9HZ6\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Agent investigation breadth vs accuracy tradeoff — Explore agents are valuable for surveying many files quickly but their conclusions need manual verification before acting. In this session, the agent reported event listener accumulation as CRITICAL (wrong — listeners registered once per spawn) while the actual bottleneck (getEventCount O(n^2)) wasn't in its top findings. Pattern: use agents for breadth, verify claims against actual code, then form your own root cause hypothesis.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T00:23:40.085Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":222438421},"formatted_output":"Total output lines: 7074\n\n[\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF89NXNJVRJQ6RTHJ310SHXC\",\n    \"type\": \"idea\",\n    \"content\": \"Need better error messages\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": \"@session-start\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T10:16:15.283Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:06.781Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": \"@01KF89NY\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93NC0FXND1244CN31ZH22Z\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"ReferenceIndex Result<T> pattern gotcha: resolve() returns Result objects with .ok field, not items directly. Must check result.ok before accessing result.item - TypeScript doesn't enforce this at compile time. Pattern: if (result.ok) { use result.item } else { handle error }. Encountered multiple times across iterations.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:20.175Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:07.260Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93NCXZNXTPWAPCFPNH0STG\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Linter/tooling auto-revert blocker: During ralph loop iterations, file changes were repeatedly auto-reverted by linter/auto-save system. Code written and verified would disappear after edits. Affected shadow.ts, index.ts, test files. Possible causes: aggressive format-on-save, linter deleting code it doesn't understand, file watcher conflicts. Blocks implementation work when it occurs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:21.120Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:07.778Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93NDYAX7CWP4QP7072AHMH\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Ralph loop session state freshness: Multiple issues with stale state in automation loops. (1) Iteration started on non-main branch from previous session. (2) Session context showed already-completed task as ready because context generated before commits reflected. (3) Picked completed work repeatedly. Solutions: generate context AFTER pulling latest, validate task is actually pending before starting, checkpoint script should update .kspec before next iteration.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:22.155Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:08.181Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93P6NTQJP3C2ZSND2J2MZT\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Subprocess spawning complexity: When promoting observations to tasks, initially tried spawning npm/tsx subprocess which caused temp directory path issues in tests. Switched to direct API calls (createTask/saveTask) which simplified implementation and avoided process overhead. Pattern: prefer direct API over subprocess when both run in same codebase.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:47.483Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:08.526Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93P7W2A063T315RXPC6ZF7\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Commander --json flag conflict: Command-specific --json flags conflict with global --json flag in Commander. Solution: use global flag only, check isJsonMode() instead of options.json. This pattern should be documented or enforced via convention.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:48.706Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:08.975Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93P8XZK7K9V8ERYYH6FE0Z\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Bash tool cd persistence: Commands run in same directory as previous command unless explicit cd. Running 'cd .kspec && git status' left session in .kspec worktree. Need explicit 'cd /path/to/main' to return. Can be confusing when working with shadow branch.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:49.792Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:09.402Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93PA837GGVE8DH3PVZE8WC\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"CLI output pattern: When implementing CLI commands with both human-readable and JSON formats, use success(message, data) instead of calling both success() and output() separately. The success() function already handles JSON mode internally, avoiding duplicate/mixed output.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:51.140Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:09.731Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93PBBYDPRH0WQSKN4Y18SV\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task status accuracy gap: Found task marked as priority 3 ready but implementation was already complete. All code, tests, and functionality existed. System correctly updated spec alignment when task completed, but task remained in ready list longer than it should have. Need earlier alignment checks or better detection of 'code exists but task not marked done' scenarios.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:52.286Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:10.062Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93PCN5NVFEHR801G77EK3X\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Shadow branch auto-commit PR challenges: PR included WIP commits from shadow that were auto-committed. Consider: (1) squash strategy for shadow commits when creating PR, (2) explicit checkpoint command before PR creation, or (3) shadow commit message convention (wip: prefix) to make cleanup easier.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:53.606Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:10.411Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93PDXFBPM2B1WYE6HFYJCX\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review automation friction: Had to manually launch review subagent, wait for output, interpret results, then fix issues. Could streamline with dedicated /review skill that: (1) checks for open PRs, (2) launches review subagent automatically, (3) interprets results + decision tree, (4) applies fixes if trivial, (5) merges if appropriate.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:50:54.895Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:10.930Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93Q1Y31HP8245N4DF67MCA\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Auto-sync vs interactive prompts anti-pattern: When adding interactive prompts to modify state, always check if automatic sync/calculation logic already exists. AlignmentIndex calculates spec status from all linked tasks - interactive prompt would allow single-task override, creating drift. Pattern: if system has 'calculated truth', don't add manual override without considering multi-entity consistency.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:51:15.396Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:11.342Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93Q2W8DC2RNGG1NA4ABQE0\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Test fixtures spec_ref conflicts: Test fixtures should avoid spec_ref assignments that conflict with derive tests. When adding spec_ref to test tasks, check if they're used in derive --dry-run tests which expect tasks not to exist yet.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:51:16.360Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:11.921Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93Q4JZ571ZGRTHZ3QXCYJQ\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Parser vs CLI layer disconnect: Meta includes were fully implemented in parser but CLI used wrong accessor (metaCtx.manifest.* vs metaCtx.*). This kind of bug suggests value in integration tests that exercise full stack, not just parser logic. Consider smoke tests for all CLI commands with complex scenarios.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:51:18.112Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:12.429Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93Q6BCQXGTJ7X4FAK13KVT\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Spec gap discovery during implementation: AC mentioned 'origin: observation_promotion' but origin field didn't exist in schema. Good example of spec-code drift. Consider: pre-implementation spec validation against schema, or schema-first approach where AC references must match existing schema fields.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:51:19.917Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:13.031Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93Q83M6RJ0YXH1H2H4F3TK\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"kspec-meta shadow branch divergence: Shadow branch has diverged significantly from remote (99 local vs 2 remote commits). Merge conflicts in sessions/ and modules/. May need manual reconciliation or a fresh sync strategy. Task changes are committed locally and functional.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:51:21.717Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:13.557Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF93Q9S85XSBT1JVV1S1F9F3\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Type guards for union types: When narrowing AnyLoadedItem | LoadedMetaItem to LoadedTask, check for required properties that exist on Task but not on meta items. Use 'status' in item && 'depends_on' in item - NOT optional properties like closed_reason which won't exist on incomplete tasks.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T17:51:23.432Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:14.020Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94EZQT8WP107P6QV9ZC4JD\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"PR review workflow pattern: Review subagents proved critical for catching issues before merge. Established pattern: (1) check for open PRs, (2) launch review subagent, (3) fix trivial issues directly, (4) re-review confirms fixes, (5) merge when checks pass. Works smoothly when changes are minor - automated review + fix + merge flow is efficient. Multi-step workflow (review→fix→merge→continue) provides good session continuity. Review caught real issues: reference matching bugs, TypeScript errors, duplicate PRs, missing tests. Self-review via subagent is valid for automation loops despite GitHub not allowing self-approval.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:04:19.579Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:14.432Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94F0W0BPTB5RP6FDWH63SM\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Incremental refactoring pattern: Large multi-iteration refactors work well when pattern is established early. Key lessons: (1) Create module first with comprehensive coverage, (2) Start with smallest files to establish pattern, (3) Commit incremental progress with clear 'what done/remains' tracking, (4) Use TodoWrite for sub-phases. String/error centralization phases showed this: early PRs for small wins, direct commits for established patterns. Tests catch issues early, smaller files build confidence. Having checkpoints and running totals (e.g., '179 of 201 = 89%') made continuation easy. This phased approach balances review overhead with execution speed.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:04:20.737Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:14.851Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94F20W3MKFPBA1XN0ABQ7P\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Implementation pattern (schema→parser→CLI→tests): New features follow clean path. Reuse agent command structure (formatTable, formatVerbose, JSON output via output()). Reference validation integration is clean - add to REF_FIELDS. Meta reference implementation was straightforward thanks to existing ReferenceIndex infrastructure. Pattern of implementing formatters first, then command registration works well. Testing is fast and reliable. Module add followed same pattern: validate inputs, create data, write file, update manifest, shadow commit. Could extract into reusable helper.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:04:21.916Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:15.326Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94FHX7C98EFRCSGAXAKBBR\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Reference implementation value: Checking prior work (../kspec-acp-test, ../kspec-ralph-test) before implementing saves significant design time. Found identical spec and working implementation providing clear blueprint. Prior work avoids edge cases and provides consistency. Explore subagents are valuable for understanding prior implementations - provided comprehensive details: file paths, schema patterns, CLI structure, test isolation challenges. Having parallel agent repos with prior work is highly valuable. Pattern: exploration as standard first step for implementation tasks.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:04:38.184Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:15.816Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94FK4G7W86NXDVTAZ77SK8\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task verification workflow: Some ready tasks are already implemented from prior sessions. Pattern: when starting task, verify current state by reading code, running tests, checking existing functionality before implementing. Saves time and avoids duplicate work. Meta commands (resolve, observe, promote, conventions) were already implemented but tasks remained pending. Need better sync between implementation status and task status - perhaps command to scan for already-implemented specs and auto-complete tasks. Consider 'verify implementation status' step especially for CLI commands.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:04:39.441Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:16.168Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94FMF9Y5VCS7EQXP4G2FRJ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Session/workflow patterns: Spike tasks with no code output don't need commits - value is in task notes documenting research. Shadow-only changes (task state updates) don't need main-branch PRs since shadow branch is source of truth. PR skill correctly detects no changes and exits cleanly for metadata-only tasks. PR workflow smooth with auto-generated branch names and /pr skill. Shadow CLI verification iteration showed pattern: pick task, verify implementation exists, complete task, no code changes needed.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:04:40.810Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:16.582Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94G1HYX2DCY796SKB9XB7P\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Task guardrails and completion checks: Feature dogfooded successfully - tested on itself during completion. Interactive prompt provides immediate feedback about AC coverage ensuring implementations match specs. Implementation preserves spec status.maturity when updating implementation status (important pattern to avoid losing maturity context). Default to 'draft' if status doesn't exist yet.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T18:04:54.208Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution\": \"Reviewed in retrospective - actionable items extracted to tasks, patterns retained as reference\",\n    \"resolved_at\": \"2026-01-19T16:12:17.054Z\",\n    \"resolved_by\": \"@claude\",\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KF94G2RY8JAX71K9BC8HJSF7\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Context and session integration: Meta focus command implementation straightforward thanks to well-structured SessionContext schema and existing loadSessionContext/saveSessionContext functions. Pattern of supporting show/set/clear modes in single command is clean and user-friendly. Auto-prepending @ to references maintains UX consistency. Context integration showed context BEFORE active work for immediate agent orie…80245 tokens truncated… catch this earlier. Observed during task-delete-static-analysis-tests (PR #558): deleted web-ui-triage.test.ts removed all @interactive-triage-ui ac-1..ac-8 coverage; Codex caught it, required creating triage.spec.ts to recover.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T14:46:12.882Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJD933WJ6W0FBY150BET1PZN\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"PR merged by review subagent while worker agent still editing files on same branch — local branch switches to main automatically, all pending Edit tool changes silently lost. Caused significant rework this session (re-applying all triage.spec.ts changes on new branch fix/triage-ac6-session-close-error). The review subagent and worker agent operate concurrently on the same branch in a fix cycle, creating a race condition. Potential mitigations: (1) worker agent checks for branch changes before editing, (2) ralph serializes review subagent after worker fully stops, (3) worker agent uses a local patch/stash before any branch changes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T15:29:16.691Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDFFJGEQ0R6JST5PR2JZVN4\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Dual review pattern (internal plan review + /codex review-plan) catches complementary issues — format vs substance. Worth standardizing for all plan imports.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T17:20:56.334Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDFFJK5FZ5DBANYTJEVH6Q9\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Shadow branch merge driver handles complex YAML conflicts (project.tasks.yaml with 38 divergent commits) automatically during rebase — reliable for ralph parallel sessions.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T17:20:56.421Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDN04RM1EHW2FKD5SRD3Y95\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Dual review pattern (plan agent + Codex) catches complementary issues. Plan agent validates design, Codex validates contracts and test coverage. Worth keeping as standard practice for non-trivial PRs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T18:57:22.197Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ0ZTHNQF93KHS4516B8C6\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"[spec-gap] Merge driver: auto-resolve .kspec-agents-hash file conflicts (deterministic hash, should always take latest)\\n\\nReasoning: Merge driver for hash file — low frequency conflict, manual resolution works\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:47.057Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ0ZZPZZY4TE3CX11Q65BP\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"[spec-gap] Plan import: generate richer task descriptions from Implementation Notes section — include file paths, what to change, verification steps instead of generic 'See plan...' text\\n\\nReasoning: Plan import richer descriptions — improvement, not blocking\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:47.222Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ114YVRSMJQSKZ2P4CQW0\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"[spec-gap] Triage ac-5 says sets result_ref but delete action may not produce one. Verify behavior and update spec or add test assertion.\\n\\nReasoning: Triage ac-5 result_ref for delete — spec may be wrong, needs verification\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:48.414Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ119THNSN93R18BVCPZSN\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"[spec-gap] Triage API spec says ac-4 and ac-5 use PUT method but implementation uses POST /:ref/override and POST /:ref/act. Spec needs updating to match reality.\\n\\nReasoning: Triage API spec PUT vs POST mismatch — spec needs updating to match implementation\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:48.570Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1281SE4DYG57NR127DKN\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"[spec-gap] @cmd-validate spec is stale — missing flags: --completeness, --staleness, --drift, --alignment, --skills, --conventions (all already implemented in code). Pre-existing drift, not introduced by trait AC task.\\n\\nReasoning: @cmd-validate spec is stale — missing 6 flags already in code. Spec drift.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:49.537Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ14VW0MD9YQ077ZM45MVQ\",\n    \"type\": \"question\",\n    \"content\": \"[spec-gap] kspec meta set convention: add --update-rule and --remove-rule flags. Currently the only way to fix a rule is to delete the entire convention and recreate it. Surfaced during skill CLI lookups task when codex review caught a wording issue in one rule.\\n\\nReasoning: Convention --update-rule — DX improvement, workaround is delete+recreate\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:52.221Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDR3S3ZJRMAB0M35SQEGXRM\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Triage record-then-act pattern with UI review works well at scale: batch-record 41 decisions, user reviews/overrides in web UI, batch-act on confirmed. Clean separation of agent proposals from user decisions. 12 overrides out of 41 shows useful agent-human collaboration.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:51:47.071Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDV6RXJE25G2B3QRF02MYW3\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex two-pass review pattern effective: implement → codex review → fix bug found → re-review clean. Caught missing previousValue in injectCodexEnv that would have broken Ralph cleanup.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T20:45:50.899Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDXCB7E87A4EYJKK009VQ2K\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Well-decomposed task descriptions with exact files and verification criteria make implementation fast — the per-adapter-auto-approve task took one focused session from start to merged PR.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T21:23:50.639Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDXCBBHHBBKXDKV5Z74BX7B\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"MOCK_ACP_VERIFY_ARGS_FILE pattern extends the existing env var verification pattern cleanly — behavioral test infrastructure for ACP agent spawning is now solid.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T21:23:50.769Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDZV06SJXM9RG4YPXRXHBHQ\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex PR review as iterative second reviewer catches real bugs. Two-round pattern (review → fix → re-review) provides high-confidence quality gate for ralph adapter/env code.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T22:06:48.025Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDZV0AJP3K3RNTZ3A9ZXQFC\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Plan-derived task descriptions with exact line numbers and numbered change steps make implementation fast and focused. The plan-to-task pipeline produces high-quality work items.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T22:06:48.146Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJEVM2Y2ZXMSY10GNP2CMBCV\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"When posting content containing $ and angle-bracket placeholders via shell-wrapped commands, interpolation can silently mutate task/PR notes; prefer literal-safe quoting or file-based payloads.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T06:12:21.570Z\",\n    \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJEVMQJJZ127WW5CHM0KQK16\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Portable {skill:<id>} tokens with renderer-side platform resolution reduced template duplication and kept Claude/Codex invocation guidance consistent across SKILL.md and supporting markdown.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T06:12:42.706Z\",\n    \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGAE26H74N8C0ZTZ6HH5V2N\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Parallel plan review (Plan agent + Codex) catches complementary issues: architectural concerns vs format/structural issues. High convergence on edge cases gives confidence. Worth standardizing as a dual-review step.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T19:50:27.281Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGAE2A5KKANQDY4KRZWFM9W\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Plan-derived tasks need manual follow-up (batch set tags + note) to be automation-ready. The derive step should produce standalone tasks.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T19:50:27.397Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGAKM10AY9KFR9JXBWFFCGX\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Core skill update UX gap: kspec skill update is version-gated, so same-version template edits are skipped and require kspec skill install-core. This is non-obvious during local template iteration. Improve guidance (update vs install-core) or adjust command behavior to detect local template changes.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": \"@session-reflect\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T19:53:29.377Z\",\n    \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": \"@01KJGQVK\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGFKJ79GAK3QF33QHRMYWJW\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Holistic plan review (plan + derived specs + tasks + traits together) before any code is written caught 6 spec gaps in @plan-auto-close-stale-active-sessions including missing targeting semantics, liveness guard, corrupt events handling, and task dependency ordering. Pattern: evaluate the full derivation tree, not just individual specs.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T21:20:50.410Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGQCA1DEK15Y59X5M8N5HR5\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex PR review threads require manual GraphQL resolution + CI re-trigger before merge. Multi-step dance every time codex posts inline comments.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T23:36:41.261Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGQCA7649GZMT2HA0Z5CXQA\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Iterative codex review loop (review → fix → re-review) converges well. Three rounds on PR #582 caught duplicate label, spec alignment drift, and missing test branch.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T23:36:41.446Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGQKPWM32W85246H3VAWDD0\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Targeted dry-run + focused test loop quickly exposed core-skill source-of-truth drift; package-distribution test caught stale plugin artifact path immediately.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": \"@session-reflect\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T23:40:43.797Z\",\n    \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGW8ZB984E1QZHMGGCHSRXR\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"CLI tests that execute dist artifacts can produce misleading failures when dist is stale; this creates avoidable debugging churn before the real code behavior is evaluated.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T01:02:14.889Z\",\n    \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGW8ZFQ697G7Z8T81MTXN35\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Using a focused validate mode matrix (schema/refs/alignment/completeness/staleness + combinations) quickly verified scoped semantics and prevented regressions while keeping turnaround fast.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T01:02:15.031Z\",\n    \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJJHARH9G3CT7R978K6AEBZ4\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Isolated worktree + backup branch pattern for shadow branch recovery. Creating a backup branch before destructive ops, then using /tmp worktree for experimental rebase, then patching the result back as a normal commit avoided force-push entirely. This pattern should be documented for future shadow branch divergence scenarios.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T16:29:27.977Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJJHARMST4YEMPE7PYSVXSCA\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Merge driver silent data loss when --non-interactive flag missing from git config. No error, no warning — just hangs on stdin and leaves files unmerged. 12 task completions lost silently. Root cause: shadow.ts registration code path diverged from actual git config. Fix tracked in @01KJJGJ1.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T16:29:28.089Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJJT519QTQXSJWRM17W06HH6\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex PR review takes 10+ minutes because npm test subagent polling is inefficient. Consider instructing Codex to skip full suite and rely on CI, or use test shards instead of full npm test.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T19:03:37.528Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJJT51HXZZBH71BXK6VXKM15\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex PR review cannot distinguish pre-existing test failures from regressions. Flags false positives (e.g. session-budget-integration flakiness on PR #590). Could pre-seed known-flaky test list or compare failure counts against main baseline.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T19:03:37.790Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJJT51PHNAYJRJFMW7HQHMXH\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Codex-then-fix cycle on PR #601 was tight: review posted, ac-9 gap caught, fixed in 1 commit, thread resolved, CI passed, merged. Total turnaround ~15 min including CI.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T19:03:37.937Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJK7F4JXEBF205YJ30MK5XS0\",\n    \"type\": \"friction\",\n    \"content\": \"Task budget guard blocks needs_work fix cycle transitions. kspec task start @ref fails with budget exhausted even when the task is in needs_work state (an existing fix cycle, not a new task start). needs_work → in_progress should be exempt from the budget guard since it is resuming prior work, not starting new work. Had to skip task state transitions and create PR without proper submit flow.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T22:56:20.063Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJK7F4T0JVSCB40JEAN9PHGP\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Minimal floating-promise fix pattern: storing async function result in a variable and attaching .catch(() => {}) before Promise.race is the clean way to prevent Node.js 22 unhandled rejection crashes when a race-loser promise is later rejected by resource cleanup.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T22:56:20.288Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJKCF1SNKNBV25JG0VPW9HZ6\",\n    \"type\": \"success\",\n    \"content\": \"Agent investigation breadth vs accuracy tradeoff — Explore agents are valuable for surveying many files quickly but their conclusions need manual verification before acting. In this session, the agent reported event listener accumulation as CRITICAL (wrong — listeners registered once per spawn) while the actual bottleneck (getEventCount O(n^2)) wasn't in its top findings. Pattern: use agents for breadth, verify claims against actual code, then form your own root cause hypothesis.\",\n    \"workflow_ref\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T00:23:40.085Z\",\n    \"author\": \"@claude\",\n    \"resolved\": false,\n    \"resolution\": null,\n    \"resolved_at\": null,\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_to\": null\n  }\n]\n","status":"completed"}